{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book","id":227352,"title":"What would you want to see in a Sin-eater Chronicle book?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-13T14:47:38-07:00","id":227352,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> What would you want to see in a Sin-eater Chronicle book?","content":"I looked, and couldn't find a similar thread. I've seen Promethean and Hunter versions, so let's do Geist. This game could use some love.<br /> <br /> I love Geist for it's themes and setting. I love the Underworld from the Upper Reaches to the Lower Mysteries and beyond. I love Krewes as cult + Gang. I love the Keystones and the way that Sin-eaters are bound to Geists. <br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Sin-eaters don't really have much drive. I wouldn't want the game to be as tightly focused as Werewolf, where it feels almost impossible to go off and do your own thing, but some more focus would really be nice. As it stands, other than being irritated by Ghosts, there's no reason for a Sin-eater to actually get involved in any Sin-eating. There's also the fact that they don't really eat sin.<br /> <br /> I've asked a lot of people about what they dislike about Geist, too, and I keep getting the same answers: There's no focus, there's no reason to do anything. Geists don't actually have a real, mechanical effect on Sin-eaters, and ghosts are annoying, but not a real problem.<br /> <br /> I <i>hate</i> the way that Krewes work, and how they're external to the characters as opposed to internal, the way that packs and cabals are. I hate that they change your Geist, and often the Geist becomes Santa Claus or something and tells you it always was, you just weren't ready to know. <br /> <br /> The mechanics are also scattershot, with Ceremonies for starting characters averaging out to 4 dots and Manifestations being clunky to use and getting a <i>ton</i> of dice modifiers, +3 to your starting Keys at the very least. <br /> <br /> I love <i>Geist</i>, but I feel like it needs a rewrite even more than Werewolf or Mage. But I also worry that because no one really likes it that it won't get one. Even if it does, we're looking at something years down the line.<br /> <br /> What do you think needs to be fixed? What would you want to see in a Geist Chronicle book?<br /> <br /> Also, <i>Rum and Bones: The Kerberoi Chronicle</i> has a nice ring to it, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T15:11:56-07:00","id":227371,"title":"","content":"Firstly I wouldn't want it to be the Kerbeori Chronicles. Kerberoi are too limited to the Underworld for them to be the default core of most Geist stories. I'm torn between the Geist Chronicle and the Krewe Chronicle.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for my answer. I could probably say a lot but it's late so I'll start with the basics: I love Geist's themes as presented, I want the mechanics to support them. Sin-Eaters are suppost to be partying off-kilter mediums. The mechanics are uber-focused on fighting and cursing others. I want that fixed. PenDragon has a great mechanic for Manifestations (I call them Unleashings just to avoid overlap with Ghosts)<br /> <br /> I want Krewes to be something you build. Ethos, Metaphysics, Mythology, Aspects. Each is an independent merit that you can buy when you're ready, each is flexible in how and why you get it. Each ties into a core aspect of the game (Metaphysics change the rules for Ceremonies for example. You're a Voodoo Krewe, now your Ceremonies work like actual Voodoo)<br /> <br /> I want Geists to actually be a threat to your charachter. And I want various options for relationships; parters who like each other. A grudging give and take. A Sin-Eater who's arch-enemies with their Geist. All should be supported.<br /> <br /> I want Thresholds that actually are a proper splat, not just a list of ways you might die and Geists you might get. Splat like personality traits come because Geists of Threshold X have similar traits that Sin-Eaters must adapt too.<br /> <br /> I want Ghosts that can actually threaten Sin-Eaters (I'm thinking special ghosts built like Slasher's Undertakings).<br /> <br /> <br /> Most of this stuff has been written in the link I sent you; though the Ceremonies stuff can be found by following the index in my signature.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T16:25:47-07:00","id":227394,"title":"","content":"&quot;Unlocks&quot; might be a good term for them, in keeping with the Key and Threshold door symbolism. Actually, I might rename them that in my thing (I still need to get around to reading yours, since I'm lazy).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T20:00:48-07:00","id":227548,"title":"","content":"I want it to be The Krewe Chronicle, with a focus on building your krewe and digging up the bones of those who have gone before. I want geists to mean as much as the Shadow did in Wraith. I want Archetypes to mean something and be valid grouping, not vague example philosophies. I want more things for sin-eaters to do other than be punk Ghostbusters; as it stands, the game is just a worse Werewolf with a few good ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-13T22:24:04-07:00","id":227606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=227548#post227548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as it stands, the game is just a worse Werewolf with a few good ideas.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much as I hate to admit it, this is true.<br /> <br /> What would you want to see out of Archeytpes and how would you want the Geist to be more like the Shadow?<br /> I'm actually thinking of doing away with Archetypes in my rewrite, and replacing them with &quot;Carnivals&quot;, which would be Sin-eater's version of Orders/Guilds/Covenants/Tribes. I really feel like the &quot;no major groups&quot; experiment didn't really work well.<br /> <br /> <sub>As an aside, I'm not fond of &quot;Krewe Chronicles&quot;; according to DaveB, the &quot;chronicle&quot; part is the &quot;outside context&quot; problem for the character types. Krewes are within the context of the Sin-eaters. Really, Abmortals or Kerberoi would be apt for Sin-eaters, or at best Geists, as they're similar to the Fallen World in that they're the driving force of the gameline. But &quot;Geist Chronicle&quot; doesn't really have a nice ring to it, and rephrases the title.</sub>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T00:13:02-07:00","id":227645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=227606#post227606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><sub>As an aside, I'm not fond of &quot;Krewe Chronicles&quot;; according to DaveB, the &quot;chronicle&quot; part is the &quot;outside context&quot; problem for the character types. Krewes are within the context of the Sin-eaters. Really, Abmortals or Kerberoi would be apt for Sin-eaters, or at best Geists, as they're similar to the Fallen World in that they're the driving force of the gameline. But &quot;Geist Chronicle&quot; doesn't really have a nice ring to it, and rephrases the title.</sub></div> </div> </div> </div>This seems to be a mistaken association with one part of the statement Dave made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong> DaveB, Falling Down Article</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As most of you have noticed, the Chronicle Books are all named after the story catalyst in their respective games. Not necessarily the antagonist, but the thing that upsets the apple cart, disrupts the lives of the characters and causes a Story. The Strix throw the All Night Society off kilter and into chaos, the Idigam are an Outside Context problem the tribes aren\u2019t properly equipped to fight. The God-Machine sends angels to do its inscrutable bidding, no matter who tries to get in its way</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Outside Context describes the Idigam, but the idea to focus on is that they disrupt the lives of the characters and cause Story. So the Strix and the Idigam are examples of actual antagonists, but the Fallen World is about the Mysteries they face.<br /> <br /> If one were to make a Chronicle Book for Geist, what the antagonist would <i>be </i>is an excellent question. However, if we're interested in Geist standing on its own two feet rather than being worse Werewolf with a few good ideas about Ghosts, then I'd hope they'd go for something more creative than a simple out of context problem.<br /> <br /> I think, one of the big things I've noticed is that the Geister want to experience living life, but as a side effect, attract ghosts who want them to solve their problems and help them move on. Those two elements don't really feel like they meet, so I'd like to see something connecting those two things. Moreover, the big impetus for story that's uniquely Geist focused seems to have to do with these Ghosts, so if I were to purpose a catalyst for Story, it would be coming to terms with their purpose and how it conflicts with their desire to live or whatever. Something like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T09:13:10-07:00","id":228039,"title":"","content":"I still need to explain the logic behind the idea for the Horseman Chronicles, don't I?<br /> <br /> We'll see if that or the hunter discusssion strikes me harder after shopping, assuming Gen Con updates don't devour the whole of today.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T10:03:31-07:00","id":228129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=227606#post227606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I really feel like the &quot;no major groups&quot; experiment didn't really work well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read Demon: The Descent?<br /> <br /> The Agenda splat for Demon is very loose socially but have meatier mechanics to reinforce their importance. I could see something similar working very well for the Archetypes in Geist. The conditions that each Agenda provide could be used similarly to great affect in Geist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T10:54:41-07:00","id":228212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=227606#post227606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually thinking of doing away with Archetypes in my rewrite, and replacing them with &quot;Carnivals&quot;, which would be Sin-eater's version of Orders/Guilds/Covenants/Tribes. I really feel like the &quot;no major groups&quot; experiment didn't really work well.</div> </div> </div> </div> I like Archetypes a lot.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T12:52:58-07:00","id":228387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=228129#post228129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Agenda splat for Demon is very loose socially but have meatier mechanics to reinforce their importance. I could see something similar working very well for the Archetypes in Geist. The conditions that each Agenda provide could be used similarly to great affect in Geist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of me is actually thinking of making Archetypes closer to Agendas, with each one having a Beat and Resolution condition, which can grant both &quot;Ectoplasmic Beats&quot; and chances at regaining Plasm. But at the same time I feel there are too many Archetypes, and some of them are too similar, while some of them feel like things that ALL Sin-eaters would do. There's a lot of talk about Sin-eaters who abuse their powers for material gain, yet only the Bonepickers get archetype bonuses--such as they are--for it? It isn't even really a ghostly trope. Likewise, just about every Sin-eater is an Advocate in some way, and helping ghosts pass on is a good way to regain Plasm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=228212#post228212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I like Archetypes a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I noticed. I didn't really like that. Although on the other side, I did find the idea of a &quot;Restful&quot; Threshold interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=228039#post228039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still need to explain the logic behind the idea for the Horseman Chronicles, don't I?<br /> <br /> We'll see if that or the hunter discusssion strikes me harder after shopping, assuming Gen Con updates don't devour the whole of today.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with that is that it would mean the Horsemen are real, or at least pertinent. That said if they were some distant but judging/shaming figures, like Luna is, then there'd be a little more impetus for Sin-eaters to police the border of life and death.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T13:53:16-07:00","id":228448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=228387#post228387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with that is that it would mean the Horsemen are real, or at least pertinent. That said if they were some distant but judging/shaming figures, like Luna is, then there'd be a little more impetus for Sin-eaters to police the border of life and death.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I mentioned an explanation of the logic-they're more convienent short hand for how I understand Geist's greatest story catalyst, the factor that flips the tables the most on Sin-Eaters<br /> <br /> Although, I must, within the spirit of the source, advise against suggesting that the Horsemen aren't real-you never know when they might take offense to that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T17:55:05-07:00","id":228589,"title":"","content":"Care to elaborate on that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T18:03:23-07:00","id":228604,"title":"","content":"One day, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-14T23:50:57-07:00","id":228846,"title":"","content":"I would like to know more about the history of sin eaters and what were the like during times of great death. I would also like a manifestation system were you can mix powers similar to how blood and smoke did. Finally I would like to know how exactly can a giest help you out besides giving advice and insight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T03:10:17-07:00","id":228948,"title":"","content":"Mix powers? Where did Blood and Smoke do that? Do you mean the Devotions? Those actually existed before.<br /> <br /> <sub>Also, not to plug my own work, but I actually started looking into the Aztec mythology and talking about how Sin-eaters were a part of that; Quetzelcoatl was a geist, and eventually became Bound to Cortez or a member of his Conquistadores, ransacking the New World. That's why Quetzelcoatl got co-opted into sainthood while the other Aztec Gods were vilified</sub>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T10:02:52-07:00","id":229181,"title":"","content":"Personally, I like the way krewes work now, at least story-wise. I wouldn't mind the mechanics being more robust in the way TKR describes, but I am 1000% comfortable with the way Krewe Channels are described (though I think it could be better written to get the concept across, since it seems to be consistently misunderstood)<br /> <br /> What I'd want is for synergy and the geist to more closely match how they're described. I think in the recent chronicle rewrites the devs have been playing around more with different and more creative and thematic ways of handling the integrity stat, and I'd like to see that continue. <br /> <br /> And yeah, I'd second giving the sin-eaters more drive. Setting up ghosts as the antagonists of your game and then giving all your characters a near-infinite ability to make ghosts pathetic means there's a lot of shuffling around wondering what to do next.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T12:32:36-07:00","id":229428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=228846#post228846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to know more about the history of sin eaters and what were the like during times of great death. I would also like a manifestation system were you can mix powers similar to how blood and smoke did. Finally I would like to know how exactly can a giest help you out besides giving advice and insight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would prefer a manifestation system that was consistent to their thematics and wasn't one of the worst systems in the game. It's so fucking tedious to make new powers and out of place in general with geists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-15T16:23:36-07:00","id":229682,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't mind if the Archetypes worked more like Seemings. It could be something cosmetic like, when your Geist is pissed off and you spend Plasm you look like a Wight (or Ghast, or Wraith, or Spectre, etc.). Or it could be something more mechanical that adds additional abilities in certain situations (like Wraiths have a Wraith form that lets them deal with Ghosts, Ghasts can raise Zombies, Wights have a chill touch, etc.). I also wouldn't mind a bit of a grittier feel, these folks have died and brought something dead back with them. Ditto what Epimetheus says above about the manifestation system. Geist has one of the clumsiest systems out of the nWoD games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T13:09:50-07:00","id":234560,"title":"","content":"As I figure out a campaign for my players, I've contemplated the whole 'lack of antagonists' thing in the book and - my take on it - is thus:<br /> <br /> There is an overlooked antagonist that most STs miss entirely, or houserule out of existance for fear that they may take some of the control of the players characters out of the hands of the players. The Geists themselves. Sin Eaters - by their very nature - are literally sharing their heads with a super powerful batshit crazy super ghost hybrid. If you want to run a Geist game, their interaction and demands on their hosts should be a major motivation in game. Whether your ghost makes them want to avenge rape victims, or finally find proof that the illuminati is covering up archeological digs that prove Napoleon was in fact an alien, the Geists should be the biggest motivation for the players to act.<br /> <br /> I want a splat book on Geists themselves, showcasing the different ways they manipulate their hosts and cause mayham.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T18:02:38-07:00","id":234847,"title":"","content":"Re: Antagonists, Geist and Werewolf occupy similar niches, in terms of plot structure; they're those who gatekeep the boundary between an unnatural world and that of the living. <br /> <br /> <i>Werewolf</i> thus gives you Spirits, which can cover any concept in existence. They also struggle with the Pure, who are foils to the Forsaken and are equally potent in combat. There's the Idigam, as big spooky chronicle drivers. There's the Claimed, there's Hosts, there's a goddamn bevy of antagonists. <i>Geist</i> has ghosts, other SIn-Eaters, and not all that much else. You don't have much of a chance to punch a Kerberoi in the dick as a SIn-Eater, and Cthonians never got covered in detail. See the problem here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T20:05:31-07:00","id":234945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=234847#post234847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: Antagonists, Geist and Werewolf occupy similar niches, in terms of plot structure; they're those who gatekeep the boundary between an unnatural world and that of the living.<br /> <br /> <i>Werewolf</i> thus gives you Spirits, which can cover any concept in existence. They also struggle with the Pure, who are foils to the Forsaken and are equally potent in combat. There's the Idigam, as big spooky chronicle drivers. There's the Claimed, there's Hosts, there's a goddamn bevy of antagonists. <i>Geist</i> has ghosts, other SIn-Eaters, and not all that much else. You don't have much of a chance to punch a Kerberoi in the dick as a SIn-Eater, and Cthonians never got covered in detail. See the problem here?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel it's disingenuous to categorize the Claimed as a totally separate antagonist group, Iminir tribal prey though they may be; doubly so to ignore unfettered geister and the other weird bullshit that vomits itself up from the land of the dead, some of which seems to potentially be responsible for the creation of an abmortal or three. The Kerberoi also seem to have been partially set up to be the main drivers for non-desperate old ghosts to wind up in the lands of the living - special dispensation from them is called out as one of the ways a ghost can be permitted to go topside.<br /> <br /> The big problem is essentially that a lot of Geist's antagonists keep their (if you'll pardon the pun) vital points in the Underworld, where they will be the source of recurring complications unless the characters head downstairs and bind the thing or whack it until it stops moving. Their sitting on top of a lot of otherwise-irretrievable swag is another big factor, I suspect, along with possibly existing in the same neck of the woods as beings who presently look and act an awful lot like some of your loved ones.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm saying is that the line needs to stress emotional investment and the sheer breadth of potential that the deadlands and its periphery has to offer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T04:36:45-07:00","id":235307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=234945#post234945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">doubly so to ignore unfettered geister and the other weird bullshit that vomits itself up from the land of the dead, some of which seems to potentially be responsible for the creation of an abmortal or three. The Kerberoi also seem to have been partially set up to be the main drivers for non-desperate old ghosts to wind up in the lands of the living - special dispensation from them is called out as one of the ways a ghost can be permitted to go topside.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that Geist has no mechanical weight to this, it's just given as a sort of aside. I don't have a link to it, and I'm not even sure it was on the OPP forums, but when asked about how Vampire improved in<i> Blood &amp; Smoke</i>, someone put it best: Everything now has more mechanical resonance that aids in giving it thematic weight. Geist doesn't have any of that. In fact, Geist has <i>none</i> of that. <br /> <br /> I actually can't think of a single mechanic in Geist that has any significance thematically. There's nothing done with the &quot;key/door/threshold&quot; theme, there's nothing done with the fact that Sin-eaters are effectively immortal. There's nothing done with the insta-crazy moments like dying or sacrificing someone for a full-heal, other than they're instant Synergy drops. Hell, Synergy itself is pretty scattershot, and the book can't decide if it's a generic Underworld morality or if it's the bond between Geist and Sin-eater. For all the talk of &quot;you can't 'Sin' against Synergy&quot; you sure as hell can. And none of it has to do with following/not following your Geist's orders or goals.<br /> <br /> That's what Geist 2e really needs. It needs focus and weight. <br /> <br /> <br /> As an addendum, Geist has a ton of enemies. Abmortals, ghosts, Kerberoi, Sacrosanct, Vacant, Wretched. Cthonians. It just gives no reason to deal with them.<br /> Abmortals only matter to Sin-eaters that care.<br /> Ghosts only matter to Sin-eaters that care.<br /> Kerberoi are in the Underworld, and even there you've gotta go pretty deep.<br /> Sacrosanct only matter if you're involved in krewe culture or one actually finds you and tries to murder you for being demon possessed.<br /> The Vacant are an actual threat to Sin-eaters who don't hang out with others... except they're just mortals and can easily be instagibbed with Sin-eater powers.<br /> The Wretched don't hate other Sin-eaters or anything, and aren't even always bad; the example one is, but you could just as easily have a &quot;Wretched&quot; who's a nicer person when the Geist is in control.<br /> Cthonians have zero information about them other than &quot;they're spooky!&quot; and feel like they were meant to be written out of the book but someone forgot a paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T06:10:58-07:00","id":235344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=235307#post235307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that Geist has no mechanical weight to this, it's just given as a sort of aside. I don't have a link to it, and I'm not even sure it was on the OPP forums, but when asked about how Vampire improved in<i> Blood &amp; Smoke</i>, someone put it best: Everything now has more mechanical resonance that aids in giving it thematic weight. Geist doesn't have any of that. In fact, Geist has <i>none</i> of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the only part of this I agree with. Geist could definitely benefit from a workover a la blood and smoke. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=235307#post235307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually can't think of a single mechanic in Geist that has any significance thematically. There's nothing done with the &quot;key/door/threshold&quot; theme, there's nothing done with the fact that Sin-eaters are effectively immortal. There's nothing done with the insta-crazy moments like dying or sacrificing someone for a full-heal, other than they're instant Synergy drops. Hell, Synergy itself is pretty scattershot, and the book can't decide if it's a generic Underworld morality or if it's the bond between Geist and Sin-eater. For all the talk of &quot;you can't 'Sin' against Synergy&quot; you sure as hell can. And none of it has to do with following/not following your Geist's orders or goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was not my interpretation at all. I think my post above was ignored, so let me reiterate: The Geist that Sin Eaters are bound to are probably one of the biggest antagonists and or driving factors a Sin Eater should deal with. Immortal? Yeah, so long as they maintain their bond.<br /> <br /> As for Synergy: my take on it that it is the bond between Geist and Sin-eater. The only reason it gets tied up in underworld morality is because the Geist is tied up in underworld morality. Destroying ghosts is as unthinkable to a ghost as decapitating your neighbor is to you, so you're surprised that doing this wouldn't break down your connection to the ghost in your head?<br /> <br /> TL;DR - I'm not sure why people think there is no driving force forcing them to do anything. Want motivation? You're ghost needs you to accomplish a specific goal. Need story? Figure out WHY your Geist wants you to accomplish that specific goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T06:48:10-07:00","id":235354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=235344#post235344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This was not my interpretation at all. I think my post above was ignored, so let me reiterate: The Geist that Sin Eaters are bound to are probably one of the biggest antagonists and or driving factors a Sin Eater should deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I saw it. And I agree with it, too. The main issue is that there's no mechanical weight to it. The Beast is a bigger challenge for Vampires, and it's barely a separate entity. Synergy is <i>said</i> to be about the connection to the Geist, but it isn't <i>shown</i> to be that. I showed a friend my revamped Synergy and he complained about it because he didn't like that ectophagia was a Synergy breaking point. His Geist in his current game on Wanton Wicked is dedicated to Ectophagia, so going by the &quot;Synergy as connection to the Geist&quot; school of thought, his Geist would be pro-ghost-eating, and it would <i>raise</i> his Synergy if anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">TL;DR - I'm not sure why people think there is no driving force forcing them to do anything. Want motivation? You're ghost needs you to accomplish a specific goal. Need story? Figure out WHY your Geist wants you to accomplish that specific goal.</span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">The problem is that there's no driving force to that. While there's <i>Dem Bones</i> and La Diabla Blanca as examples, and maybe Michael ben Michael, you don't actually have to listen to the voice in the back of your head. And even then, the voice in the back of your head could just as easily want to drink and party, same as you. An adrenaline junkie raver who pops pills and climbs mountains could very easily just be a Bonepicker who abuses her powers and has a Geist who says nothing other than &quot;Whooooo!&quot;<br /> <br /> You don't actually <i>need</i> to do anything.<br /> <br /> Sure, you don't <i>need</i> to do anything as most other supernaturals--a vampire can get a small herd and be content, a mage doesn't need to delve into the mysteries, a changeling can pretend to be a rape victim and get professional counseling, a Demon can move to the boonies and live a mundane life--but you're strongly <i>encouraged</i> to go out and do things because of the society--vampires have to deal with the Danse even if they don't want to get involved, Mages are likely to get picked up by the Orders and deal with greater politics, a Changeling's life is going to crumble when confronted by other fae if they try to hide, a Demon's Agenda will always pull him back even if he goes away from the God-Machine. Geist doesn't have that. The only thing it has are krewes, and not only is there no actual reason to join a ritually bound Krewe (most of the benefits are lackluster, or only good for bigger krewes), there's no Orders or Courts to make infighting matter. Krewes are gangs, except actual gangs get 'em young, or when they're in prison.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of mechanics not backing up the fluff.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T08:58:37-07:00","id":235443,"title":"","content":"I agree. The system lacks a &quot;Your Geist DEMANDS you do this!&quot;-sorta mechanic. I dont nessesarily agree that it needs additional antagonists, it just needs to do a better job at dragging the things allready existing in the World of Darkness which can function as antagonists, into the Geist mix. Personally, I look to Inferno for both of these. They have a machanic for &quot;Your Demon DEMANDS you do this!&quot;-mechanic, and the Posessed can function as nifty &quot;Inferno Sin-Eaters&quot; if you flavor them as such in your own chronicle.<br /> I dont even think the Contest of Wills system needs alot of tweaking to work. I've almost just face-lifted it straight for my own chronicle.<br /> You can also get alot of mileage out of Mages and Thaumaturges abusing ghosts, and the Geists (if not the Sin-Eater themselves) not being alright with that.<br /> <br /> As for the Krewe system, I dont know how that could easily be fixed without changing what it is. Perhaps tune down the Gang aspect? I never really understood why the The Bound would nessesarily adopt gang-culture, anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T09:17:56-07:00","id":235457,"title":"","content":"I've been writing up a system overhaul for Geist, and I looked into both how the Beast is handled in <i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i> and how the Possessed are handled to figure out how to work with the Geist conflicting with the Sin-eater. In the end, I went with giving the Geist a dice pool based on the Sin-eaters Psyche rating. I posted it somewhere, but I can't remember where, so I'll add it to the end of this post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can also get alot of mileage out of Mages and Thaumaturges abusing ghosts, and the Geists (if not the Sin-Eater themselves) not being alright with that. </div> </div> </div>One of the main problems is that there's not really any reason Sin-eaters would care about that. Going through Geist, a lot of the suggested plotlines only really work if the players are &quot;good&quot; people. If they're antagonistic, or even if they're just neutral, there are very few reasons for them to get involved.<br /> <br /> Geist <i>does</i> have antagonists. A lot of them. It just doesn't give much reason for you to care.<br /> An Abmortal could be a great antagonist, but they don't have anywhere near the same narrative punch as, say, the Strix. When a Strix shows up in a city, shit goes down. It's an &quot;and then it started raining&quot; to any bad situation.<br /> <br /> They throw Cities into chaos. But Geist? Doesn't have that. No reason for them to care about anything. It's always a bad sign when the setting has no drive beyond the goodness of people's hearts. And I think that might be one reason that some people criticize Geist as a game in which there are no consequences. <hr /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trinigan FG\">Interaction with the Geist</span></span><br /> The Bargain fuses Sin-eater and Geist together in unison, but they\u2019re still separate entities even if they possess the same space. Sometimes their goals and desires conflict, and they might struggle against each other. The Geist is for the most part a passenger, but even a back seat driver can make a grab for the wheel sometimes. A Sin-eater can allow their Geist to take control, if they choose, forgoing any contest. The Geist controls the physical body and the Sin-eater gains an additional Aspiration directed towards what the Geist wants to accomplish. Once they accomplish it, the Geist relinquishes control.<br /> Sometimes a Sin-eater doesn\u2019t<i>want</i> to give up their body, though. Either out of personal possession--it is<i>her</i> body, after all--and sometimes because the goal of the Geist conflicts with the Sin-eater\u2019s convictions or own goals. Geists can often be dangerous when left unchained. If a Sin-eater wants to struggle against the Geist, they perform a sort of Abjuration against themselves. The Sin-eater rolls Stamina + Composure to keep control, while the Storyteller rolls based on Psyche for the Geist.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 100%\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trinigan FG\"><b>Psyche Rating</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Trinigan FG\"><b>Dice to Struggle</b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>1 to 3</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>4</b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>4 to 5</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>5</b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>6 to 8</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>7</b></span></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>9 to 10</b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>9</b></span></td> </tr> </table></div> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">A Sin-eater can spend a point of Willpower to resist the Geist, only instead of providing +3 on the roll, it staves the Geist off for another turn. During this turn, the Sin-eater physically strains, growling, exerting control over their body. The roll for the turn is held off. When a Sin-eater finally stops spending Willpower (either out of choice or because they simply can\u2019t) then when the roll finally happens, the Sin-eater gains +1 for each point turn spent holding it off.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">If the Sin-eater wins, the Geist is pushed back and calms down (metaphorically, at least. It won\u2019t attempt to take over for the rest of the scene, but it might still grumble and groan) as the Sin-eater retains control over their own body. If the Geist wins, they take control, as described above.</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T09:46:45-07:00","id":237086,"title":"","content":"Thing is though, its only a perfect merger in the system. In the fluff, they constantly talk about how a Sin-Eater might be driven to do heinous acts, in the name of complying with the Geist, mostly to avoid having a shrill shreaking Banshee howling in your mind 24/7.<br /> I dont view Geist as being entire devoid of what you call Angst, I just see as a game that has a bright side to it aswell. You've died and come back with a Death-God as your new head-mate, that sucks! On the flip side, you've died and come back with a Death-God as your new head-mate, thats great! Its the contrast that does it for me. The bright aspects shines all the brighter, in contrast to the grim darkness of having an alien specter in your mind, that tirelessly urges you to commit actions of questionable morality, in the name of its own unknowable agenda.<br /> I can understand the notion though. Perhaps a straight up possession-thing would be too much to have, atleast at mid-to-high Synergy. I had an idea for my own Geist game, which basically allows the Geists to inflicts things like Guilt, Swooning and so forth, as Tilts if the Sin-Eater conssistently fails to awcknowledge the demands of the Geist. That way, it'll start as simple bad and feelings (which the book also says is a way for Geists to force Sin-Eaters to comply) and if the Sin-Eater continues to disobey its spectral passenger, it'll turn into outright possession as Synergy plummets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T12:32:34-07:00","id":237239,"title":"","content":"I agree with Rater's perspective. While I would like to see the relationship between geist and host done better and possibly with mechanical teeth to it, having a hostile geist or one that can take struggle against your actions would spoil a lot of the game for me. It doesn't necessarily have to be a benefit, but making it hostile can quickly make it feel like something the GM is manipulating just to screw the player's goals and frustrates the experience of geist which is, refreshingly, not a game about angst.<br /> There's already a splat for having a ride-along entity that can take over your body and makes you do terrible things: Inferno Possessed. Geist is not that game for a reason.<br /> <br /> I will say, though, that being able to inflict social conditions is an awesome idea that I hadn't thought of before (I haven't really jumped in to play a full GMC game yet). I think that a situation like low Synergy allowing the geist to give you you pretty dangerous near body-jacking conditions, mid range having lighter touch conditions which can be ignored but do nudge you to certain actions (possibly with an alternate buy-off; a way to not do Exactly what the geist wants, but similar enough to sate it), and then high Synergy giving beneficial conditions as the geist and host work together -- That's a system I could really support being implemented.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T13:41:59-07:00","id":237284,"title":"","content":"The issue is that Geist and Sin-eater <i>aren't</i> perfectly in-sync. In fact, &quot;The Bargain&quot; is frankly a bad term for it. It's not an actual bargain at all, it's simply &quot;will you let me live in your body if you get to live? Also, I'll throw in cool powers&quot;. If anything, it's an ultimatum, since the other choice is dying. There are no terms or conditions, and neither party can void the bargain. There's also very few Geists and very few mediums out there, meaning that a Geist can't be picky about who they merge with. Conflict doesn't mean &quot;angst&quot;, and &quot;Supernatural angst&quot; isn't a bad thing. Geist already has quite a bit of it, and quite a bit of it has to do with the Geist itself.<br /> <br /> For instance, in the book, we're given examples of Geists that <i>do</i> have the agenda of &quot;eat drink fuck fight&quot;. In fact, eating, drinking, fucking, or fighting is a viable way to regain Plasm (though it's mentioned once and barely at all). And you say that it's a selling point that Geist doesn't have Supernatural Angst... not only does it still have that, but you can't really call it a &quot;selling point&quot; since Geist is one of the least talked about games... Only Promethean has less posts in it's forum (which is surprising; though it does bode well for a Geist 2e)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The idea that if your geist wants you to do something you don't wanna, you can tell them to sit down and shut the hell up is an other selling point. </div> </div> </div> You can't, though. You can ignore them, which has no mechanical effect, but it's still going to constantly be going <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/63728/Dem-Bones-Geist-The-SinEaters\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Dem bones, dem bones, dem bones&quot;</a> in your head. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pYb8Wm6-QfA\" target=\"_blank\">Now hear the word of the Lord!</a><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm mean, sin-Eater cultures are essentially parties and Grave humor. If the condition sucked, you'd think it'd be more morbid, isntead of just morbid humor. That's all the evidence you need that The Sin-Eater's don't have the supernatural angst. </div> </div> </div>Sin-eaters party because the world sucks and the dead are everywhere. They party because they know what awaits everyone. The partying and grave humour in Geist works <i>because</i> of the darkness and horror of the <b>World of Darkness</b>. They're not partying because they have no problems, they're partying because they've died, and they could die again. &quot;Eat drink and be merry, for tomorrow we die&quot;.<br /> <br /> &#8203;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seraph Kitty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=237239#post237239\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">making it hostile can quickly make it feel like something the GM is manipulating just to screw the player's goals and frustrates the experience of geist which is, refreshingly, not a game about angst.<br /> There's already a splat for having a ride-along entity that can take over your body and makes you do terrible things: Inferno Possessed. Geist is not that game for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's also Vampire (Frenzy), Werewolf (<i>Kuruth</i>), and Promethean (Torment). Geist has that in the fluff, but in none of the mechanics. <br /> The fluff talks about how the Sin-eater can go to sleep and the Geist can take over, and things like that, but there's no mechanics to it, no weight to it. As I've mentioned before &quot;there's no weight to it&quot; is a common problem with Geist.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T18:21:31-07:00","id":237595,"title":"","content":"Referencing the frenzy systems in other games is in no way equivalent to the geist. In other games, experiencing primal/emotional triggers can drive you into fear and rage - this is a fine system, it works for them, and if there was something Just Like That in geist, but fit to its themes, I'd probably support it. But that is very different from a mechanic where the geist can take over and use the character's body for its own goals. In its worst cases of abuse, that can turn into &quot;player wants to do [this]; gm wants player to do [that] - roll for possession&quot;. Forcinng a character to act out the unrestrained fantasies of a Death archetype and then sticking the player with the consequences is a very hostile mechanic, and can quickly lead to extremely frustrating gameplay. It might be an experience some players want - and Inferno exists to supply it. There are better ways to reinforce geists themes. The social conditions, I think, is the best one I've heard so far. There was also another one some time ago in a different thread where you could bribe the geist with something similar to its archetype or manipulate it by appealing to its human remnants, which also works with the themes better. Discussions about giving the relationship with the geist mechanical teeth should start at Those points - not with possession.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T18:57:33-07:00","id":237619,"title":"","content":"As much as I enjoy hearing everyones perpectives, I feel the thread is getting a bit derailed and going into a debate about this particular aspect of Geist rather than a &quot;What would you like to see?&quot;. Everyone has made their arguements, and everyone has had a chance to speak their minds about the opposing sides arguements. From where I'm standing, it looks like we can all agree that the system needs a more active mechanism for interactions with the Geist, for good or ill.<br /> I dont feel like we need to continue this particular discussion any further. What needed to be said, seems to have been said allready.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Perhaps a seperate thread devoted to this discussion could be made? It is an interesting exchange of opinion, I find.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1958,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","user":"Krobeles","date":". 08-22-2014, 09:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T02:39:31-07:00","id":238070,"title":"","content":"What I'd like to see is some focus given to more of the ghost story tropes - particularly I think there's a lot of room for Bound characters to have a sort of 'cyclical story' that relates to their death or Bargain in some way, that they can either indulge or forcibly fight against.<br /> <br /> Also, has anyone read the Skinjacker Trilogy? It's a YA eries but it's got some damn fine inspiration/creepy tones for Geist","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T08:42:40-07:00","id":238223,"title":"","content":"Geist has a lot of good ideas. These ideas don't seem to be working together towards any one feel or type of campaign. I'd like to see Geist tightened up, focused on some particular playstyles, and then have the book reinforce its themes dutifully.<br /> <br /> Is this a game about second chances? Then the reason you came back, your Fetters (replace name?) need to be a major part of character creation, like Touchstones for Vampire or the Durance for Changeling.<br /> <br /> Is the game meant to focus on the tension of the Geist's will and the character's will? Then defining that will needs to be a part of character creation and there needs to be rules to represent that struggle.<br /> <br /> Is the game about enjoying life? Then enjoying life needs to be represented in the mechanics.<br /> <br /> Et cetera, et cetera, et cetera. Really, Geist isn't a bad game, just needs some polish and some focusing.<br /> <br /> Oh, and &quot;Murder Mystery&quot; needs to be a normal mode of play, and the powers / etc. need to support that. Three to five STs I know picked up Geist and said &quot;Oh hey. I'll run a Ghost Stories / Murder Mystery game.&quot; Then they player picked boneyard and the ST cried, usually never picking up the game again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 08-23-2014, 12:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T14:34:18-07:00","id":238536,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the powers kind of nip &quot;Murder mystery&quot; in the bud. Any attempt at a murder mystery is curtailed by the fact that Geists have amazing powers that can solve a mystery in a moment. This isn't necessarily BAD, per se. After all, <i>Pushing Daisies</i> is a great show about a guy who has a power that basically instantly solves a murder case in most instances. They get a lot of play out of subverting the usefulness of it. Geist, though, most of the time their powers are super effective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T12:47:13-07:00","id":239474,"title":"","content":"You can still run a murder mystery, it just needs a supernatural hook to be effective. Most of a Sin-Eaters powers of murder-solving play around with the ghost and body. What if the body is in a morque or a forensic lab, being studied by the actual police? What if there is no ghost, that the ghost that is, has been so throughly brain-blasted by whatever horror comitted the crime, as to render any communication with it neigh useless?<br /> And to be fair, which system really allows an effective murder mystery, outside of Hunter? As a Mage you run into much the same problems as with Sin-Eaters, a Vampire could possibly do something like leech memory out of the corpses blood and both Wereworlf and Vampire could have some ritual shit that allowed to fuck around the ghost too. Perhaps a Promethean or Changeling might be slightly more stunted, but I would be surprised if one could not create a Transmutation or Contract that allowed them to play around with things.<br /> <br /> I think what Geist needs, are story hooks to make suggestions as to how one might concievably run a murder mystery, given The Bounds bucket of murder-solving abillities without having the entire thing turn into a; &quot;The Storyteller has convieniently shot down your powers, for the sake of the story. Just go with it!&quot;.<br /> <br /> I agree with SoulGambit. The game has alot of disconnected (though very cool) thematic sparks strewn throughout the book, but with little to no mechanical impact to back them up. To be frank, at this point, I think throwing any of them out the door would be a shame. Perhaps a set of comprehensive mechanics could be pressented for each, and then the storyteller could deside for himself what his chronicle would be about?<br /> Is his particular chronicle about second chances? Then he uses the mechanics that emphasize the theme of second chances.<br /> Is his particular chronicle about the tension of the Geists will and the characters will? Then he uses the mechanics that emphazise the theme of mental dissonance.<br /> This way, everyone gets a slice of the Geist-cake, and the games thematic focus isn't shifted for anyone who doesn't specifically desire the focus to be shifted. Of course this might be a pipe-dream, as I could easily imagine a book that encompasses all of these mechanical elements, to take up something like 10000 pages, and nobody wants to write nor buy something like that, outside of a physics study.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T21:00:10-07:00","id":239888,"title":"","content":"You can address the issue by adjusting the powers, and/or putting a &quot;so you want to run a murder mystery&quot; section in the ST portion of the book. I suspect the best results will actually come from some combination of the two. I personally have no problems with boneyard, but that's -only- because I participated in / ran a Naruto Persistant World for some time and have oodles of experience with pesky Hyuuga. Whether or not other gamelines allow for an effective murder mystery doesn't really matter. New STs to the line consistently expect Geist to do murder mystery well, so it needs to do it if it wants to retain that population.<br /> <br /> Generally speaking, I follow the philosophy that a core book should set a tone and do a small number of types of games <i>really</i> well, with supplements introducing material to explore those types more and/or introduce new types. This is mostly personal preference, but I find it makes for an over-all better game.<br /> <br /> Mechanics are actually pretty easy once you decide on a theme and stick with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T03:06:39-07:00","id":240069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=239474#post239474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game has alot of disconnected (though very cool) thematic sparks strewn throughout the book, but with little to no mechanical impact to back them up</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a definite flaw of Geist. It's almost <i>too</i> harped on, though. <br /> <br /> As for murder mystery, the kind that it does best is a <i>Cold Case</i> style thing, not going to the morgue and interviewing a fresh corpse. Frankly the biggest thing that shoots that kind of story in the foot isn't even the Manifestations and how powerful they are; it's Plasmic Infusion. Though of course they can get a good lead by using their ability to touch a corpse and feel it's last moments. Even with just their base powers, Sin-eaters are a force to be reckoned with. They've got probably the most of any supernatural. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T03:46:15-07:00","id":240098,"title":"","content":"Which of the Geist writers are still around, and posting on the forum? I know Rose did, who else? What are their forum names? I kinda want some 'official' word on what Geist is supposed to be like and how things were intended to be. I know Baron Samedi wrote their bit in Mortal Remains, but did he write the corebook?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T15:06:02-07:00","id":240791,"title":"","content":"For story telling purposes, id love to see old laws bleeding out into the material world around powerful avernian gates.<br /> <br /> A kerberoi chronicle would be fun if they actually made sin-eaters lives harder in the real world. Otherwise, they'd just remain terrifying, but something that doesnt really stand in a SE's way, if theyre smart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T16:33:06-07:00","id":240883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=240098#post240098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which of the Geist writers are still around, and posting on the forum? I know Rose did, who else? What are their forum names? I kinda want some 'official' word on what Geist is supposed to be like and how things were intended to be. I know Baron Samedi wrote their bit in Mortal Remains, but did he write the corebook?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Geist book hasn't really even been announced yet, and it probably won't be this year. My guess is that we'll get an announcement in 2015 and the book in 2016.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T00:34:08-07:00","id":241156,"title":"","content":"I meant who wrote the original book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T21:27:35-07:00","id":241972,"title":"","content":"Rose Bailey and Matt Mcfarland, Rich Thomas are all active here. Eddy Webb is as well. Stew Wilson is busy being the master of both old and new Werewolf, in addition to whatever else he's working on, but he posts here as well. <br /> <br /> Of the names I can see in my book, I'm fairly certain that Joseph Carriker is still around, and Malcolm Sheppard spends time on the rpg.net forums, I believe.<br /> <br /> The designer of the game, Ethan Skemp (Who also was Designer for <i>Werewolf: The Forsaken </i>and <i>Changeling: The Lost</i>) seems to have moved on to work as a game designer with an indie game developer, Xaviant.<br /> <br /> The other developers/writers seem to have either moved on or just haven't been contracted for any recent projects. I haven't gotten the impression any of those who are around on the forums have the time/energy to do a post-mortem (heh) discussion of Geist. I'm sure you could find something like that floating around already, though I'd love it if they shared any other thoughts they have.<br /> <br /> Despite whatever flaws the first edition has, I think the process we've seen with the 2nd edition books thus far really speaks to a willingness to learn lessons and revisit things, demonstrated in what we've heard about Werewolf and Mage and what we've seen for Vampire. I'm sure when it's closer to next year there'll be more discussion of what Geist's future is looking like and what issues they're willing to address.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T07:16:34-07:00","id":242230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite whatever flaws the first edition has, I think the process we've seen with the 2nd edition books thus far really speaks to a willingness to learn lessons and revisit things, demonstrated in what we've heard about Werewolf and Mage and what we've seen for Vampire. I'm sure when it's closer to next year there'll be more discussion of what Geist's future is looking like and what issues they're willing to address. </div> </div> </div>This. I'm excited for all of the 2nd Edition books, even a hypothetical Geist one. Hell, I'll probably borrow one of my friend's Werewolf books when it becomes available to see if its worth playing (I am rather not fond of Forsaken, I admit). Blood and Smoke won me over, maybe Idigam will as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T02:52:15-07:00","id":242935,"title":"","content":"I did not write any of the Corebook or Book of the Dead. I'd love to work on a 2e though, and worked on the RMC as well as Mortal Remains.<br /> <br /> One thing with the Geist and the Sin-Eater is we have had a lot of games (Wraith, Dark Reflections, Risen, Kindred of the East, and outside WW/OPP, Deadlands) with a dark force (or light in Spectres case) that is struggled with, with possession systems and what not. To me, that is not BAD, not at all, but it has been done, and done well. While the merged psyches has been somewhat done in Mummy: The Resurrection, Geist feels like a very different game. I would not mind some system for sorting out stuff between Geist and Sin-Eater, but would not want it to be a major focus as really if anything Geist is somewhat more novel, with it not being an innately good or innately bad thing. Not wholly original, but not what has been done as much, at least by OPP.<br /> <br /> Now, something for that if your Synergy gets especially low (assuming a 2e uses Synergy or something like it) might work pretty well, but it would be a consequence of that. I don't want it to be totally off the table, but I don't want to retred ground tread by Wraith or other games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 08-28-2014, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T05:47:20-07:00","id":243030,"title":"","content":"I don't know. I absolutely love the themes and aesthetics of Geists, but it's that...in terms of styles of abilities, it kind of feels like Geist is watered-down version of Mage.<br /> <br /> What I would wish for is a lot stronger presence for Geist, (as opposed to the character, Sin-eater) in terms of what it actually is and what it does. For now, Geist seems mostly like to be a cosmetic thing. I don't necessarily mean that Geist should be each Sin-eater's inner antagonist, but more investment should be in that direction, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1229-torete","name":"torete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1229_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"125"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T16:33:09-07:00","id":243482,"title":"","content":"+1 for Geist not being an inner antagonist by default. I'd rather it be an actual, honest to goodness, ally with a few strings attached and some interesting plothooks. Then throw in some mechanic or whatever for antagonistic Geists for the people who are in to that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T18:44:47-07:00","id":243518,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of exploring the geist being in control in an entirely separate way. They don't have to be <i>antagonists</i> for you to struggle against them. You can still have conflict with your friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-28T19:58:34-07:00","id":243552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=243518#post243518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They don't have to be <i>antagonists</i> for you to struggle against them. You can still have conflict with your friends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. What if the Geist wants you to go have sex with a random person, and you're just not into those kinds of relationships? What if the Geist wants you to enjoy a saucy steak, but you're on a diet? What if you're a Vegan? What if the Geist wants you to go out and dance like its 1999, but you'd rather enjoy a quiet drink here in the WIP lounge?<br /> None of these are strictly antagonistic in nature, but still a situation in which your wishes are in conflict with those of your Geist, reasonable though those suggestions might be.<br /> What about an introverted person who becomes a Sin-Eater? That person might prefer his days to tick by playing World of Warcraft 24/7, but that is hardly the life experience the Geist signed up for. In this situation, the Geist even has the objectively correct idea (Dont play WoW to the detriment of your social life and career), yet the Sin-Eater might not agree. Although those kinds of situations are entirely manageable by a Storyteller winging it, I feel like we need something - Anything! - to mechanically repressent those kinds of disonnance, outside of &quot;Roll Synergy&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T03:39:56-07:00","id":243813,"title":"","content":"I think the Geist should be a potential enemy or ally depending on the player and have mechanics in place to allow each method. IE - High synergy you get a bonus, Low synergy your Geist jerks the steering wheel from time to time. Player v Geist doesn't have to be a central conflict, but that doesn't mean it can't be a minor one that crops up every now and again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T13:32:43-07:00","id":244298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=243552#post243552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed. What if the Geist wants you to go have sex with a random person, and you're just not into those kinds of relationships? What if the Geist wants you to enjoy a saucy steak, but you're on a diet? What if you're a Vegan? What if the Geist wants you to go out and dance like its 1999, but you'd rather enjoy a quiet drink here in the VIP lounge?</div> </div> </div> </div>This guy gets it. You don't have to be evil to cause conflict. And conversely, what about the Reaper who's Geist screams <i>kill kill kill</i> but the Sin-eater is just up on the rooftop (casually clinging to a gargoyle and standing on a crenulation, obvs) going &quot;patience, patience...&quot; while watching their victim? They're still working as allies, but they have different ways of doing things. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like we need something - Anything! - to mechanically repressent those kinds of disonnance, outside of &quot;Roll Synergy&quot;. </div> </div> </div> To be fair, we don't really even have that. It's one of the problems.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I used to consider Geist my favourite game line before I started trying to make a system overhaul. I used to not have the problems that other people had, but now after trying to address their problems I'm really starting to hate them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T16:22:19-07:00","id":245053,"title":"","content":"Oh, I almost forgot. I would really, really like the ability to actually eat people's Sins. Possibly have Fetters of my own (why I made the bargain), Fetters from my Geist (ooo... Mystery / Conspiracy), and Fetters I can claim from Ghosts (people? idk). Should *probably* be tied to recovering Plasm, but that isn't required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T19:20:43-07:00","id":245132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=244298#post244298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I used to consider Geist my favourite game line before I started trying to make a system overhaul. I used to not have the problems that other people had, but now after trying to address their problems I'm really starting to hate them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Geist really <i>needs</i> an overhaul, honestly. Right now it just feels like a bunch of interesting ideas without anything to really bring them together. <br /> <br /> Side note, I think its kind of weird that its the only game where you aren't the thing behind the colon in the title.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T19:26:40-07:00","id":245136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=245053#post245053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I almost forgot. I would really, really like the ability to actually eat people's Sins. Possibly have Fetters of my own (why I made the bargain), Fetters from my Geist (ooo... Mystery / Conspiracy), and Fetters I can claim from Ghosts (people? idk). Should *probably* be tied to recovering Plasm, but that isn't required.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god. I fucking love this idea, especially the idea of claiming the ghosts fetters, effectively &quot;Eating their sins&quot;. Might try to make some homebrew rule and throw it into my choronicle. Thanks man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T20:57:34-07:00","id":245161,"title":"","content":"When I first read Geist, I skimmedi t like three times looking for where the rules for eating people's sins was. I was rather weirded out that they weren't there.<br /> <br /> Another issue is that there is no Masquerade / Lie equivalent. When I first read the book, I thought this was <i>awesome</i>. In fact, I presented to my players as, &quot;And unlike every other splat, you may feel free to tell as many people as possible that you can speak to the dead. If you're really good at it, maybe you'll even get your own talk show.&quot; Implying that it was people's general attitude towards the afterlife that created a quasi Masquerade rather than any effort on part of the Sin Eaters. People maintained their own Masquerade and fooled themselves because to do otherwise would be to accept death, which people have a hard time doing. Everyone thought this was pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Then it turned out Geist's powers include turning into a flying incorporeal tentacle monster and eating state senators on national television and dropping the same exact old car from a 10 story building. Repeatedly. Out of thin air.<br /> <br /> One of these things does not belong. Either a Lie equivalent needs to exist, or Geist powers need to be built from the ground up as &quot;things mortals could explain away if they tried hard enough.&quot; The issue with the latter is that its harder to make the powers fun/evocative/cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T03:57:12-07:00","id":245271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=245161#post245161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I first read Geist, I skimmedi t like three times looking for where the rules for eating people's sins was. I was rather weirded out that they weren't there.<br /> <br /> Another issue is that there is no Masquerade / Lie equivalent. When I first read the book, I thought this was <i>awesome</i>. In fact, I presented to my players as, &quot;And unlike every other splat, you may feel free to tell as many people as possible that you can speak to the dead. If you're really good at it, maybe you'll even get your own talk show.&quot; Implying that it was people's general attitude towards the afterlife that created a quasi Masquerade rather than any effort on part of the Sin Eaters. People maintained their own Masquerade and fooled themselves because to do otherwise would be to accept death, which people have a hard time doing. Everyone thought this was pretty cool.<br /> <br /> Then it turned out Geist's powers include turning into a flying incorporeal tentacle monster and eating state senators on national television and dropping the same exact old car from a 10 story building. Repeatedly. Out of thin air.<br /> <br /> One of these things does not belong. Either a Lie equivalent needs to exist, or Geist powers need to be built from the ground up as &quot;things mortals could explain away if they tried hard enough.&quot; The issue with the latter is that its harder to make the powers fun/evocative/cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont nessesarily see this as an issue. What stops a Vampire from doing that, outside of the fact that they will be killed by the other Vampires? Mages and Werewolves atleast make people forget shit (well, if the wolves transform, anyway) but Vampires have no such luxury. Whats to stop a Vampire from having a talk show and showing everyone that the supernal exists? Whats stopping a Promethean from comming to the conclusion; &quot;Perhaps if everyone knew that I existed and what I was, they wouldn't hate me so much!&quot;<br /> I usually chalk it up to two things. First: if everyone knew you could to ghosts and revive the dead, EVERYONE would want your aid. There is an example of this in Mirrors, in which they suggest Sin-Eaters literally has their doors kicked down by mobs who want to get thier help. Second: I know this is a universal point, but Hunters. If everyone knew you could talk to ghosts, you'd be harried by Hunters around the clock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T12:21:16-07:00","id":245553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=245271#post245271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dont nessesarily see this as an issue. What stops a Vampire from doing that, outside of the fact that they will be killed by the other Vampires? Mages and Werewolves atleast make people forget shit (well, if the wolves transform, anyway) but Vampires have no such luxury. Whats to stop a Vampire from having a talk show and showing everyone that the supernal exists? Whats stopping a Promethean from comming to the conclusion; &quot;Perhaps if everyone knew that I existed and what I was, they wouldn't hate me so much!&quot;<br /> I usually chalk it up to two things. First: if everyone knew you could to ghosts and revive the dead, EVERYONE would want your aid. There is an example of this in Mirrors, in which they suggest Sin-Eaters literally has their doors kicked down by mobs who want to get thier help. Second: I know this is a universal point, but Hunters. If everyone knew you could talk to ghosts, you'd be harried by Hunters around the clock.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the case of Vampires? Paranoia and the capacity to meet final death. Sin Eaters are almost impossible to put down permanently.<br /> <br /> In the case of Promethens? Disquiet. Honestly, a Promethean trying to &quot;come out&quot; but suffering from massive amount of Disquiet would be a cool story *files away for later*<br /> <br /> Anyways, I'm okay with the only thing being between Sin Eaters and Hunters is a Masquerade equivalent (instead of a Lie equivalent), but that needs to be covered. Personally, I'd just make witnessing over Geist powers *always* an Integrity break (that gets Obsession way too often for the Sin Eater's own good) and that overt supernatural stuff is blurry / distorted when recorded. Enough so that the crazy reporter from Network Zero and desperate people track you down, but not enough to be *proof*. But that's personal preferance, there are a bunch of ways to skin this cat.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T13:39:50-07:00","id":245638,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eaters are not impossible to put down permanently. It just takes work and time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T13:55:28-07:00","id":245643,"title":"","content":"One tiny question. Is a Chronicle something that can happen in foreseeable future, or I should work with Sin-Eater's current core? <br /> <br /> Frankly, I need Sin-Eaters for my homebrew because the conspiracy I cook up logically would have a relationship with Sin-Eaters, even if it would be a cold war like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T14:33:31-07:00","id":245654,"title":"","content":"The decision has not been made if it will happen or not. Vampire has one, Werewolf, Mage, Promethean and Changeling are getting one. We will have to see what happens there and they will decide on Hunter, Geist, and Mummy. I'd love to see one, personally, but we don't have a date or anything definite. I can say the RMC coming up for Geist is the system in the current corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T14:45:30-07:00","id":245658,"title":"","content":"A personal hope will be for Geists to be treated somewhat like Personas or Stands, capable of manifesting through the Sin-Eater's will and interacting with the world. Draws on some more modern horror(ish) material, means that every Sin-Eater has access to a set of standard poltergeisty effects, and is cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T14:45:46-07:00","id":245659,"title":"","content":"Hunter has GMC rules update, though, so that's not full chronicle, but still a good thing. I would be already happy if only GMC rules update for Geist got released, as I could run that WW2 era Task Force Valkyrie x Geist chronicle without deliberating how to make it compatible with GMC on my own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T15:01:38-07:00","id":245662,"title":"","content":"Oh I'd love even a smaller GMC update. Hopefully we can get something. Though at this stage, more Geist I will be happy with regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T15:12:14-07:00","id":245663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh I'd love even a smaller GMC update. Hopefully we can get something. Though at this stage, more Geist I will be happy with regardless. </div> </div> </div>Well, one of reasons I'm writing a conspiracy that should include Sin-Eaters as the supernatural splats they commonly interact with is because the person who introduced me to NWoD in first place happens to like Geist the most, and any homebrews are likely welcome with scarcity of canon material in comparison to other lines. I think I should start writing it more seriously after September, I think, and hopefully get my NWoD buddies from Skype to provide some feedback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-31T21:54:19-07:00","id":245876,"title":"","content":"If they are NPCs you can probably build them with Dread Powers. Didn't Mortal Remains update some of them or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-01T05:23:12-07:00","id":246087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If they are NPCs you can probably build them with Dread Powers. Didn't Mortal Remains update some of them or something? </div> </div> </div>I'm too pedantic to build supernaturals with Dread Powers. I go for other splats when I introduce a supernatural.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T09:43:50-07:00","id":246859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=245161#post245161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of these things does not belong. Either a Lie equivalent needs to exist, or Geist powers need to be built from the ground up as &quot;things mortals could explain away if they tried hard enough.&quot; The issue with the latter is that its harder to make the powers fun/evocative/cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, most of the Manifestations are invisible to people who can't see into Twilight. Of course, on the other hand <i>that makes no fucking sense with some of the powers</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=245553#post245553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case of Vampires? Paranoia and the capacity to meet final death. Sin Eaters are almost impossible to put down permanently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. All you need to do is make it prohibitively hard for the Geist. If you put the Sin-eater in concrete and dump him in a lake, what does the Geist gain from reviving him? Even the most obsessive Geist is just going to say &quot;fuck it&quot; and let them die and find a new place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=245658#post245658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A personal hope will be for Geists to be treated somewhat like Personas or Stands, capable of manifesting through the Sin-Eater's will and interacting with the world. Draws on some more modern horror(ish) material, means that every Sin-Eater has access to a set of standard poltergeisty effects, and is cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Phantasmal Key! Rage and Marionette are Stands!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=245662#post245662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I'd love even a smaller GMC update. Hopefully we can get something. Though at this stage, more Geist I will be happy with regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like the problem with this is that it's a lot easier to update risking Willpower and a few Endowments than it is to update ALL OF THE MANIFESTATIONS. Hell, GMC still leaves the Tactics un-updated.<br /> <br /> QUOTE=Katsura;n246087]I'm too pedantic to build supernaturals with Dread Powers. I go for other splats when I introduce a supernatural.[/QUOTE] Ewww... why? If they aren't player characters, you don't need those hard and fast mechanics. Hell, I want to run a Supernatural game using only Dread Powers and monster templates...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T09:54:36-07:00","id":246876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=246859#post246859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Phantasmal Key! Rage and Marionette are Stands!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but I want it as a built in feature. Plus I'd like to see a complete, and I mean complete, rehash of the Manifestation/Key System. As is I think it's the most confusing part of the system, and a bit of a turn off for a lot of players (it was for my group). I ended up replacing it entirely with a custom &quot;make your own power&quot; system, loosely inspired by the original structure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T11:30:27-07:00","id":246981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ewww... why? If they aren't player characters, you don't need those hard and fast mechanics. Hell, I want to run a Supernatural game using only Dread Powers and monster templates... </div> </div> </div>Too autistic (diagnosed with Asperger's from early childhood) to hold back, whether in roleplaying or research stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Phantasmal Key! Rage and Marionette are Stands! </div> </div> </div>That makes Jotaro's thought that he was possessed by &quot;an evil spirit&quot; hilarious in hindsight.<br /> <br /> Also, Stand users do see ghosts.<br /> <br /> Also, crossover between Araki's <i>Deadman's Questions</i>and Geist could be interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 09-02-2014, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T12:56:29-07:00","id":247062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=246859#post246859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ewww... why? If they aren't player characters, you don't need those hard and fast mechanics. Hell, I want to run a Supernatural game using only Dread Powers and monster templates...</div> </div> </div> </div>Tangential though it might be (At best!) to the main topic of the thread, I actually do this too. I dont want to plan out my encounters in the style of &quot;The PC's beat this antagonist&quot; or &quot;The PC's get beaten by this antagonist&quot;, and by having loosely defined stats and mechanics for my antagonists I constantly feel inclined to skev the stats in favor of whatever I feel like on the fly. By having ridge traits like this, the PC's victory will entirely depend on their own ingeniuty and the luck of the dice. I also dont want my PC's to feel like their enemies are &quot;Just that storyteller character, with all the bougos powers that he comes up with on the fly&quot;. I want them to essentially feel like they're fighting another PC with a different agenda and moral code, which sets them at odd's with the PC's, and by modeling the antagonists after splats with characters sheets and all, that experience is easily conveyed. It also makes it easy to gauge how much more powerful a powerful NPC is to the PC's, by easily tallying up much experience it would take to bumb a newly minted PC to the level of the antagonist.<br /> I want the PC's victories and loses to be dignified and the easiest way of doing that, I feel, is to have ridge traits for my antagonists exactly as their PC counterparts has.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T12:59:18-07:00","id":247067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Katsura</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=246981#post246981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes Jotaro's thought that he was possessed by &quot;an evil spirit&quot; hilarious in hindsight.<br /> <br /> Also, Stand users do see ghosts.<br /> <br /> Also, crossover between Araki's <i>Deadman's Questions</i>and Geist could be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find Person and JJBA to be excellent Geist inspiration in general. Creepy plots, strand powers, ephemeral beings few can see. The supernatural powers featured in Jojo, especially later volumes, embody the sort of strangeness I hope for in Geist Manifestations. Bizarre, mysterious powers with strange rules and applications, each a little mystery in itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 09-02-2014, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-02T14:29:46-07:00","id":247120,"title":"","content":"If Goetic Demon can manifest in Stand like form, it can be also inspiration for Awakening (and totally you can have Not!Stand in Ascension with Manifest Avatar)<br /> <br /> I know Araki actually wrote a work on horror genre, so I probably should start saving money to both ship in a copy and hire some moonrunereader to translate it for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T08:54:07-07:00","id":247885,"title":"","content":"A few thoughts:<br /> <br /> * If I had to pick a chronicle focus, I'd go for Abmortals. They are the fly in the ointment in terms of the progression of life and death and are also sort of dark reflections of Sin-Eaters (who are also cheating death, in their own fashion). If I had my druthers, the rules from WoD: Immortals would be included in the Chronicle book and effects added to reflect how they mess with things just by existing in an area. Their activities should cause issues that can't be ignored by the local ghosts and ghost-adjacent. <br /> * I love the idea of Sin-Eaters taking on the fetters of others. Resolving them would then become a big focus of their activity. I'd almost want it to be their primary means for recharging their ghost-juice. It should also definitely be something they can do post-mortem, so sin-eaters can finally actually do the death-bed thing where they take on the burdens of the dying so they can pass on peacefully. Let's actually implement the title, people!<br /> * I am in agreement with those who note that the murder-mystery aspect is just too easily bypassed by their powers. Also, I was flabbergasted that they have as one of their basic powers the ability to make a ghost lucid. This just torpedoes so much potential plot and role-play, I can't imagine why they included it. Figuring out what the deal is with a ghost should be the point of a session, not something you can just ask them after hitting them with a magic &quot;be rational&quot; power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T07:36:21-07:00","id":248836,"title":"","content":"My pet Chronicle idea for Geist is &quot;Out of the Light: the Shadow Chronicles&quot; based loosely on this quote from the Allegory of the Cave.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cAny one who has common sense will remember that the bewilderments of the eyes are of two kinds, and arise from two causes, either from coming out of the light or from going into the light.&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T08:00:05-07:00","id":248866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=247885#post247885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* I am in agreement with those who note that the murder-mystery aspect is just too easily bypassed by their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;How did this guy die?&quot; is already immediately half-answered by the nature of Thresholds and deathmarks and the point of dealing with ghosts is more &quot;how do we get them to leave?/what do we do with them?&quot; than the more peripheral question of &quot;how did they get here?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I was flabbergasted that they have as one of their basic powers the ability to make a ghost lucid. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Make a ghost able to be interacted with as a character instead of a setpiece at the cost of blood and plasm and also you have to be able to touch them&quot; is something that is rather more and less than what you're making it out to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This just torpedoes so much potential plot and role-play, I can't imagine why they included it. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Spend ten minutes running and screaming and trying to bind the thing&quot; is not what I would call &quot;plot.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Figuring out what the deal is with a ghost should be the point of a session, not something you can just ask them after hitting them with a magic &quot;be rational&quot; power. </div> </div> </div>Except the text points out that ghosts are biased and often incorrect and do not gain knowledge they did not have in the process of dying, lethal damage is not a minor cost to pay, and plasm scarcity is observably a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-04-2014, 11:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T12:50:07-07:00","id":249069,"title":"","content":"Tbh. It is a useless power. If it didn't exist, guess what? Ghosts would be lucid and talk to the PCs anyways because they are a quest giver and the ST isn't going to have their players spend ten minutes running and screaming before getting to the actual quest. Maybe a little scare tactics to characterize the ghost and weave in some hints to the actual plot. If anything, the power existing makes getting quests harder Now the ST is obligated to occasionally make it useful, which means instead of the ghost calmly sitting down for tea its picking up a bazooka.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong. Its not really a power that detracts from the game in some horrible fashion. Its &quot;meh,&quot; &quot;okay,&quot; &quot;whatever.&quot; A waste of wordcount at best. It doesn't add much in the way of drama to the story and only exists because of a false set of assumptions the reader won't make unless you specifically force them to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T13:42:27-07:00","id":249117,"title":"","content":"I think on a personal scale, being a Sin Eater should be about unfinished business an the repetition of actions from life after death. There are some Sin-Eaters who slip back into their old lives and continue to do the same shit that got them dead in the first place, some use their death as a cleansing and abandon their old ways, giving it the figner as they drive into the sunset.<br /> <br /> But just like he ghosts that they deal with, the life they left should call back to them and influence their actions in perhaps odd and unusual ways, in the same way a phantom is drawn to wail and re-enact the night of their death every year.<br /> <br /> It's a game of second chances: Do you grasp it or let it slip away, and what are the consequences of each choice?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T20:05:26-07:00","id":249405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=246876#post246876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but I want it as a built in feature. Plus I'd like to see a complete, and I mean complete, rehash of the Manifestation/Key System. As is I think it's the most confusing part of the system, and a bit of a turn off for a lot of players (it was for my group). I ended up replacing it entirely with a custom &quot;make your own power&quot; system, loosely inspired by the original structure.</div> </div> </div> </div>It definitely needs it. What was the original structure?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=247067#post247067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find Person and JJBA to be excellent Geist inspiration in general. Creepy plots, strand powers, ephemeral beings few can see. The supernatural powers featured in Jojo, especially later volumes, embody the sort of strangeness I hope for in Geist Manifestations. Bizarre, mysterious powers with strange rules and applications, each a little mystery in itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Persona actually gets the shout out in Geist's inspiration section.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=247885#post247885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A few thoughts:<br /> * If I had to pick a chronicle focus, I'd go for Abmortals. They are the fly in the ointment in terms of the progression of life and death and are also sort of dark reflections of Sin-Eaters (who are also cheating death, in their own fashion). If I had my druthers, the rules from WoD: Immortals would be included in the Chronicle book and effects added to reflect how they mess with things just by existing in an area. Their activities should cause issues that can't be ignored by the local ghosts and ghost-adjacent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Abmortals would be a good focus <i>if</i> they elaborated on them, and gave them a reason to be &quot;bad&quot;. I mean, what stops an Abmortal from putting on a costume and fighting crime currently? What reason do Sin-eaters have for hating them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T20:20:37-07:00","id":249423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=248866#post248866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;How did this guy die?&quot; is already immediately half-answered by the nature of Thresholds and deathmarks and the point of dealing with ghosts is more &quot;how do we get them to leave?/what do we do with them?&quot; than the more peripheral question of &quot;how did they get here?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> This question is a lot easier to answer when you can say &quot;how do we get you to leave?&quot;<br /> Think of <i>Ghostwhisperer</i> or <i>Supernatural</i>, or any show like that. Almost all of them would be solved instantly if they could ask the ghost questions and communicate freely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Make a ghost able to be interacted with as a character instead of a setpiece at the cost of blood and plasm and also you have to be able to touch them&quot; is something that is rather more and less than what you're making it out to be. </div> </div> </div>Ghosts aren't setpieces to begin with. There's not really even any purpose to dealing with the ghosts that are only set pieces. They just loop around and do their thing, playing out how they died. It's the ones like Poltergeists and Yellowbones that you have to worry about.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Spend ten minutes running and screaming and trying to bind the thing&quot; is not what I would call &quot;plot.&quot; </div> </div> </div> Look at any ghost story. Most of the plot is centered on knowing who the ghost is and what they want. Once they figure that out, the only problem is the ghost stopping them from burning it's bones or whatever when the ghosts are the enemies (<i>Supernatural</i>) or solving their death if the ghosts are victims (<i>Ghost Whisperer, Tru Calling</i>). Sin-eaters skip that step. They go right to &quot;hey, what's the problem? Cool, let's solve it.&quot; In fact, their only real issue is often going to <i>be</i> binding the thing. They just have to get it to hold still and they can probably stop it murdering people with a bit of Plasm and Blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except the text points out that ghosts are biased and often incorrect and do not gain knowledge they did not have in the process of dying, lethal damage is not a minor cost to pay, and plasm scarcity is observably a thing. </div> </div> </div>No it doesn't. In fact in several places it says that ghosts <i>can</i> gain knowledge. Ghosts get experience points even after they're dead, that's why Yellowbones are so deadly, and why the Underworld is a great place to learn. They also can actually be <i>smarter</i> than they were in life because Power=Intelligence once you restore their cognizance. Sure, some might be dicks and hold back information if you're just interrogating them, but I can't think of a reason a ghost wouldn't give you straight answers if you were literally asking for help solving the ghost's own murder.<br /> <br /> More than that, Plasm isn't actually that scarce. Regaining it is just unobtrusive and undefined. You can get Plasm back by getting into a big fight, or doing drugs with a rusty needle. You also get all your Plasm back for helping a ghost pass on, meaning that it's always worth it to spend a point of it to understand a ghost. Or, since 1L is a heavy price to pay, 2 plasm and 1B.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T00:31:59-07:00","id":249623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=249405#post249405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It definitely needs it. What was the original structure?</div> </div> </div> </div>The structure of having set keys, they purchasing manifestations and gaining the key'd versions. I took that and adapted it into a more freeform, DIY power system where the Sin-Eater builds her own unique Manifesations by linking together keys, manifestations and assigning triggers. <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1qB-KCdwuN6-qTwTj09k5VpCWh96oLH15EvnZOYXrh7Q/edit#heading=h.mbn5myjhywkx\" target=\"_blank\">Peruse if you please</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T06:31:13-07:00","id":249728,"title":"","content":"Personally, I love the Threshold an Key system, I think it's great and thematically appropriate - what I'm not a fan of is the Keys themselves, since they don't, in my opinion, connect too well to the fundamental essence of the Sin-Eaters and are too much like generic power grouping. I wouldn't want a more DIY power structure for them, to be honest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T07:23:28-07:00","id":249770,"title":"","content":"I agree that Mage-style isn't appropriate to them. I also feel that the Key + Manifestation system needs an overhaul. I do like the &quot;feel&quot; and aethetics of the keys themselves. Not the particular ones, but the idea of having keys and that being the source of your supernatural power.<br /> <br /> That said, its a hassle to integrate as an X+Y = Effect system. Running idea is that you can use a key directly to apply some debuff that makes the person susceptable to manifestations. But that feels off or meh. I considered nixing Manifestations entirely and making Keys powers within themselves (maybe a Hold (know stuff), Lock (deny Thing), and Unlock (flood with thing) structure? *shrugs*).<br /> <br /> Defining what Geists are suppossed to actually be able to do, however, is actually pretty hard. Ignoring structure for a moment, what types of things should Geists be able to actually do? They are effectively Ghost-Themed Necromancers.\\<br /> <br /> Oh that said. Cribbing Idigam''s new ritual strcture pretty much exactly is amazing and fits geist perfectly. IF Build Your Own powers belong somewhere, its there. I still don't think they do, but if they exist, that is where they should be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 09-05-2014, 10:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T11:12:36-07:00","id":249953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=249405#post249405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Abmortals would be a good focus <i>if</i> they elaborated on them, and gave them a reason to be &quot;bad&quot;. I mean, what stops an Abmortal from putting on a costume and fighting crime currently? What reason do Sin-eaters have for hating them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that (in addition to them often being serial killers to support their immortality) that they should have some sort of negative effect just by existing. Like, they throw off the whole balance of the world. One idea that comes to mind is that they &quot;displace&quot; their death sort of like Sin-Eaters do, so that every time they avoid death someone else (who wasn't supposed to die yet) takes the hit and this has weird effects on reality. Maybe the resultant ghosts are messed up because they died before their time or the death-energy just builds up in their vicinity in a way sort of like Promethean Wastelands, causing a high incidence of accidents and disease and stuff as reality over-compensates for their immortality. Lots of possibilities (and plenty of cross-over potential).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-05T12:45:42-07:00","id":250059,"title":"","content":"I don't agree with abmortals needing something that makes them natural antagonists - but Sin Eaters COULD USE some sort of natural antagonists. I think the best answer is that such a book needs to introduce a natural antagonist that no sin eater - no matter how evil - can truly ignore.<br /> <br /> I like abmortals as is - gives me a different template that I can give a mortal if I want to make an interesting character - but the template itself doesn't dictate how I use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-06T20:50:13-07:00","id":251210,"title":"","content":"I'd like room for expansion: Geist is one of my favorite games tonally and while I can wrap my head around the experiment of putting EVERYTHING into one book, I felt like it didn't leave enough room to actually dig into the great stuff they gave us. I'd love full write-ups on the Archetypes, for example, or a series of sample Krewes to help everyone wrap their minds around the concept. Or even just sample Krewes to pick up and drop into play as needed.<br /> <br /> It's actually hard to say what I want for the second edition, because a lot of what I want is enough of an expansion on what was in the first edition to really enjoy it like I want to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1097-underwoodfive","name":"underwoodfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T05:51:56-07:00","id":252206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reason for Sin-Eater's to oppose Abmortals: Almost every single Abmortal is a serial killer.<br /> <br /> Serial murder results in unclean deaths, according to Synergy rules, and violent deaths are likely to produce Ghosts. Thus, Abmortals are likely to leave strings of pissed off specters in their wake, which makes the Sin-Eater's job harder, because ghosts can tell who can see them and will badger the Sin-Eater until they get help.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the general arguement against this is that this assumes that the Sin-Eater gives a shit about Ghosts. The Sin-Eaters &quot;Job&quot; isn't really a job, so much as a self-imposed vocation. Nobody is forcing the Sin-Eater to do it (The Geist might, but its just as likely to not give a shit) so the door is entirely open for the Sin-Eater to not give a shit.<br /> What if the Ghosts pester the Sin-Eater about it? What stops him from destroying the ghosts and eating their corpus?<br /> <br /> Personally, I feel like this is a bad arguement, because it could be said for anybody and everything. If your PC's are entirely apathetic dickbags, then your story isn't really going anywhere in the first place, no matter what you throw at them. Unless you throw it directly in their faces of course, which you still totally do with the Abmortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T10:47:38-07:00","id":252478,"title":"","content":"If your PCs are entirely apathetic dickbags, isn't Any story not really going to go anywhere? Sure, other gamelines may have more invasive and threatening things to throw at them, but no one's 'forcing' them either; the baseline assumptions of all the games is that the PCs care about the splat's &quot;main job&quot; at least enough - or they'd be playing a different game. Vampires can ignore blood and politics by grabbing a few dominated humans and going on vacation; werewolves don't /have/ to deal with spirits; changeling can entirely focus on trying to be human if they're willing to ignore people getting taken. Sin-Eaters might not have a &quot;strong motivation&quot; (if, say, a man perpetually on fire begging for his daughter to be safe isn't strong enough for you), but character apathy can ruin every game.<br /> <br /> [addendum:] I will concede that Sin Eaters would be well served by a stronger motivation, but I think that is more of an issue that stems from poor presentation (which I'd say is geist's primary weakness), not from total apathy. [and, lest we forget, many initial corebooks suffered from poor presentation; I tell my werewolf players to ignore the core and read Lore and Rage first.] I'd also love to see an &quot;outside context problem&quot; introduced - but that's a concept that was launched with the chronicle books, and it's not necessarily a fault of 1e to lack them. But they aren't without a reason to care, certainly no more so than other splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Second Chance for<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=709\" data-tempid=\"temp_709_1572548741915_354\" /><br /> A Beautiful Madness</div>","edited":{"userid":425,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","user":"Seraph Kitty","date":".  merged posts 09-08-2014, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/425-seraph-kitty","name":"Seraph Kitty","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar425_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-08T11:58:10-07:00","id":252531,"title":"","content":"Yes, thank you! The &quot;they have no reason to care&quot; argumentation was starting to bug me and I hadn't put my finger on why. <br /> <br /> Your reason to care is the same reason any medium in fiction has to care: you can see and hear the ghosts. They can tell that you can see and hear them. So they're going to keep asking and you're going to keep seeing problems. You <i>could </i>obstinately ignore them, but that would make you a tragic (and probably unbalanced) NPC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T04:58:41-07:00","id":253234,"title":"","content":"I personally need Sin Eaters to remotely care, as my homebrew Hunter Conspiracy does ghost related things that may be questionable. Letting their own members being possessed permamently by beings which really run whole business, as part of ancestor worship, while enslaving non-ancestor ghosts when it suits their interests. There may be tensions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T22:52:48-07:00","id":253852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=252206#post252206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I feel like this is a bad arguement, because it could be said for anybody and everything. If your PC's are entirely apathetic dickbags, then your story isn't really going anywhere in the first place, no matter what you throw at them. Unless you throw it directly in their faces of course, which you still totally do with the Abmortals.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gabby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=252531#post252531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, thank you! The &quot;they have no reason to care&quot; argumentation was starting to bug me and I hadn't put my finger on why.<br /> <br /> Your reason to care is the same reason any medium in fiction has to care: you can see and hear the ghosts. They can tell that you can see and hear them. So they're going to keep asking and you're going to keep seeing problems. You <i>could </i>obstinately ignore them, but that would make you a tragic (and probably unbalanced) NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue is that without some overarching reason--the Sensitivity in Princess, the Orders in Mage, the Oath in Forsaken--you don't really have any splat-wide reason for doing anything. Yes, individual Sin-eaters with a conscience--likely player characters--will care. But there's no reason that the average Sin-eater would. The setting only works if the players decided they want to be good guys who benevolently take up the mantle of ghost busters.<br /> <br /> The other half of this is that the fluff <i>acts</i> as if they care but gives them no reason to do so. Why would krewes fight over territory for the right to... solve crimes and lay ghosts to rest? Why would they bother with Abmortals that aren't serial killers? I mean, the Hungry Exorcist eats ghosts and that's supposed to be super bad, but... why? Why should Sin-eaters care about that?<br /> <br /> The average medium in a fictional setting is going to be motivated by a sense of purpose, but that's because we're only focusing on that one medium who makes for the best story. We don't see any others in the world who ignore their gifts or who use their ability to talk to ghosts to figure out the password and security codes of bank vaults, or just have ephemeral beings shake the tables and make spectral manifestations pretending to be dead loved ones to con people. Yes, the PCs will likely want to do good things because they're good guys. But many won't care because it doesn't personally effect them. Order and Covenant and Tribe gives someone a reason to care.<br /> <br /> Geists don't have that. So their entire society seems to work on &quot;It's the right thing!&quot; but there's still talk of infighting and all that even when there's no logical reason for it. The setting is very flat. And even then, this is the World of Darkness. Not every PC is going to want to help lay ghosts to rest because &quot;it's the right thing to do&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 09-10-2014, 01:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T23:18:41-07:00","id":253863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=253852#post253852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would krewes fight over territory for the right to... solve crimes and lay ghosts to rest?</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gang#Types_and_structure\" target=\"_blank\">It's like you're totally unfamiliar with how street gangs work.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T23:28:51-07:00","id":253864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=253852#post253852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issue is that without some overarching reason--the Sensitivity in Princess, the Orders in Mage, the Oath in Forsaken--you don't really have any splat-wide reason for doing anything. Yes, individual Sin-eaters with a conscience--likely player characters--will care. But there's no reason that the average Sin-eater would. The setting only works if the players decided they want to be good guys who benevolently take up the mantle of ghost busters.<br /> <br /> The other half of this is that the fluff <i>acts</i> as if they care but gives them no reason to do so. Why would krewes fight over territory for the right to... solve crimes and lay ghosts to rest? Why would they bother with Abmortals that aren't serial killers? I mean, the Hungry Exorcist eats ghosts and that's supposed to be super bad, but... why? Why should Sin-eaters care about that?<br /> <br /> The average medium in a fictional setting is going to be motivated by a sense of purpose, but that's because we're only focusing on that one medium who makes for the best story. We don't see any others in the world who ignore their gifts or who use their ability to talk to ghosts to figure out the password and security codes of bank vaults, or just have ephemeral beings shake the tables and make spectral manifestations pretending to be dead loved ones to con people. Yes, the PCs will likely want to do good things because they're good guys. But many won't care because it doesn't personally effect them. Order and Covenant and Tribe gives someone a reason to care.<br /> <br /> Geists don't have that. So their entire society seems to work on &quot;It's the right thing!&quot; but there's still talk of infighting and all that even when there's no logical reason for it. The setting is very flat. And even then, this is the World of Darkness. Not every PC is going to want to help lay ghosts to rest because &quot;it's the right thing to do&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't say that they nessesarily had to be good, just that they shouldn't be apathetic. As long as your story is progressing and people are having fun, you're doing something right. You could just as easily have a story about a selfish Sin-Eater Necromancer plummeting the Dead Dominions for power (and exploiting ghosts to the same effect) as you could a Sin-Eater playing ghost buster.<br /> Personally, I wouldn't want a clear cut villian like the Abyss in Mage or the Strix in Vampire. Those seem too &quot;Evil for Eldritch unknowable reasons&quot; kinds of evil for Geist. I think the fact that the antagonists in Geist are antagonists wither because you wronged them yourself (Kerberoi, angry Ghosts/Geists) or because you have different political views to them (Sacrosanct, Abmortals).<br /> That said, I agree that antagnost aspect of Geist is slightly lacking, especially since the Kerberoi cant hound you into the living world, so as soon as you're back up, you're rather safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-09T23:38:26-07:00","id":253865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=253864#post253864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I agree that antagnost aspect of Geist is slightly lacking, especially since the Kerberoi cant hound you into the living world, so as soon as you're back up, you're rather safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I strongly suspect that however the Enforcement Numen gets carried over will include something like a temporary anchor of &quot;[Subject of Kerberos-Assigned Task]&quot; for ghostly subjects, if nothing else. (Also, I note with some trepidation the phrase &quot;largely bound to the Underworld with few exceptions.&quot; That's a worrying anomaly to run across.)<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I'm fairly certain the fact that both of the corebook's sample Kerberoi have their divergences from the basic role of &quot;impartial enforcer of the Old Laws&quot; highlighted isn't a coincidence - their having/retaining/developing personalities and agendas is definitely something that seems to be present in the 1e portrayal to some degree, if the story hook concerning the Black Madonna in Glimpses of the Unknown is any indication","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-10-2014, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T11:42:21-07:00","id":254487,"title":"","content":"The fact that Sin-eaters can act like muggle street gangs is sort of the problem. There's no reason for them to do what they do, nothing supernaturally compels them, and the only culture is the same kind of culture that mortals have. There's no greater drive than that. Territory for the sake of territory doesn't really even do Sin-eaters any good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=253864#post253864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say that they nessesarily had to be good, just that they shouldn't be apathetic.</div> </div> </div> </div>There-in lies the rub: You can't design a setting and say &quot;as long as no one's apathetic, it'll be fine&quot;, because there's no reason NOT to be apathetic. Geist <i>needs</i> reasons, but it doesn't currently support any.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, I wouldn't want a clear cut villian like the Abyss in Mage or the Strix in Vampire. Those seem too &quot;Evil for Eldritch unknowable reasons&quot; kinds of evil for Geist. I think the fact that the antagonists in Geist are antagonists wither because you wronged them yourself (Kerberoi, angry Ghosts/Geists) or because you have different political views to them (Sacrosanct, Abmortals).<br /> That said, I agree that antagnost aspect of Geist is slightly lacking, especially since the Kerberoi cant hound you into the living world, so as soon as you're back up, you're rather safe. </div> </div> </div>Most current Geist antagonists are more or less eldritch evils. I mean, the Kerberoi are... sort of like that? I mean, some of the fluff makes them out to be just mayor-sheriffs, other fluff makes them out to have a grudge against Sin-eaters.<br /> <br /> That said, the Kerberoi can hound you. The Judges of Yama can drag you back to the Underworld to Lowgate, for instance. The Kerberoi themselves can't, but they have agents.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-11T12:09:42-07:00","id":254509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=254487#post254487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There-in lies the rub: You can't design a setting and say &quot;as long as no one's apathetic, it'll be fine&quot;, because there's no reason NOT to be apathetic. Geist <i>needs</i> reasons, but it doesn't currently support any.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why I called my half written draft the &quot;Geist Chronicles&quot;; your Bound partner seemed like the best place to get that reason.<br /> <br /> (Besides; Sin-Eaters have a ton of reasons to be apathetic, if you define apathy as: 1) use powers to become rich; 2) enjoy spending money; 3) die with dignity)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T03:04:44-07:00","id":255152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=254509#post254509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why I called my half written draft the &quot;Geist Chronicles&quot;; your Bound partner seemed like the best place to get that reason.<br /> <br /> (Besides; Sin-Eaters have a ton of reasons to be apathetic, if you define apathy as: 1) use powers to become rich; 2) enjoy spending money; 3) die with dignity)</div> </div> </div> </div> Well that kind of apathy sounds like the geist game is Profit, Hustle, or maybe Dallas with ghosts, none of those strikes me as horribly inappropriate for a nwod game. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T08:25:07-07:00","id":255330,"title":"","content":"I shut up about this but I think it needs to be restated: as TKR just pointed out, the Geist is you're best tool for fighting apathetic douche bag character concepts. They can act as an antagonist to push your characters to do what you (as a storyteller) want them to care about.<br /> <br /> <i>Hey, look, a ghostly serial killer! I don't care. Gonna go get drunk!</i> - says the player.<br /> <br /> <i>Ah, but your Geist is pretty pissed off by the whole ordeal. Kind of hard to enjoy your party with an angry Geist that you can't tune out in your ear... - </i>you reply, grinning.<br /> <br /> Edit: and to the people who reply and complain that they don't want Geists to be the antagonists of the story: not all antagonists are bad guys, or the bad guy. They're just the characters who make trouble for the protagonist. The landlord who wants to be paid by your broke hero is an antagonist, even though your story is based around your hero fighting to get paid by his cheapskate boss and the landlord is perfectly in the right. Basically, anyone who forces the protagonist to do something is an antagonist, if not a major one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","user":"Oddness","date":". 09-12-2014, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T11:35:20-07:00","id":255428,"title":"","content":"I did intentionally design the rules so that a Sin-Eater who's best buds with his Geist, a heroic Sin-Eater who's keeping an evil ghost locked up in their soul with pure willpower, and a heroic Sin-Eater who uses the metaphorical ability to dig up the dead to keep their evil Geist down are all valid charachter concepts.<br /> <br /> I kinda wish I'd get my inspiration back, I like what I worked on so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 09-12-2014, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T12:30:37-07:00","id":255495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=255330#post255330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I shut up about this but I think it needs to be restated: as TKR just pointed out, the Geist is you're best tool for fighting apathetic douche bag character concepts. They can act as an antagonist to push your characters to do what you (as a storyteller) want them to care about.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that <i>at the moment</i> the Geist itself a) has no reason to care either, and b) has no actual effect on you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-12T12:39:50-07:00","id":255502,"title":"","content":"a) I disagree most strongly. A Geist is an evolved form of a Ghost. Ghosts <i>always</i> have a reason to care, that's why they didn't Pass On.<br /> b) Give it one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T05:16:17-07:00","id":255966,"title":"","content":"The problem is that a Geist's reason to stick around doesn't have to have anything to do with ghosts. In fact, most often a ghost sticks around not because it has anything to do with other ghosts, but out of revenge or greed or simple fear of the unknown and what comes Next. Geists don't really seem to have reasons <i>for dealing with ghosts</i>. Just for not passing on.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=255502#post255502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">b) Give it one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah, but then you get into houseruling and homebrewing. I mean, I linked that &quot;Geist can take you over&quot; chart earlier in the thread. but that's not in the book, that's just me giving the Geist a way to actually effect the player characters for ignoring them. That's one of the things they need in the new edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T06:33:56-07:00","id":257240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=255966#post255966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is that a Geist's reason to stick around doesn't have to have anything to do with ghosts. In fact, most often a ghost sticks around not because it has anything to do with other ghosts, but out of revenge or greed or simple fear of the unknown and what comes Next. Geists don't really seem to have reasons <i>for dealing with ghosts</i>. Just for not passing on.<br /> <br /> Well yeah, but then you get into houseruling and homebrewing. I mean, I linked that &quot;Geist can take you over&quot; chart earlier in the thread. but that's not in the book, that's just me giving the Geist a way to actually effect the player characters for ignoring them. That's one of the things they need in the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you tell a player that his bound Geist is in his ear trying to get him to investigate the strange newcomer because something about her feels off and familiar to the Geist, and the player chooses to ignore the geist (who's hounding him day and night with this) - that player is no longer roleplaying. So start giving him degeneration roles (or lost synergy if that's not the term for it in Geist) to reflect him losing touch with his Geist.<br /> <br /> Bam. In the rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-15T22:08:04-07:00","id":257871,"title":"","content":"Considering Sin-Eaters are empowered by their Virtues, I think that the Empyrean would be a great out-of-context antagonistic force with these lower depth &quot;Angels&quot; being both territory and predator motivated to antagonize Sin-Eaters with the added of bonus of having the same or similar package of the Inferno so the generic ghost stories have a &quot;twist&quot;.<br /> <br /> or maybe the lower depths in general considering the ties to the &quot;deep below&quot; of the Underworld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T05:45:22-07:00","id":258061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoeMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=257871#post257871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering Sin-Eaters are empowered by their Virtues, I think that the Empyrean would be a great out-of-context antagonistic force with these lower depth &quot;Angels&quot; being both territory and predator motivated to antagonize Sin-Eaters with the added of bonus of having the same or similar package of the Inferno so the generic ghost stories have a &quot;twist&quot;.<br /> <br /> or maybe the lower depths in general considering the ties to the &quot;deep below&quot; of the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>How are Sin-Eaters empowered by their Virtues? Not as far as I remember.<br /> That said, I actually run with a simmilar concept for my own Geist chronicle. I use both the Empyrean and Inferno as NPC's, with both being a sort of &quot;crooked mirror&quot; version of Sin-Eaters with their respective Posessed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-16T13:57:29-07:00","id":258439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=258061#post258061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How are Sin-Eaters empowered by their Virtues? Not as far as I remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am referring to the fact that fulfilling their Virtues through their archetype fills up their plasm completely while their Vice only gives them one plasm.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now that I think about it they should have their Virtue shtick expanded and explored a bit more because it kinda feels a bit gimmicky to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","user":"DoeMan","date":". 09-16-2014, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-17T03:05:01-07:00","id":258889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DoeMan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=258439#post258439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am referring to the fact that fulfilling their Virtues through their archetype fills up their plasm completely while their Vice only gives them one plasm.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Now that I think about it they should have their Virtue shtick expanded and explored a bit more because it kinda feels a bit gimmicky to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would prefer to have it thrown out of the window, rather than expanded, actually. I much prefer something along the lines of giving the Geist a Vice and a Virtue, and have those give the Sin-Eater plasm when fulfilled..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T06:09:47-07:00","id":259709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=255428#post255428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did intentionally design the rules so that a Sin-Eater who's best buds with his Geist, a heroic Sin-Eater who's keeping an evil ghost locked up in their soul with pure willpower, and a heroic Sin-Eater who uses the metaphorical ability to dig up the dead to keep their evil Geist down are all valid charachter concepts.<br /> <br /> I kinda wish I'd get my inspiration back, I like what I worked on so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds really interesting, actually. Have you considered posting what you have so far?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T10:12:38-07:00","id":259826,"title":"","content":"Why not? I'll post the rules for Conflicts of Minds and if people seem interested I'll post more stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-18T15:49:52-07:00","id":260162,"title":"","content":"I've actually got an idea kicking around (inspired by a post here) that Geists give their Sin-eater a Passion, and that Passion is essentially a recurring Aspiration, the fulfillment of which grants both Plasm and venue specific beats.<br /> <br /> I need to work on it a bit more. I have a lot of homebrew stuff kicking around to the point that I should probably start making threads for it and link it in my signature like The Kings Raven. I also flit from one project to the other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=257240#post257240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you tell a player that his bound Geist is in his ear trying to get him to investigate the strange newcomer because something about her feels off and familiar to the Geist, and the player chooses to ignore the geist (who's hounding him day and night with this) - that player is no longer roleplaying. So start giving him degeneration roles (or lost synergy if that's not the term for it in Geist) to reflect him losing touch with his Geist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Roleplaying ignoring something is still roleplaying. You also don't lose Synergy for not doing what your Geist wants. It's also important to note that Geists themselves don't even have a reason to care about the strange newcomer.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T03:50:24-07:00","id":260489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=260162#post260162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Roleplaying ignoring something is still roleplaying ... It's also important to note that Geists themselves don't even have a reason to care about the strange newcomer.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Good points. Aren't a Geists Anchors/Influences usually over specific kinds of death, though? They might be motivated by similarities in how the ghost died.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You also don't lose Synergy for not doing what your Geist wants. </div> </div> </div>Why not? Surely that's not going to bring you <i>closer</i> together, after all - quite the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-19-2014, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-19T06:45:15-07:00","id":260581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=260162#post260162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Roleplaying ignoring something is still roleplaying. You also don't lose Synergy for not doing what your Geist wants. It's also important to note that Geists themselves don't even have a reason to care about the strange newcomer.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I was more refferring to the idea of a player saying 'oh, that thing my Geist wants? I ignore it' when the Geist is harping about it constantly is kind of like saying 'oh, that need to eat thing I do to survive? I ignore it' - at a certain point it stops being a request and starts becoming a drive, a need in order to get some peace and quiet. This isn't your little brother asking for candy here, this is a voice in your head going 24/7 - there's only so much you can ignore it before it starts making it hard to focus.<br /> <br /> As for not losing synergy for not doing what your Geist wants: I thought that was the exact intention. It's a measure of how well you get along with your Geist. Most synergy degeneration rolls are for doing things that go against the nature of your Geist - just like a mortal degeneration roll are for doing things (or seeing things) that go against the assumed moral nature of humans.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, I don't think it should be for just anything: maybe have a Geist become obsessed with protecting children and have Synergy loses for if their character were to find out that a child they ignored was hurt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-20T17:46:04-07:00","id":261617,"title":"","content":"Here's a bullet list of what I want from a Geist Chronicle book/ Geist NWoD 2nd ed.<br /> - 9 Manifestations, with one based off each stat. If your gonna do powers based off stats and hit seven of them, you might as well hit the other two.<br /> - Archetypes and Thresholds having more game rules associated with them, beyond just roleplaying cues. Threshold gives you A Key. I'd like your achetype choice and threshold to do things like give you favored skills or attributes, keys, favored Manifestations, and a unique power and weakness. <br /> - More done with the concepts of the dead Grande Krewes, perhaps something analogous to Mage Legacies, Vampire Bloodlines, and/or Promethean Athanors.<br /> - More detail in the Antagonist chapters. Actual details on Chthonians, more details on Abmortals and Sacrosanct. <br /> - THE ANTAGONISTS TO BE WRITTEN USING THE FINAL RULES SUCH THAT THEIR STAT BLOCKS MAKE SENSE AND CAN BE USED IN THE GAME (lol teh kerberoi can haz up to 5 dots of keys in three different keys KEYS DON'T HAVE DOT RATINGS RABBLE RABBLE RABBLE)<br /> - A players Guide with additional options.<br /> - A Storytellers Guide with expanded rules for antagonists and setting secrets.<br /> - Actual rules for tier 2 and 3 Krewes. Actual rules for Tier 3 Krewe Benefits. Some Examples. <br /> - At least three support books beyond PG and StG, one focusing on the Underworld (a better version of WOD:Book of the Dead an actually imprinted as a Geist book), one focusing on a major antagonist group (I don't care which one, just a full book on a major antagonist category like Sacrosanct or Abmortals) and a third book that just expands some aspect of the game, like a guide to Krewes, or a Setting Book (Pick a city, I don't know, have we used Boston? How about Miami? Whatever).<br /> - Did I mention having the rules set be consistent through out the entire book?<br /> - Manifestations that are useful for the Social Maneuvering rules. Like the Passion Key. Passion Shroud and Passion Caul offering various protections from social attacks, Passion Rage not dealing damage but breaking down doors like Hard Leverage on steroids. <br /> - Mementos to get close to the same level of treatment as Gadgets in Demon (especially in the Players Guide).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T16:49:46-07:00","id":262542,"title":"","content":"Dude, I think you might want to get the revised book. They fixed a lot of the stuff you're caps locking.<br /> <br /> Also, we're talking about one book. You're asking for a line of books as your request for this one book. In the same breath as complaining about how the Geist book didn't make sense. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T17:11:35-07:00","id":262551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=262542#post262542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dude, I think you might want to get the revised book. They fixed a lot of the stuff you're caps locking.<br /> <br /> Also, we're talking about one book. You're asking for a line of books as your request for this one book. In the same breath as complaining about how the Geist book didn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, some of these want-to-sees amount to &quot;the 2e version of the game is a 2e version of the game.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T17:20:55-07:00","id":262554,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;What would you want to see in a Sin-eater Chronicle book?&quot;</span></b><br /><br /> A more coherent game line to start. Giest (ironically) up and died during the drought that we were in and suffered the most from the lack of new info on overall antagonists, organizations, and overall structure.<br /> <br /> Out of all the game lines, Giest is the one that need a complete overhaul the most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-21T19:58:57-07:00","id":262610,"title":"","content":"I don't think I'll ever get ot writing the full logic post I wanted, and it's less relevant now, so allow me to say the the greatest story catalyst of Geist is,well, Death.<br /> <br /> The reason I proposed the Horsemen Chronicles instead of the Death Chronicles is because, well, let's be honest, the first sounds cooler and creates the illusion that it's something you can actually really fight it, which is the balance beam Sin-Eaters walk on-they all know they will die, they did it once, but in one way or another they can fight against that fact. They won't win, but they'll produce many important victories in their loss, and those are more important anyway.<br /> <br /> That and, iconically, the Horsemen are the greatest symbols of death, bar none.[/biasspeaking]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T20:47:14-07:00","id":263370,"title":"","content":"Man, I need to post more often. I also need to go back to working on my Geist fan rewrite.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=260489#post260489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good points. Aren't a Geists Anchors/Influences usually over specific kinds of death, though? They might be motivated by similarities in how the ghost died.<br /> Why not? Surely that's not going to bring you <i>closer</i> together, after all - quite the opposite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Geists don't actually HAVE Anchors or Influences. There's really barely a bit of lip service paid to &quot;they represent a specific kind of death&quot;. And Synergy doesn't actually measure your connection with the Geist, it just claims to. It really measures how much you cleave to your new Underworld-centric morality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=260581#post260581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was more refferring to the idea of a player saying 'oh, that thing my Geist wants? I ignore it' when the Geist is harping about it constantly is kind of like saying 'oh, that need to eat thing I do to survive? I ignore it' - at a certain point it stops being a request and starts becoming a drive, a need in order to get some peace and quiet. This isn't your little brother asking for candy here, this is a voice in your head going 24/7 - there's only so much you can ignore it before it starts making it hard to focus.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, but that's the problem; ignoring food has game play consequences. Ignoring the Geist doesn't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for not losing synergy for not doing what your Geist wants: I thought that was the exact intention. It's a measure of how well you get along with your Geist. Most synergy degeneration rolls are for doing things that go against the nature of your Geist - just like a mortal degeneration roll are for doing things (or seeing things) that go against the assumed moral nature of humans </div> </div> </div> Synergy is going against your new Underworld centric morality. If your Geist is crazypants and thinks that eating ghosts will make it stronger and that's it's obsession? Well too bad, you become crazy, lose Synergy, and the Geist takes over all because you did what the Geist wanted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=262551#post262551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, some of these want-to-sees amount to &quot;the 2e version of the game is a 2e version of the game.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yeah... what else would they be?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=262554#post262554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of all the game lines, Giest is the one that need a complete overhaul the most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Signed so hard my pen breaks through the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T20:52:38-07:00","id":263374,"title":"","content":"Also, speaking of, I don't know if I've posted it, but <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/vz1xlbpv83mfb88/Geist_House_Rules_Overview.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">my houserules so far</a>, and a half finished <a href=\"http://www.mediafire.com/view/g777mige3tw1rpg/Geist_Update.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;fan errata&quot;</a>. I'm not very through with them, though. I keep thinking of new things to add, and organization isn't exactly my strong suit (plus I lost the originals and need to rewrite it). Every time I read <i>Geist</i> I come up with something new that just bugs me. It was something about Angelo Moralez last time...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T21:12:35-07:00","id":263383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=263370#post263370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yeah... what else would they be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something that <i>is not necessarily guaranteed to happen by the nature of the project.</i><br /> <br /> If the essence of your requested adjustment is a tautological description of the baseline result, it can go without saying, much like how I can order a hamburger - the meal known more fully as a hamburger sandwich - without having to specify that I would like my hamburger to be a sandwich.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-22T21:28:43-07:00","id":263411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=263370#post263370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geists don't actually HAVE Anchors or Influences. There's really barely a bit of lip service paid to &quot;they represent a specific kind of death&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're confused, which is understandable.<br /> <br /> Writers (mostly Dave) have discussed on prior occasions on the forums the way that Geist's notable ephemeral beings are tentatively modeled in the 2e system now that the ghost rules aren't a skeleton of a skeleton papered over with kludges. Part of that is that Kerberoi and Geister are modeled as higher-Ranking ghosts whose Influences are based on their Dominions (for the former) and particular forms of death like Death By Fire (for the latter), largely replacing the Influences that ghosts draw upon to manifest via the Anchor tag.<br /> <br /> That, and the basic common sense extrapolation from 2e giving ghosts Influences into what is already known about Geist's metaphysics, is what people are talking about when they refer to these aspects of the system.<br /> <br /> Also, our differences aside, I really must implore you to ease back from approaching the game as a mine of what-can-I-find-that-bugs-me-and-where-do-the-mechanics-contradict. It's not terribly productive or conducive to developing a feel for what the intended baseline milieu of the setting is, which is where 2e is liable to aim for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T02:34:07-07:00","id":263551,"title":"","content":"I personally would really, really like there to be powers that your <i>Geist</i> can use but <i>you</i> can't. Seriously, that should be a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=263370#post263370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Geists don't actually HAVE Anchors or Influences. There's really barely a bit of lip service paid to &quot;they represent a specific kind of death&quot;. And Synergy doesn't actually measure your connection with the Geist, it just claims to. It really measures how much you cleave to your new Underworld-centric morality.<br /> <br /> Yeah, but that's the problem; ignoring food has game play consequences. Ignoring the Geist doesn't.<br /> <br /> Synergy is going against your new Underworld centric morality. If your Geist is crazypants and thinks that eating ghosts will make it stronger and that's it's obsession? Well too bad, you become crazy, lose Synergy, and the Geist takes over all because you did what the Geist wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know, these are actually good points. It might seem obvious, but: <b>give Geist motivations mechanical representation.</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 09-23-2014, 05:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T06:19:54-07:00","id":263699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=263370#post263370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but that's the problem; ignoring food has game play consequences. Ignoring the Geist doesn't.<br /> <br /> Synergy is going against your new Underworld centric morality. If your Geist is crazypants and thinks that eating ghosts will make it stronger and that's it's obsession? Well too bad, you become crazy, lose Synergy, and the Geist takes over all because you did what the Geist wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is where we disagree, and it's the crux of what's upsetting you. I think you're getting too wrapped up in the examples of breaking points and not in the actual description of synergy.<br /> <br /> Imagine you are forced to share your body with a man from a lost tribe that has never seen society. Suddenly you have two very different (alien if you will) viewpoints of the world. Imagine you can't communicate with him very well but he's in control of the body... and he's thirsty. He's thirsty and there's fresh, clear water in the room down the hall. You tell him not to drink that water but have a hard time explaining why. See, he's never heard of a toilet before.<br /> <br /> To him, not drinking out of the toilet is some weird abstract morality that the civilized world brought on: to you it's just a disgusting act that makes your stomach turn. This is what synergy seems to be meant to represent and why we have the suggested breaking points we do. Your example of a crazy pants ghost that wants to eat ghosts is actually the exception to the rule: I'd argue that Geist would either not be against eating ghosts (and would therefore not have that breaking point - like a vampire doesn't have a breaking point for sucking blood) or else would trigger that breaking point because he blames his host for allowing him to commit such a disgusting act.<br /> <br /> Either way, if you stop thinking of it as a hard and fast morality rule and start thinking of it as 'how well your mind is tuned with the Geists', the rest of the book makes a lot more sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Holy hell. I looked it up to make sure I'm not off base. Page 83, first line: &quot;Synergy is not a moral code. It is a measure of how unified a sin-eater is with his geist&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1085,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","user":"Oddness","date":". 09-23-2014, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T13:07:34-07:00","id":264752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=263699#post263699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is where we disagree, and it's the crux of what's upsetting you. I think you're getting too wrapped up in the examples of breaking points and not in the actual description of synergy.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, Geist was pre-GMC. Which means &quot;eats ghosts&quot; is a universal rule for all Synergy and not something that only applies to some Geists but not Ghostmuncher mc Hungry.<br /> <br /> That's a flaw that needs to be corrected. Synergy <i>should</i> just be about how in tune you are with your Geist.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T17:35:51-07:00","id":265025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=263411#post263411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're confused, which is understandable.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's understandable because it's never been mentioned anywhere? Most of what I'm talking about is addressing problems that Geist <i>has</i>. Not potential solutions. Acting as if there are solutions already isn't really helpful when there aren't. While it might make sense for Geists to be represented in 2e as having Influences, currently they don't. Which is what we should be talking about. As King's Raven just said: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=264752#post264752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's a flaw that needs to be corrected. Synergy <i>should</i> just be about how in tune you are with your Geist.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=263551#post263551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, these are actually good points. It might seem obvious, but: <b>give Geist motivations mechanical representation.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>This is without a doubt the thing I love about <i>Blood &amp; Smoke</i>. There's a lot of ludonarrative weight in something as simple as a Keystone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=263699#post263699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is where we disagree, and it's the crux of what's upsetting you. I think you're getting too wrapped up in the examples of breaking points and not in the actual description of synergy.<br /> Either way, if you stop thinking of it as a hard and fast morality rule and start thinking of it as 'how well your mind is tuned with the Geists', the rest of the book makes a lot more sense.<br /> EDIT: Holy hell. I looked it up to make sure I'm not off base. Page 83, first line: &quot;Synergy is not a moral code. It is a measure of how unified a sin-eater is with his geist&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the problem. What Synergy <i>actually</i> represents and what it <i>claims</i> to represent are two vastly different things. It claims to be about unity and togetherness with your Geist, the symbiosis that you both share. But in reality all it measures is your death focused belief system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T08:01:57-07:00","id":265474,"title":"","content":"Look, if you're going to throw extreme cases at the system until you break it and then complain that its horribly broken, you're going to break every single system. The problems you're pointing out aren't arguably the Sin-Eaters ruleset fault because it quickly becomes negligible when you use a god machine reading. So what if a crazy ghost eating geist breaks the synergy system - a serial killer PC breaks the morality system the same way. You know how you deal with that problem? You don't allow serial killer PCs. <br /> <br /> Specifically, the undeniable intention of Synergy is to be a measure of how well you're able to get along with the strange alien personality that now shares your body. The breaking points you take offense to are meant to represent things it (the vast majority of geists) finds abhorrent - eating ghosts and generally not living. If you want a Geist that wants to do things that Geists normally find abhorrent, you're attempting to play the equivalent to a mass murderer mortal. Before GM, your response to ideas that wouldn't be represented by the rules as written because the authors hadn't considered them would be to reinterpret the rules and try to keep the original intentions in mind. Not to throw the books down in disgust and move on.<br /> <br /> But here's what's really upsetting me about this argument: you're presenting these edge cases as if they are front and center in every game and make Geist unplayable - which simply isn't true. If you demand that everyone use your rigid interpretation of the system to prove your argument, you're sabotaging the argument. By definition the new chronicle book will reinterpret the rules with a god-machine philosophy in mind and, like integrity, synergy will become a bit more flexible to accommodate for the crazy edge cases that storytellers wont want to allow most of the time anyways. I'm sure everyone agrees that the god machine rule set vastly improves the existing rules and, while it may not perfect them, it'll likely make all the systems more streamlined. <br /> <br /> So lets focus on things a new chronicle book wouldn't by definition fix - things like how we'd like Krewes to change, or the overall ambiguous nature of a lot of the npcs in Geist. What do we actually love about Geist and what could use some looking at that isn't explicitly going to be fixed by the new ruleset? What constructive criticism can we give to whitewolf to improve on Geist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T23:05:38-07:00","id":265983,"title":"","content":"Let's keep it polite guys. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T23:15:01-07:00","id":265989,"title":"","content":"In the spirit of the thing, some foundational bits of hope:<br /> <br /> That the state of the Underworld's overarching nature be made more clear - the focus on subterranean visuals tends to lead the mind away from the more unusual vistas like those Book of the Dead mentions (dense dead woods, flame-spewing metal <i>Doom</i> corridors, narrow bridges that drop into a seemingly bottomless abyss, etc.) - basically, emphasis on the Underworld as <i>the Big Black</i> over the Literal Giant Cave Network; it leaves space for things to happen in, further justifies the general shallowness of charted maps, allows for some ambiguity in mapping the borders of the Dead Dominions, and hooks nicely into the bit from Vampire's <i>Mythologies</i> about how there might be <i>several</i> Underworlds.<br /> <br /> That the ways in which ghosts can advance in Rank within the Underworld receive some attention, factoring as those things are likely to into things like powerful geister representing multiple types of death and the metric by which ghosts might be drawn deeper into the dark now that age is no longer the primary measurement of ghostly potency.<br /> <br /> That the Kerberoi receive a consistent portrayal in terms of role and cognizance that makes it clear their proxy-agency in the sunlit lands is a thing that happens with something resembling notable frequency and builds on the trend loosely set by the Triptych and the Clockwork Hive of the Dominions as creatures who -with some regularity - develop an agenda above and beyond the scope of their duties as the executive branch of their slice of Tartarus over time. (Things like the fate of the Scissorman or the story seed from Glimpses of the Unknown about Kerberoi going to war and what this means for the victor are also worth some focus, I think.)<br /> <br /> That ghostly Twilight be properly outfitted with inanimate elements besides particularly morose specters - the unquiet dead have a handicap on the amount of evocative imagery that can be brought to bear in their slice of Twilight thanks to the Rank-hobble, so things that aren't there in the solid half of the land of the living deserve some emphasis, particularly if this can be made to tie into the way lost places and objects sometimes find their way into the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-26-2014, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T23:30:42-07:00","id":265999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=265989#post265989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That the Kerberoi receive a consistent portrayal in terms of role and cognizance that makes it clear their proxy-agency in the sunlit lands is a thing that happens with something resembling notable frequency</div> </div> </div> </div> I want the opposite. I want Kerberoi to be almost literal extensions of the Old Laws.<br /> <br /> Now I do want underworld beasties who have proxies and plans involving the living world; just not the Kerberoi. Powerful Ghosts, Geists, and stranger things.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-26T18:10:25-07:00","id":266539,"title":"","content":"There are a few things I'd like to see a little different in Geist, though I find the game as is more or less just fine (I'll touch on the big Synergy debate here at the end of my post)...<br /> One thing fluff-wise is to reverse the power where a Sin-Eater can see a person's age... I'd like to have it as a kind of timer hanging over people's heads where a Sin-Eater can literally see when that person is due to die. I think you could do alot with that power and there could be some tie-in to the God-Machine's Infrastructural plans... Imagine this: You as a Sin-Eater spot a person who has about a minute left on the clock... They walk out into the road and a car is gonna slam into them when all of a sudden they get saved by somebody (its a Demon or an Angel due to Fall, but you probably don't know that) and all of a sudden, their clock boosts a couple of years before counting down again... Thats a story arc right there as this is likely something that you've never seen before.<br /> <br /> I think the Pass-On ceremony should be an inate ability also... It seems to me (YMMV of course) that it's pretty much a compulsory buy unless your Archetype is more focused on dealing with the living, such as the Celebrants or the Pilgrims.<br /> <br /> Synergy: My take is this is how united you are with your Geist. The Geist is an unknowable near eldritch abomination despite it's origins... It has a weird link with death and aside from it's clear Influences and what it wants from their Bound host (need a better word than 'host', as the two are basically joined by the soul and the Bound has general control, it doesn't fit in my minds eye for the relationship the pair have) some things will likely erk it. Destroying Fetters (remember in G-M rules ghosts possess via fetters now) is a sin against Synergy 7... Generally messing up the natural order of death or trying to renege from The Deal drops Synergy. Synergy dropping leads to mental issues and also brings the Geist closer to saying 'To heck with it, I'mma just gonna take you over now'.<br /> <br /> The Geist isn't there to snatch control away though (until it decides enough is enough at Synergy 0 of course...) The Deal is that the Geist is bringing the Sin-Eater back, to feel what life is like and live it. The Core gives examples of Geists wanting to do things people generally wouldn't do and not acting normally... If it came up and was told to live with no viewpoint or reference, it'd likely wreck it's body rather quickly. It seems by the crunch at least perfectly happy to sit back and let the Sin-Eater do their thing, living life for the pair of them. The Sin-Eater also has leverage on the Geist with their Keystone, so it's not immediately gonna mess round with the Sin-Eater until pushed into it when Synergy drops enough. Its only when Synergy is out that the Geist itself reneges on The Deal, even though it can be malicious and ressurrect a Sin-Eater when it promised it wouldn't. The system of Max Synergy dropping along with the point drop could represent the Geist being annoyed at the Sin-Eater ending up dead... The Deal is to live after all...<br /> <br /> Perhaps a rename to something representing the level of patience the Geist currently has with their Sin-Eater would be better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3951,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","user":"wander","date":".  got rid of 'wall of text', making post easier to read 09-27-2014, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T19:30:16-07:00","id":267138,"title":"","content":"After some thought, I've decided what I think would help the Geist books the most. I may do up a houserule document for this...<br /> <br /> I want the Chronicle to be called the Cthonian chronicle - and I want it to detail new rules for building ghosts, Geists and Cthonians - basically a handbook to twilight creatures. Unlike vampire, we don't need a new creature to fear, just a better description of the ones we have.<br /> <br /> To be more specific - something I intend to do for my game is document some abilities that ghosts, Geists and Cthonians might manifest in their twilight forms that they cannot show to the average mortal. I'm going to pull inspiration from Demon in writing these: monstrous forms that will make physical combat with a yellowbones a scary proposition if you have a form in the twilight. I'm thinking things straight out of beetlegeuse - monstrous ghost worms, or deformed creatures with claws instead of hands and eyeballs on stalks. Big ones, fast ones, tough ones - think of Demon's true forms but without any sign of technology.<br /> <br /> Then I'm going to add rules to differentiate a ghost, a Geist and a Cthonian. It'll likely differ based mostly on powerlevels but I'd really like to give a reason why a Geist might actually want to be careful around a particularly old ghost - call it yellowbones and tread lightly. Rules for Geists are a bit easier - they've already got Keys and manifestations to use so their changed physical form will likely mostly be for looks when it comes to combat. Cthonians will be the ones that truly need to be alien - it'll be a challenge to give examples of them without defining them.<br /> <br /> This has actually got me a little excited...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T10:53:24-07:00","id":267528,"title":"","content":"I totally agree if there's anything a Sin-Eater really has to fear, it's a powerful Yellow Bones... Kerberos and Cthonians are something only to worry about when venturing through an Avernian Gate, something a Celebrant or Pilgrim may never really bother to do... Thats the purview of the other Archetypes... But a Yellow Bones bothering the living is something generally every Sin-Eater has reason to go up against and also fear... The G-M rules update states about Rank 3 Ghosts only being possible once they've gone to The Underworld to build their Rank up from 1 or 2... We also know that Ghosts, Spirits and Angels now have 'Avernian Gate' as an option for Manifestation... Its quite possible for a Death Spirit to call up an Avernian Gate and summon up a Yellow Bones...<br /> <br /> My wonder for a Chronicle based round Geist is what jurisdiction the Uratha and the Bound have when Death Spirits cause issues by summoning Yellow Bones through Avernian Gates...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T15:35:42-07:00","id":267728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=267528#post267528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I totally agree if there's anything a Sin-Eater really has to fear, it's a powerful Yellow Bones... Kerberos and Cthonians are something only to worry about when venturing through an Avernian Gate, something a Celebrant or Pilgrim may never really bother to do... Thats the purview of the other Archetypes\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Half the point of the Enforcement Numen was that occasionally you'll find ghosts topside who are there for reasons to do with the weird jurisprudence of the Old Laws rather than personal business relating to the individual shreds of leftover ego that make ghosts stay ghosts.<br /> <br /> The Kerberoi present a complication of &quot;this thing is bigger than two or three mysterious hauntings&quot; that a singular troublesome fugitive doesn't bring to bear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The G-M rules update states about Rank 3 Ghosts only being possible once they've gone to The Underworld to build their Rank up from 1 or 2... We also know that Ghosts, Spirits and Angels now have 'Avernian Gate' as an option for Manifestation... Its quite possible for a Death Spirit to call up an Avernian Gate and summon up a Yellow Bones...<br /> <br /> My wonder for a Chronicle based round Geist is what jurisdiction the Uratha and the Bound have when Death Spirits cause issues by summoning Yellow Bones through Avernian Gates... </div> </div> </div>Anything weaker than a greater Jaggling is still going to have to go poking around extant real-estate or curating the resonance to suit, given that Avernian Gate is an opener of existing gates rather than a ripper of such like Shadow Gateway is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T19:18:43-07:00","id":267837,"title":"","content":"I did not know that, that an Avernian Gate needed to be in the vicinity... The G-M rules only state that the Manifest is only possible in a place 'Resonant with Death', it's pretty unclear on it either opening an existing gate or creating one wholesale, but thats really just my own confusion I guess...<br /> <br /> Whilst I'm in this topic though, I was checking through Synergy and saw one sin is destroying a Ghost, which in the old rules came about if their Corpus was reduced to zero. This flat-out destroyed the ghost, rather than banishing them elsewhere. Now from my reading of the G-M rules for Ghosts, destroying Corpus will discorporate a ghost, but if it still has Essence it will reform later in a safe place (generally an Anchor it holds).<br /> <br /> This makes it harder to destroy a Ghost, as most likely for a Bound to get it out of the way to not reform now, they'd have to bleed it of it's Essence (a task in itself depending on what anchors the ghost might have), which sends it to the Underworld. Of course the Bound could go into the Underworld, chase up the Ghost and destroy it's Corpus there whilst it's drained of Essence. This brings me back to my previous post stating perhaps 'Pass On' should be an inherent ability... As it gives more choice to the PC in permanently getting rid of a troublesome Ghost... I think then destroying a Ghost as generally being something premeditated and harder to do now should be a greater sin against Synergy also.<br /> <br /> Point being, the player can choose whether in the Underworld to send on a ghost peacefully or destroy them Quincey-style rather than them needing to think whether to just leave the ghost be imprisoned until they come back again (ala Batman and the Joker) or wiping them out purely because they do or do not have the 'Pass On' ceremony and deciding whether something drastic needs to be done or not about the ghost. It puts more power to the player and Bound then and I think at least, builds their personality a bit better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T20:00:22-07:00","id":267888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=267837#post267837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did not know that, that an Avernian Gate needed to be in the vicinity... The G-M rules only state that the Manifest is only possible in a place 'Resonant with Death', it's pretty unclear on it either opening an existing gate or creating one wholesale, but thats really just my own confusion I guess\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>From the sidebar in the Manifestation Conditions section: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avernian Gateways</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doorways to the Underworld, also called Avernian gates, exist all over the world but are invisible to all but a handful of psychics. <b>The gateways are in Twilight, made of ghostly ephemera, and appear in places with the Resonant Condition tagged as \u201cDeath\u201d \u2014 anywhere that people die in large numbers or that has a feel of Death about it can house a gate.</b> They remain closed unless they are the nearest gate to a ghost who loses his last Anchor, in which case they open for a turn as his Corpus passes on.</div> </div> </div> </div>From the listing of Manifestation Effects:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Avernian Gateway</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Ghost, angel or death-related spirit only \u2014 Requires Open Condition) By spending three Essence, the entity <b>opens a nearby gateway to the Underworld,</b> and applies the Underworld Gate Condition to the location.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Whilst I'm in this topic though, I was checking through Synergy and saw one sin is destroying a Ghost, which in the old rules came about if their Corpus was reduced to zero. This flat-out destroyed the ghost, rather than banishing them elsewhere. Now from my reading of the G-M rules for Ghosts, destroying Corpus will discorporate a ghost, but if it still has Essence it will reform later in a safe place (generally an Anchor it holds). </div> </div> </div>*cough*:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WoD Core Rulebook, p208, &quot;Ghost Traits&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghosts regenerate Corpus in the same amount of time that mortals heal damage (see p. 175). <b>If a ghost suffers as many points of aggravated damage as it has Corpus dots, the ghost is destroyed.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geist: the Sin-Eaters Core Rulebook, p275, &quot;The Sundered: Ghosts of the Great Below - Systems&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A ghost who loses all Corpus due to bashing or lethal damage acts as if dead \u2014 the ghost \u201cdies\u201d and becomes an unmoving corpse. When a day passes and the ghost regains a point of Corpus, however, it returns to the hollow mockery of life it normally possesses. However, do-ing aggravated damage to the ghost (such as using blessed items, as noted above) can present a far more permanent solution. <b>If the ghost loses all its Corpus to aggravated damage while in the Underworld, the ghost is utterly destroyed. The shade discorporates in a howling fit of anguish. This is akin to murder or manslaughter, however, and is a violation of a Sin Eater\u2019s Synergy 4.</b></div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This makes it harder to destroy a Ghost, as most likely for a Bound to get it out of the way to not reform now, they'd have to bleed it of it's Essence (a task in itself depending on what anchors the ghost might have), which sends it to the Underworld. </div> </div> </div>Given the 2e effects of aggravated damage on ephemeral beings, it's not actually that much harder than it was in 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Point being, the player can choose whether in the Underworld to send on a ghost peacefully or destroy them Quincey-style rather than them needing to think whether to just leave the ghost be imprisoned until they come back again (ala Batman and the Joker) or wiping them out purely because they do or do not have the 'Pass On' ceremony and deciding whether something drastic needs to be done or not about the ghost. It puts more power to the player and Bound then and I think at least, builds their personality a bit better. </div> </div> </div>Psst: Fetters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T06:20:33-07:00","id":268211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=267728#post267728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Half the point of the Enforcement Numen was that occasionally you'll find ghosts topside who are there for reasons to do with the weird jurisprudence of the Old Laws rather than personal business relating to the individual shreds of leftover ego that make ghosts stay ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you expand on this? Are you saying that sometimes a Kerborei or a Cthonian will come topside to deal with something dealing with an old law?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T09:37:16-07:00","id":268303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=268211#post268211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you expand on this? Are you saying that sometimes a Kerborei or a Cthonian will come topside to deal with something dealing with an old law?</div> </div> </div> </div>I am saying that the Kerberoi have had a universal ability to foist a task-based punishment on anyone who breaks the Old Laws via the Enforcement Numen since the corebook, and\u2026<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GtSE Core, p280, &quot;Agents of the Old Laws&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And what happens when a transgressor flees to the living world? The Kerberos cannot leave the depths. They must remain in the Underworld. So how do they get to those who have escaped to the world of the quick? They have agents that operate for them.<br /> <br /> <b>A Kerberos generally prevents ghosts from leaving the Underworld, but on occasions where the ghost\u2019s freedom will serve the Old Laws, the Kerberos might grant that specter a \u201cfree pass\u201d to re-enter the world of the living in order to hunt down escaped transgressors.</b> Similarly, a Kerberos can actually have mortal agents, or even agents among the Sin-Eaters. Those who enter the Underworld and break a law might not discover that their punishment is actually to serve the Kerberos as one of its agents in the living world.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:15:09-07:00","id":268366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *cough*: (snipped) </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but what you quoted was all stuff before the G-M rules update. In 1e, you destroy a ghost by taking out their Corpus, end of. In G-M, if they have Essence left, they just discorporate to reform later. This quote from the G-M rules explains it;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ephemeral entities that lose all Corpus from lethal or aggravated<br /> wounds explode into a burst of ephemera stylized to<br /> their nature. A forest-spirit dies in a hail of rapidly-vanishing pine<br /> needles, while ghosts crumble, screaming, into the ground. <b>The<br /> entity isn\u2019t actually dead, though, unless it has also run out of Essence.</b><br /> <b>If it has even a single Essence point remaining, it reforms<br /> in a safe place (a Conditioned location, usually), hibernating.<br /> Once it has regained Essence points equal to Corpus dots, it<br /> spends an Essence point and reawakens.</b> As the entity can\u2019t act<br /> while hibernating, this means waiting for the one Essence a day<br /> for being in a suitable area to slowly build up to Corpus, and that<br /> more powerful entities take longer to recover from being \u201ckilled.\u201d </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Psst: Fetters. </div> </div> </div>In 2e a Ghost has Fetter as a Manifest, but not all Ghosts have that by default (Ghosts get a Manifest per Rank and their default Twilight Form, it's perfectly possible a Ghost doesn't choose Fetter, especially if it's a Rank 1). A Ghost can't automatically Fetter itself to avoid being banished now (also Fetters, much like Anchors can be taken away) and if a Ghost with the Manifest finds itself without an Anchor (because it's been destroyed or otherwise resolved by the PCs like by abduration for example) then it has nought to Fetter too unless it's uses it's Influences to soup one up for a brief time. When Essence is bled out, it's going to the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Cool about the Kerberos though, I didn't catch that before <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:29:55-07:00","id":268397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=268366#post268366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e a Ghost has Fetter as a Manifest, but not all Ghosts have that by default (Ghosts get a Manifest per Rank and their default Twilight Form, it's perfectly possible a Ghost doesn't choose Fetter, especially if it's a Rank 1). A Ghost can't automatically Fetter itself to avoid being banished now (also Fetters, much like Anchors can be taken away) and if a Ghost with the Manifest finds itself without an Anchor (because it's been destroyed or otherwise resolved by the PCs like by abduration for example) then it has nought to Fetter too unless it's uses it's Influences to soup one up for a brief time. When Essence is bled out, it's going to the Underworld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being that I have a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/71851-unpacking-manifestation-conditions\">thread</a> about the Ephemeral Being rules it can be assumed that I am familiar with how Manifestation Effects work, but that notwithstanding, I'm talking about Fetters as Geist defines the term, i.e. the ghostly equivalent of spirit-fetishes whereby one of the unquiet dead is imprisoned within its anchor in lieu of destroying it or banishing it to the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T11:37:38-07:00","id":268404,"title":"","content":"Ah, I see <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I never meant to say you didn't know how the rules worked, it just seemed you ignored my statement about how getting rid of Corpus doesn't insta-destroy a Ghost anymore (if it still has Essence).<br /> <br /> Back On-Topic; I think with Ghost rules slightly changed, that should have a knock-on effect with the rules for the Bound and how ghosts can be dealt with and also an updated look at Synergy sins... Perhaps with creating Bound version-Fetters as one?<br /> <br /> Edit: I came away from this wondering why I've never had the option to bind Ghosts to a Fetter myself in-play outside of buying a Fetter ready-made as a Merit and I realised the Ceremony for it is a 5-dot version... Which makes binding a ghost into a Fetter a lesser done thing generally than making a ghost pass on... I find it strange there are options to deal with ghosts but whilst the fluff speaks as if you can do all this as a Bound, its all stuff that fills in the limited dots you get for Merits or the few dots you can get some Manifestations for... If anything I come away from this thinking new Bound are underpowered compared to how they're described in the fluff...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3951,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","user":"wander","date":". 09-29-2014, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T12:26:30-07:00","id":268460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=268404#post268404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I never meant to say you didn't know how the rules worked, it just seemed you ignored my statement about how getting rid of Corpus doesn't insta-destroy a Ghost anymore (if it still has Essence).</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's just that \u2014<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GMC Rules Revisions, Ephemeral Beings, &quot;Combat&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ephemeral beings record and heal from wounds the same way as material characters, but in addition <b>lose one point of Essence for every aggravated wound they suffer.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Ephemeral entities that lose all Corpus from lethal</b> or aggravated <b>wounds </b><b>explode into a burst of ephemera stylized to their nature.</b> A forest-spirit dies in a hail of rapidly-vanishing pine needles, while ghosts crumble, screaming, into the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u2014 it is still <i>dramatically</i> easier to destroy a ghost with a source of aggravated damage like a blessed item or a bane than it is to &quot;just&quot; beat the thing into nonexistence, particularly now that ghosts are subject to daily-level Essence-bleed and use Essence rather than Willpower to manifest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T11:16:10-07:00","id":269300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Avernian gates = Death resonance </div> </div> </div>Hmm, does this mean you can create an Averian Gate by killing a bunch of people, or making a huge pile of bones or something? And permanently destroy one by cleaning up the area around it?<br /> <br /> (You know, the same way you might exorcise a Spirit by messing around with it's Resonant Condition?)<br /> <br /> It makes sense, but it's a different-seeming way of looking at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T11:26:53-07:00","id":269304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=269300#post269300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, does this mean you can create an Averian Gate by killing a bunch of people, or making a huge pile of bones or something? And permanently destroy one by cleaning up the area around it?<br /> <br /> (You know, the same way you might exorcise a Spirit by messing around with it's Resonant Condition?)<br /> <br /> It makes sense, but it's a different-seeming way of looking at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was allways a part of the system that you could destroy an Avernian Gate by messing with its resonance. The old system didn't explicitly say that that was what happened, but the things you had to do to destroy one, was the equivalent of such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T12:42:48-07:00","id":269349,"title":"","content":"There is also that Ceremony, 'Create Deathly Passage' (ooooo) that allows the Bound to create new pathways to the Underworld at places and this can even reopen defunct Avernian Gates (which shows they can be shut and wiped out)... It still only works when done in a place where the dead have mounted in the past, more than just a place resonant with death (its stated a brand new cemetary won't do, an ancient battlefield where legions of the dead are buried will do fine though). I expect an update of the Ceremony will allow the 'Death Resonant' condition to be placed back on a location if it was previously removed (likely bothering not only other Krewes, but also some Uratha Packs).<br /> <br /> The Ceremony is something not easily done though, it's a five-pointer and it can take a while for the Gate to called up for besides the other components the summoning circle need to achieve.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T19:59:29-07:00","id":269737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=268397#post268397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being that I have a <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/71851-unpacking-manifestation-conditions\">thread</a> about the Ephemeral Being rules it can be assumed that I am familiar with how Manifestation Effects work</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Unless you wrote the book, your musings don't really mean anything other than your own interpretations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T20:42:30-07:00","id":269786,"title":"","content":"The problems with that sort of argument is that it only works if someone in the current discussion <i>did</i> write the book.<br /> <br /> Which none of us did, so it's back to academic peer review.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T20:43:02-07:00","id":269787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=269300#post269300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmm, does this mean you can create an Averian Gate by killing a bunch of people, or making a huge pile of bones or something? And permanently destroy one by cleaning up the area around it?<br /> <br /> (You know, the same way you might exorcise a Spirit by messing around with it's Resonant Condition?)<br /> <br /> It makes sense, but it's a different-seeming way of looking at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the distinct feeling that Avernian Gates function as a kind of lock/autorenew on the Resonant [Death] Condition, though evidently the Condition can still be knocked out from under the Gate to close/un-Open it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T21:16:32-07:00","id":269801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=269786#post269786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problems with that sort of argument is that it only works if someone in the current discussion <i>did</i> write the book.<br /> <br /> Which none of us did, so it's back to academic peer review.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's kind of my point. &quot;I have a thread of my own interpretations so I know quite a bit&quot; doesn't really mean anything.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=269787#post269787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get the distinct feeling that Avernian Gates function as a kind of lock/autorenew on the Resonant [Death] Condition, though evidently the Condition can still be knocked out from under the Gate to close/un-Open it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like that whole section needs a lot more explanation. The fact that it needs a flow chart to explain how things work means that it's got some serious problems. I hope it gets fixed for when we get an actual 2e corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T21:46:01-07:00","id":269831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=269801#post269801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThat's kind of my point. &quot;I have a thread of my own interpretations so I know quite a bit&quot; doesn't really mean anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>It means &quot;I have read and endeavored to understand the intent of the material, particularly in the context of the preceding edition's examples of How Ephemeral Beings Behave, and thus can be assumed to be familiar with the literal content of the section in question&quot; and you are literally derailing your own thread by trying to make this into A Thing. Please refrain.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like that whole section needs a lot more explanation. The fact that it needs a flow chart to explain how things work means that it's got some serious problems. I hope it gets fixed for when we get an actual 2e corebook. </div> </div> </div>It's more that the flowchart was borked, really, which is why it's absent in Demon Core, where the rules appendix saw its first reprint. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/47612-how-do-ephemeral-entity-rules-work?p=47623#post47623\">I covered this </a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/47612-how-do-ephemeral-entity-rules-work?p=47623#post47623\">a while ago</a><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/47612-how-do-ephemeral-entity-rules-work?p=47623#post47623\">, too,</a> I should like to note.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T02:06:17-07:00","id":269976,"title":"","content":"A hypothetical new Geist core would be clearer by virtue of not talking about Spirits or Angels - it'd be just ghosts. Forsaken 2E's equivalent is just spirits.<br /> <br /> I'm interested to see people's eventual reactions to Awakening 2E's ephemeral entities rules - because they have to cover spirits, ghosts, goetia, supernal entities, gulmoth, acamoth, and any bizarre creatures the Storyteller decides to invent in slightly less room than Werewolf gives to spirits, and given that mages don't tend to hold with influencing or adjusting conditions, instead just setting the entity into whichever state they want, (mage's Spirit spells to summon spirits force the spirit into the Manifestation you want, whether it has the ability to do it or not!) they're a lot simpler. No flowchart, because most of the Conditions aren't referenced. Anyone who wants the details of how a spirit might carefully build someone up to being Claimed can get the GMC expansion for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T04:58:32-07:00","id":270063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=269976#post269976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A hypothetical new Geist core would be clearer by virtue of not talking about Spirits or Angels - it'd be just ghosts. Forsaken 2E's equivalent is just spirits.<br /> <br /> I'm interested to see people's eventual reactions to Awakening 2E's ephemeral entities rules - because they have to cover spirits, ghosts, goetia, supernal entities, gulmoth, acamoth, and any bizarre creatures the Storyteller decides to invent in slightly less room than Werewolf gives to spirits, and given that mages don't tend to hold with influencing or adjusting conditions, instead just setting the entity into whichever state they want, (mage's Spirit spells to summon spirits force the spirit into the Manifestation you want, whether it has the ability to do it or not!) they're a lot simpler. No flowchart, because most of the Conditions aren't referenced. Anyone who wants the details of how a spirit might carefully build someone up to being Claimed can get the GMC expansion for free.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would helping a Spirit Claim somebody be a major act of Hubris?<br /> <br /> Because that seems like it'd be a pretty major act of Hubris.<br /> <br /> Since that's Mage stuff though, I'll veer back toward Geist.<br /> <br /> I'm reminded of the Storm Lords stereotype of Sin-Eaters: Claimed by the dead is still Claimed. Something I'd like to see in Geist 2E? Actual rules for being Claimed by Ghosts. I get that that's supposed to be a Spirit thing, but the idea of ghosts powerful enough to physically merge with unwilling mortals sounds like a fun way to get villains. And feels Strix-y. I'm of the opinion that...what was it called, Synthesis?...was basically a Strix Claiming somebody.<br /> <br /> Woo, managed to work the big three and Geist into this post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T05:18:27-07:00","id":270068,"title":"","content":"Satchel; a Rank 1 Ghost could have 7 Corpus and 10 Essence (A Rank 2 could have 8 Corpus and 15 Essence), so it's perfectly possible a Ghost could have their Corpus spent and still have Essence left if they don't discorporate to get away beforehand (max of 3 or 7 beforehand in this case). A rarity as a ghost is likely to use manifests, influences and numen in defence, but it is at least mechanically possible for a ghost to be banished to the Underworld rather than be destroyed by having their Corpus spent. The paragraph you quoted before stating about ghosts deaths from G-M rules update also was one I quoted prior, with my bolding cut off to prove your point more valid. Thats my last say on the matter, I don't want to make a derail.<br /> <br /> *coughs*<br /> <br /> Anyway... On-topic! Yep, I totally see a yellow-bones coming back from the Underworld (It would have to be a Rank 3 Ghost at least to Claim and so they'd have to have 'levelled up' from basic ghost by spending some time in the Underworld) and doing a Claim. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Could easily make a plot out of some horrifying ghost being sent out from a Gate to do that. And inline with the thread, I think seeing a variety of sample ghosts that have interesting uses like a Claiming yellowbones and the difference between Rank 1 shades and Rank 2 communicative ghosts would be nice now the rules have been changed and updated. A bit more info on Avernian Gates apparently wouldn't go amiss either <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T04:56:17-07:00","id":272150,"title":"","content":"Something I'de like to see curbed, is the entire &quot;A Sin-Eater was a quasi-medium prior to the Bargain&quot; aspect. I never liked the fact that all Sin-Eaters had to have had some interaction with Ghosts or Necromantic forces before their eventual death. It seemed rather restrictive and didn't really make much sense, in my opinion. I understand the rationale behind it, but I dont agree that it was a particularily good idea. So thats one thing I'de like to just see quietly slip into the night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T07:40:50-07:00","id":272197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272150#post272150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never liked the fact that all Sin-Eaters had to have had some interaction with Ghosts or Necromantic forces before their eventual death.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking as someone for whom that connection is one of my favorite aspects of SE character creation, saying that &quot;all Sin-Eaters&quot; were such is a resounding falsehood. It's the Bound equivalent of being a &quot;templated&quot; wolf-blood before becoming a werewolf and just as non-guaranteed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T09:17:06-07:00","id":272277,"title":"","content":"The core did make it seem that a Sin-Eater very likely had in some way interacted with the dead in the past that it seemed to be all of them, though of course me saying 'very likely' is of course different from saying 'always'. The wording of this part of the Core could at least go through a bit of revision for more clarification.<br /> I know at least in a brief Geist game I played in which my character was a Mortal beforehand, I had three Merit points in Unseen Sense:Ghosts which were traded to make my Sin-Eater Psyche 2 when they were finally Bound to their Geist. I have also played a Sin-Eater that had no Ceremonies or Psyche boost etc from Merits using just ones from the Blue Books. I sure missed the Pass On Ceremony and I find Merits to be good for getting the Charm Ceremony, some charms to make keys from in-game and being a bit more versatile otherwise, though of course all that depends on the type of character and the concept being played.<br /> To be honest though, unless you are doing such a game where you play a Mortal first it's likely not going to affect the game or your character's background so much and isn't necessary to dwell too much on. It is a good way to explain how a starting character could know this or that about ghosts without the dreaded 'metagaming' accusations coming up.<br /> <br /> Of course some kind of ruling like a special Merit or something that a Mortal who is due to be Bound or a list of suitable Supernatural Merits to give them if playing a game where the Bargain occurs would be a good side-bar to add into the 2e Geist book if someone wanted to go down that road.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T17:16:39-07:00","id":272585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272197#post272197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as someone for whom that connection is one of my favorite aspects of SE character creation, saying that &quot;all Sin-Eaters&quot; were such is a resounding falsehood. It's the Bound equivalent of being a &quot;templated&quot; wolf-blood before becoming a werewolf and just as non-guaranteed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright. I am not religiously opposed to it, so do you care to explain why you feel that its a good idea?<br /> From my point of view, its the equivalent of saying &quot;Your back-story <b>MUST</b> include this element, or else you're doing it!&quot;. Its restrictive, and anything that restricts a player or storytellers creativity is, in my opinion, a blazing mistake. Aparently, you feel differently, although I cannot think why. Do you wish to explain your position?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T18:33:54-07:00","id":272608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272585#post272585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright. I am not religiously opposed to it, so do you care to explain why you feel that its a good idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fun, it ties into the semifatalism and chthonic bleedover that Morbid Reality opens up, it gives a sense of continuity from regular human to sensitive human to Bound to whatever-comes-next (and continues the general trend of supernatural fields drawing characters closer and closer into their orbits with continued exposure), it gives a lot of proto-Bound experience with stuff that makes them look kind of nuts and establishes a potential background from which characters might reasonably learn conventional supernatural secrecy, and it gives you a nice base from which to direct your character's worldview and areas of expertise, which is <i>important</i> in a game where personal stories are such a significant element of in-rules innovation.<br /> <br /> Your turn. What of value is gained by cutting this option off, given that it is specifically an option which is only common enough to be a noticeable trend rather than truly universal?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> From my point of view, its the equivalent of saying <u>&quot;Your back-story <b>MUST</b> include this element, or else you're doing it!&quot;.</u> Its restrictive, and anything that restricts a player or storytellers creativity is, in my opinion, a blazing mistake. Aparently, you feel differently, although I cannot think why. Do you wish to explain your position? </div> </div> </div>My position is that the underlined is blatantly incorrect and that I was perfectly fine with my one pure-Geist game of note having a fifty-fifty split between PCs who had a preestablished connection with death and PCs who didn't.*<br /> <br /> My position is that I'm having goddamn Demon &quot;but I don't WANNA play a robot!&quot; flashbacks and would prefer that this prove not to be a repeat of that unsightly display.<br /> <br /> My position is that I haven't <i>got</i> a position apart from &quot;stop talking nonsense and actually read the books,&quot; as is often the case.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*I opt not to count the character who had a dying dream moments before his Bargain and the character who was repurposed from an abandoned previous game by way of revealing that game to have been a delirious episode brought on by exposure and brain cancer, given that these seem unlikely to meet your criteria; the widowed doctor who stopped being haunted by the wife he died trying to resurrect and the demideathlord's daughter are more in line with what you're talking about, but even those two weren't exactly overt psychics beforehand. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T19:54:39-07:00","id":272677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272608#post272608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fun, it ties into the semifatalism and chthonic bleedover that Morbid Reality opens up, it gives a sense of continuity from regular human to sensitive human to Bound to whatever-comes-next (and continues the general trend of supernatural fields drawing characters closer and closer into their orbits with continued exposure), it gives a lot of proto-Bound experience with stuff that makes them look kind of nuts and establishes a potential background from which characters might reasonably learn conventional supernatural secrecy, and it gives you a nice base from which to direct your character's worldview and areas of expertise, which is <i>important</i> in a game where personal stories are such a significant element of in-rules innovation.<br /> <br /> Your turn. What of value is gained by cutting this option off, given that it is specifically an option which is only common enough to be a noticeable trend rather than truly universal?<br /> <br /> <br /> My position is that the underlined is blatantly incorrect and that I was perfectly fine with my one pure-Geist game of note having a fifty-fifty split between PCs who had a preestablished connection with death and PCs who didn't.*<br /> <br /> My position is that I'm having goddamn Demon &quot;but I don't WANNA play a robot!&quot; flashbacks and would prefer that this prove not to be a repeat of that unsightly display.<br /> <br /> My position is that I haven't <i>got</i> a position apart from &quot;stop talking nonsense and actually read the books,&quot; as is often the case.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*I opt not to count the character who had a dying dream moments before his Bargain and the character who was repurposed from an abandoned previous game by way of revealing that game to have been a delirious episode brought on by exposure and brain cancer, given that these seem unlikely to meet your criteria; the widowed doctor who stopped being haunted by the wife he died trying to resurrect and the demideathlord's daughter are more in line with what you're talking about, but even those two weren't exactly overt psychics beforehand. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is though, equating what I'm saying to to the &quot;I dont wanna play a robot&quot; debate from demon, is incorrect and not comperable at all. I am taking issue with the system trying to dictate the framework of my characters backstory, not the actual game, characters, mechanics or thematics. Demon is further differentiated by the fact that the character was never human to begin with, which would invalidate any issue a player could have with being a robot or former agent of the god machine. I can sorta understand what you think it adds, but I dont agree that what is gained balances what is lost. Ultimately, you only gain a feel of &quot;people slowly become increasingly supernatural by exposure&quot;, a thematic not all storytellers decide to implement, and you lose a hefty chunk of player agency when it comes to creating the backstory you want.<br /> I understand that you can allways choose to overlooked those particular lines - something I mostly do - but I fail to remember any place which specifically says something along the lines &quot;Sin-Eaters-to-be sometimes show latent psychic abillities, but is not allways the case&quot;.<br /> If it does say that somewhere, the fact that I fail to remember it, despite having browsed the Sin-Eater book just a few days ago to prepare for a Geist session, would show the lack of emphasis on it, if nothing else.<br /> <br /> Lastely, telling people to &quot;read the books&quot; are alittle insulting, given the fact that you're either implying I'm of poor memory or too dense to read the material before I speak my mind. This is further aggrevated by the fact that we're not really discussing the old book here. We're discussing my wish for a possible future change/addition to a new book. If I were saying something demonstrably false, your statement would make sense, but this isn't something thats demonstrably false. Its a difference of opinion, which cannot merely be solved by me re-reading the material.<br /> I dont think it was your intention to insult, but I'd be pleased if you would consider what you're implying alittle more carefully in the future.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T21:56:42-07:00","id":272727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272677#post272677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is though, equating what I'm saying to to the &quot;I dont wanna play a robot&quot; debate from demon, is incorrect and not comperable at all. I am taking issue with the system trying to dictate the framework of my characters backstory, not the actual game, characters, mechanics or thematics. Demon is further differentiated by the fact that the character was never human to begin with, which would invalidate any issue a player could have with being a robot or former agent of the god machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's rather a lot to get out of &quot;the thing you are complaining about being forced to do is not a thing that you are being forced to do even without invoking the 'you can do what you want at your table' caveat and your apparently deliberate disregarding of my pointing this out in the name of continuing to make this complaint, as occurred in the specific conversation about Demon to which I am alluding, is frustrating in the extreme.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ultimately, you only gain a feel of &quot;people slowly become increasingly supernatural by exposure&quot;, a thematic not all storytellers decide to implement, and you lose a hefty chunk of player agency when it comes to creating the backstory you want. </div> </div> </div>You lose <i>nothing</i> because <i>it is not a universal quality</i> and <i>you are not required to implement it in any more concrete a sense than &quot;your character's backstory results in your character becoming one of the Bound.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Even if we were to assume it were an absolute quality, the sidebar accompanying the section says that <i>Unseen Sense</i> can suffice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I understand that you can allways choose to overlooked those particular lines - something I mostly do - but I fail to remember any place which specifically says something along the lines &quot;Sin-Eaters-to-be sometimes show latent psychic abillities, but is not allways the case&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Do me a favor, very quickly.<br /> <br /> Go look at the writeups for literally any of the sample SE characters in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Look very carefully.<br /> <br /> Show me, if you can,* where any of them have supernatural powers described in the pre-Bargain portion of their Background sections.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* You cannot, because no such description exists.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it does say that somewhere, the fact that I fail to remember it, despite having browsed the Sin-Eater book just a few days ago to prepare for a Geist session, would show the lack of emphasis on it, if nothing else. </div> </div> </div>I'll here point out with a certain degree of vitriol that you are insisting that I prove a negative and preemptively crowing about lack of emphasis. This is semantically knackered.<br /> <br /> I learned Aristotelian logic a couple years ago; conveniently, the variables used for such are S and P, so let's say S = Sin-eaters and P = former Psychics and sit down for a primer/refresher:<br /> <br /> &quot;All S are P&quot; is what's called an A Statement; in the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Square_of_opposition\" target=\"_blank\">square of opposition</a>, an A Statement is directly incompatible with what are called O Statements, such as &quot;Some S are not P&quot;; if one is true, the other has to be false, as might be gathered by the relationship those two statement-types have being called &quot;contradictory.&quot; Likewise, &quot;Some S are P&quot; - an I Statement - is subaltern to - that is, implied by - the corresponding A Statement. O Statements, as you might guess from the thing being called the <i>square</i> of opposition, are subaltern to corresponding E Statements - &quot;No S are P&quot; - and thus if the universal statement (the one that addresses an entire category instead of a nonzero set of instances) is true, then the particular (the one addressing the aforesaid set of instances) must be true as well, but the particular can be true while the universal is false.<br /> <br /> There's two more relationships besides contradictory and subaltern in the square, and they're nicely symmetrical in what they mean. There's <i>contrary</i>, which is the relationship between corresponding A and E Statements - as could be inferred by universal statements that mean opposite things, &quot;All S are P&quot; and &quot;No S are P&quot; cannot both be true at the same time. (They can both be false - such as if the criterion P is something that can be found in some but not all members of group S.) Their subalternate I and E Statements, meanwhile, are <i>subcontrary</i> - they can both be true, but they can't both be <i>false</i>; the only way this could happen is if you were talking about a set of zero members, which you can't do with particular statements, so if Some S are P is false, then Some S are not P has to be true.<br /> <br /> So let's unpack this:<br /> <br /> It's logically impossible, within the confines of this argument, for All Sin-eaters to be former Psychics <i>and </i>for Some Sin-Eaters to not be former Psychics, but it's possible for Some Sin-eaters to be former Psychics <i>and</i> for Some Sin-eaters to <i>not</i> be former Psychics. (We can extrapolate from pre-release talk about Geist mentioning the involvement of other supernaturals in the gameline, <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/default0bf9.html?g=posts&amp;m=1506124#post1506124\" target=\"_blank\">word-of-writer</a>, and the lack of mention in sample characters and anywhere else in the line that the bit in Chapter One about every Sin-Eater being Born With A Caul is an artifact of an earlier iteration that didn't get through the book's notorious editing rush rather than a Definitely Factual Thing - it's not exactly unprecedented, given the corebook's directly opposed statements on Kerberoi forms.)<br /> <br /> On the other hand, &quot;No Sin-eaters are former Psychics,&quot; if made a true statement as you propose,* means &quot;Some Sin-eaters are former Psychics&quot; <i>cannot</i> be true, since its contradictor is not false, while &quot;Some Sin-eaters are not former Psychics&quot; stands untouched.<br /> <br /> In other words, going from the evidence of one true particular negative statement - the sample Sin-Eater characters provided by the books - and filtering it through the square of opposition, you lose more by adding a universal negative* than by not doing so.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* I'll here note that if you're <i>not</i> proposing that No Sin-eaters are former Psychics, then you've opted to literally argue for absolutely nothing, painted over a core of &quot;I hope that the book is edited in such a manner that we don't have blatant contradictions in setting lore like we did in 1e core.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastely, telling people to &quot;read the books&quot; are alittle insulting, given the fact that you're either implying I'm of poor memory or too dense to read the material before I speak my mind. This is further aggrevated by the fact that we're not really discussing the old book here. We're discussing my wish for a possible future change/addition to a new book. </div> </div> </div>It is my sincere hope that I do not need to explain how &quot;I hope [change that is not a change] is made&quot; is aggravating cruft that I've spent a sizeable portion of my posts in two other more-confirmed gamelines' What-do-you-want-to-see threads snapping more verbose versions of &quot;read the books&quot; at and thus not something I possess especial reserves of patience for.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I dont think it was your intention to insult, but I'd be pleased if you would consider what you're implying a little more carefully in the future. </div> </div> </div>I would be pleased if I didn't have to struggle with communicative difficulties imparting the understanding of authorial intent that I've synthesized for this game from its own books and bluebook mentions, posts by the writers, and inference from the latter-day fluff to people who haven't taken literally weeks and months of their time deliberately processing the material like I have but don't understand how to properly leverage a position of ignorance by actually asking sincere questions.<br /> <br /> That is, ultimately, what I would like to see in a Geist 2e Chronicle book.<br /> <img src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/thothmoreyouknow.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Corrected a miswriting of the logical unpacking. 10-05-2014, 02:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T03:15:51-07:00","id":272821,"title":"","content":"I am done. If you cant - or wont - stop being a condescending prick about this, I am not going to humor you any longer.<br /> If you really get that annoyed with people because they - in your opinion - dont understand the books, you probably need to stop taking this so damn seriously.<br /> <br /> For everyone else: I am sorry I let the thread get derailed like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T05:37:23-07:00","id":272890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272608#post272608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My position is that I haven't <i>got</i> a position apart from &quot;stop talking nonsense and actually read the books,&quot; as is often the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although when I pointed out to you the parts of the book that said every single one of the Bound had a supernatural connection to the forces of death beforehand, you said you had better things to do than reading it.<br /> <br /> <br /> But back on topic...<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel;n265989That the state of the Underworld's overarching nature be made more clear - the focus on subterranean visuals tends to lead the mind away from the more unusual vistas like those Book of the Dead mentions (dense dead woods, flame-spewing metal [I</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doom[/I] corridors, narrow bridges that drop into a seemingly bottomless abyss, etc.) - basically, emphasis on the Underworld as <i>the Big Black</i> over the Literal Giant Cave Network; it leaves space for things to happen in, further justifies the general shallowness of charted maps, allows for some ambiguity in mapping the borders of the Dead Dominions, and hooks nicely into the bit from Vampire's <i>Mythologies</i> about how there might be <i>several</i> Underworlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would favour this as a major difference between the Depths and the Dominions. As in, keep the cave network (with occasional underground lakes, and the twisted underground structures close to the Gates) for the Depths, and go into the alternatives in most of the Dominions, to the point where some Sineaters might see them as more like parallel dimensions accessed via the Depths than all part of the same world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=253852#post253852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other half of this is that the fluff <i>acts</i> as if they care but gives them no reason to do so. Why would krewes fight over territory for the right to... solve crimes and lay ghosts to rest? Why would they bother with Abmortals that aren't serial killers? I mean, the Hungry Exorcist eats ghosts and that's supposed to be super bad, but... why? Why should Sin-eaters care about that?</div> </div> </div> </div>In part they have a built in reason to care because they have a built in connection - it's hard to ignore something that's with you constantly. Though of course, as you say, there's less of a built-in reason as to what reaction their caring will bring. So...<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=253864#post253864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I wouldn't want a clear cut villian like the Abyss in Mage or the Strix in Vampire. Those seem too &quot;Evil for Eldritch unknowable reasons&quot; kinds of evil for Geist. I think the fact that the antagonists in Geist are antagonists wither because you wronged them yourself (Kerberoi, angry Ghosts/Geists) or because you have different political views to them (Sacrosanct, Abmortals).</div> </div> </div> </div>I would assume that Onyx Path intend to make the driving forces somewhat different in each 2e game. In Werewolf we have an out of context problem, in Vampire we have a mix of OCP and black mirror, both Mage and Promethean suggest problems of environment, and &quot;Huntsman Chronicle&quot; implies the Gentry are at the root of it for Changeling.<br /> <br /> So in Geist, what about each other? If there's no built-in &quot;way for Sineaters to be,&quot; what if the big enemy is/are Sineaters (or Geists) trying to impose one? Death has provoked a lot of philosophy, krewes already come with DIY mythologies, and we already have Sacrosanct - the foundations for a chronicle centred on warring ideologies are already laid. The PC's even be part of such an ideology, or just trying to do general Sineating in the cracks between them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 10-05-2014, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T06:49:14-07:00","id":272910,"title":"","content":"Hey guys, I'm with Krob on this (and yeah, I'm guilty too)<br /> <br /> Can we keep the discussion on possible suggestions for expanding Geist and stop trying to change what Geist is? We can yell at each other about the things we like or don't like about it in other threads. Yes, Geist has some problems. Yes, most of those problems are caused by faulty interpretations of the rules - whether or not you're in the right for interpreting the rules that way. It doesn't matter though because that's not what this thread is about. If you're upset about a weakness of the system then start a seperate thread and you can discuss other possible interpretations or houserules to fix the problems there. Posting it here is just derailing or griping and is not helpful.<br /> <br /> So, going further - describe things you'd like expanded on, not how you want the writers to completely rewrite all your pet peeves. I still vote for an expansion of the ghost building rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T08:48:30-07:00","id":272960,"title":"","content":"Yes but, since this will be a 2e book it makes sense that it rewrites the 1e material rather than simply expands upon it. <br /> <br /> Personally, I wouldn't mind if Geist is changed to be more focused on the fact that players are as much ghost as they are human. The main essence is that they're sharing their body with someone or something else. A deeper exploration of that would be useful. I would love some expanded ghost making rules but am less interested sojourning through the Underworld. It seems to me that Geists want something in the real world or they wouldn't have merged with the PC's character. Thus mechanics that are less dependent on sojourning through the Underworld would be more helpful. This was always a fatal flaw in Wraith.<br /> <br /> To that end we must first disassemble, then fix what isn't working, before finally reassembling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T09:43:07-07:00","id":272976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272960#post272960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes but, since this will be a 2e book it makes sense that it rewrites the 1e material rather than simply expands upon it.<br /> <br /> [\u2026]<br /> <br /> To that end we must first disassemble, then fix what isn't working, before finally reassembling.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are not writing the book, is the thing, and thus the task of actually fixing the thing is neither our job nor the purpose of this type of thread.<br /> <br /> &quot;Multiple examples of krewes at each level of organization&quot; and &quot;ways Underworld 'politics' can tie into things that happen in the living world&quot; are within the category of things-we'd-like-to-see. &quot;This thing from 1e sucks&quot; and observations about how Geist's 1e mechanics are broken are not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T17:54:40-07:00","id":273359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One thing fluff-wise is to reverse the power where a Sin-Eater can see a person's age... I'd like to have it as a kind of timer hanging over people's heads where a Sin-Eater can literally see when that person is due to die. I think you could do alot with that power and there could be some tie-in to the God-Machine's Infrastructural plans... Imagine this: You as a Sin-Eater spot a person who has about a minute left on the clock... They walk out into the road and a car is gonna slam into them when all of a sudden they get saved by somebody (its a Demon or an Angel due to Fall, but you probably don't know that) and all of a sudden, their clock boosts a couple of years before counting down again... Thats a story arc right there as this is likely something that you've never seen before.<br /> <br /> I think the Pass-On ceremony should be an inate ability also... It seems to me (YMMV of course) that it's pretty much a compulsory buy unless your Archetype is more focused on dealing with the living, such as the Celebrants or the Pilgrims. </div> </div> </div>This from my message back on p.9 I am sure got lost in the debates and is what I'd like to see in Geist 2e. I think powering up the Geist and Book of the Dead Merits to warrant a player wanting to pick them up over the ones in the GMC rules (outside of a Bound likely getting 10 Merit Points for being a supernatural now) would be cool. I sure would like my Bound to have a few charms on them and some cool ceremonies without me wondering if I shoulda took some GMC rules Merits instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T07:20:13-07:00","id":273786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272910#post272910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, going further - describe things you'd like expanded on, not how you want the writers to completely rewrite all your pet peeves. I still vote for an expansion of the ghost building rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>There isn't much I want expanded per se. Stuff cleaned up, sure, but that's something we can pretty much count on. I do hope for a port/translation of some of the new numina from Mummy (most specifically, Untethered, Impassioned Soul, Lucid Dead, Old Soul, Revenant, and Intruder) - but again, most of that seems more likely than not.<br /> <br /> I suppose it's because Geist is self-contained - most requests in threads like this boil down to stuff from supplements we want in the core.<br /> <br /> In that vein, I would like to see is some of the extra detail on the Depths we see in Book of the Dead. The Gates as an alternative to the Rivers, the extra Rivers, the Tableaux, that sort of thing. Though when it comes to Dominions, I find the ones already in the Geist core more evocative.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T09:44:18-07:00","id":273938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>I think the Pass-On ceremony should be an inate ability also... It seems to me (YMMV of course) that it's pretty much a compulsory buy unless your Archetype is more focused on dealing with the living, such as the Celebrants or the Pilgrims.</i> </div> </div> </div>God, I hope not. If every group dealt with ghosts by just forcing them into the next realm, it'd make the game kind of unoriginal. I think even the book says its a last resort - for moral reasons, but also because its the boring blunt force approach.<br /> <br /> You can also destroy the ghosts anchors or resolve its unfinished business - both options that might require more work but lead to stories that amount to more than &quot;Ghost! I punch it in the face&quot; results.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T08:57:51-07:00","id":274740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272890#post272890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would favour this as a major difference between the Depths and the Dominions. As in, keep the cave network (with occasional underground lakes, and the twisted underground structures close to the Gates) for the Depths, and go into the alternatives in most of the Dominions, to the point where some Sineaters might see them as more like parallel dimensions accessed via the Depths than all part of the same world.</div> </div> </div> </div>My main point is that it would be preferable to see the Underworld framed in such a manner that the default assumption of &quot;what's on the other side of this wall?&quot; be &quot;empty space that might contain something unusual, from artifacts to bound monsters to a whole other otherworld&quot; rather than &quot;rocks, I guess.&quot;<br /> <br /> There's existing tidbits of this like the occasional sound of traffic and construction equipment or the toxic gases and other hazards that keep one from getting the best look at a given stretch of tunnel, but it bears emphasis that, static maze or not, Tartarus is in large part an unknown quantity. More than a few of the more esoteric antagonists could stand to benefit from having the Great Below described in terms that help readers imagine ways in which they might influence the living and the dead - the prison is porous, after all, and chthonic acoustics carry strangely between worlds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T15:33:45-07:00","id":275022,"title":"","content":"@ Oddness... Seems to me from reading the write-up though that 'Pass On' is finding a ghost in the Underworld and doing a small kind of ceremony of burning a photo of them or whatever and letting them pass on out of the Underworld same as resolving their unfinished business. To me its not the same as draining a ghost of essence then opening a gate to the Underworld to whale on them/smack them with their bane until they pop.<br /> Now those two should still be viable options, I just don't like the thought of dealing with ghosts the same way because you lack Ceremonies or options to do so. I wanna see Sin-Eaters to have the options behind them to judge ghosts accordingly, sending on peacefully ghosts that are more benevolent, targetting other ghosts into sending them downstairs to the Underworld or straight up murderising them if need be (Synergy Sin be damned, sometimes a Yellowbones needs taking out...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T04:33:51-07:00","id":275321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=275022#post275022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@ Oddness... Seems to me from reading the write-up though that 'Pass On' is finding a ghost in the Underworld and doing a small kind of ceremony of burning a photo of them or whatever and letting them pass on out of the Underworld same as resolving their unfinished business. To me its not the same as draining a ghost of essence then opening a gate to the Underworld to whale on them/smack them with their bane until they pop.<br /> Now those two should still be viable options, I just don't like the thought of dealing with ghosts the same way because you lack Ceremonies or options to do so. I wanna see Sin-Eaters to have the options behind them to judge ghosts accordingly, sending on peacefully ghosts that are more benevolent, targetting other ghosts into sending them downstairs to the Underworld or straight up murderising them if need be (Synergy Sin be damned, sometimes a Yellowbones needs taking out...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Have a look at page 274 and 275. The book explains that once a ghosts purpose is resolved it is free to pass on of its own free will - a sin eater doesn't necessarily have to do anything. This looks contradictory but note that the ritual specifies the ghost has resolved all his anchors. I'm not sure if this was a mistake on the writers part (you could ask for clarification I guess) but my interpretation is this:<br /> <br /> An anchor is a ghosts connection to the world, while the purpose is why it remained. An example might be that the ghosts purpose is to get vengence for his murder - in which case getting that vengence would resolve the ghosts issue and send them packing. A more noble ghost might decide that this isn't enough and have a purpose of stopping that sort of murder from ever happening again - its purpose is now too broad to simply resolve short of wiping out the entire race. Anchors on the other hand are specific connections to the mortal realm - A beloved toy or the place that the ghost resided maybe. These are places that the ghost has some specific connection to and provide a way for the ghost to continue to attempt its purpose. If these are gone the ghost is forced into the underworld - where it can either give up on accomplishing its purpose or hope to find some other way to form a new anchor.<br /> <br /> The ritual then is how you force a ghost with no anchors to move on even though its purpose isn't truly complete. It clearly hasn't stopped anyone from ever getting raped again, or helped everyone who's lost in the woods get home safely: but since it no longer has a way to connect to the mortal realm there's not much point in trying. It's done everything it could and its time to move on. The ritual is essentially the assisted suicide for ghosts that a few might be interested in. Most however will choose to fight on for the slim chance of finding a new way to resolve its purpose - perhaps by convincing sin eaters to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T13:14:09-07:00","id":275699,"title":"","content":"Man, I always come back to these thread and there's so much to catch up on, and I'm one of those losers who likes to reply to everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272197#post272197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking as someone for whom that connection is one of my favorite aspects of SE character creation, saying that &quot;all Sin-Eaters&quot; were such is a resounding falsehood. It's the Bound equivalent of being a &quot;templated&quot; wolf-blood before becoming a werewolf and just as non-guaranteed.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is that a non-guarantee? You were required to have some ghostly sense to become a Sin-eater. In my games, at least, I expanded that to be much much looser, and not as open and obvious as the &quot;you used to tell people how they were going to die when you were a little kid&quot;. More along the lines of just having an Unseen Sense that you didn't understand, or having something that made Ghosts want to be around you. And for some of my players we admittedly just sort of handwaved it to be one previous near death experience or didn't even worry about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272277#post272277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core did make it seem that a Sin-Eater very likely had in some way interacted with the dead in the past that it seemed to be all of them</div> </div> </div> </div> It's one of the requirements. Page 67 even has one of the questions you should ask players/yourself as &quot;How sensitive were you?&quot;<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To be honest though, unless you are doing such a game where you play a Mortal first it's likely not going to affect the game or your character's background so much and isn't necessary to dwell too much on. It is a good way to explain how a starting character could know this or that about ghosts without the dreaded 'metagaming' accusations coming up. </div> </div> </div>It very much affects your background. If I knew about ghosts before becoming a Sin-eater, it isn't as wondrous and strange.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272608#post272608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's fun, it ties into the semifatalism and chthonic bleedover that Morbid Reality opens up, it gives a sense of continuity from regular human to sensitive human to Bound to whatever-comes-next (and continues the general trend of supernatural fields drawing characters closer and closer into their orbits with continued exposure), it gives a lot of proto-Bound experience with stuff that makes them look kind of nuts and establishes a potential background from which characters might reasonably learn conventional supernatural secrecy, and it gives you a nice base from which to direct your character's worldview and areas of expertise, which is <i>important</i> in a game where personal stories are such a significant element of in-rules innovation.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except that a lot of people want to be completely new to the World of Darkness and their Awakening/Embrace/First Change/Durance/Bargain to be their first experience with the supernatural. They don't want to walk down a hallway, they want to cross <i>a threshold</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My position is that I'm having goddamn Demon &quot;but I don't WANNA play a robot!&quot; flashbacks and would prefer that this prove not to be a repeat of that unsightly display.<br /> <br /> My position is that I haven't <i>got</i> a position apart from &quot;stop talking nonsense and actually read the books,&quot; as is often the case. </div> </div> </div> Actually a lot of the time that's exactly what you rebutt with, but that's neither here nor there. The books actually do say &quot;you were psychic in some way&quot;, which is a hindrance. As for Demon, contrasting what I said above, Demon, Mummy, and Promethean are inherently games where you're playing from the opposite end: You're not a human who became a monster, you're a monster who became something like a human, or is at least passing themselves off as a human.<br /> <br /> Geist doesn't really gain anything by forcing the players to have been sensitive in some way. In fact, it kind of defeats a few of the themes, like I said above about thresholds. The feel of the Bargain is that there's no going back, that you've crossed a line and the door is now closed. That's not as strongly emphasized if you already had one foot in the grave to begin with. As an option? Yes, it's a nice one. I like &quot;you've been hanging around supernatural stuff and now it rubbed off on you&quot;. I even liked the plot in my Mage game where to turn someone into a Sin-eater to save his life, I needed to first give him Unseen Sense and make him a suitable host for the Geist, which entailed a long plot to get him a magic book that showed the names of the dead and how they died. Sidenote: Vet a geist before you shove it into your best friend. &quot;Hiroshima Shadow&quot; is a name to run away from really fast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272727#post272727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do me a favor, very quickly.<br /> <br /> Go look at the writeups for literally any of the sample SE characters in the corebook.<br /> <br /> Look very carefully.<br /> <br /> Show me, if you can,* where any of them have supernatural powers described in the pre-Bargain portion of their Background sections.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* You cannot, because no such description exists.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>That has more to do with the fact that Geist is an incredibly horribly written book. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would be pleased if I didn't have to struggle with communicative difficulties imparting the understanding of authorial intent that I've synthesized for this game from its own books and bluebook mentions, posts by the writers, and inference from the latter-day fluff to people who haven't taken literally weeks and months of their time deliberately processing the material like I have but don't understand how to properly leverage a position of ignorance by actually asking sincere questions. </div> </div> </div>That is, ultimately, an issue with <i>you</i>, not anyone else. In no small part due to the fact that you intentionally use the most circumlocutious and verbose description possible to assure people just how smart and well read you are. More than that, you're basing your entire argument on the fact that Krobeles isn't aware of an out of the way forum post--on a now defunct forum--as opposed to what the book directly states. Quoth the book, which you have treated as law before (when arguing with me about whether Geists have anchors, for instance):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geist: the Sin-eaters, page 67</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>How Sensitive Where You?</b><br /> <b><i>All Sin-eaters</i></b> were somehow sensitive before the merging.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI have no idea what the point of the Thoth &quot;Now You Know&quot; is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T13:26:55-07:00","id":275709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=272890#post272890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would favour this as a major difference between the Depths and the Dominions. As in, keep the cave network (with occasional underground lakes, and the twisted underground structures close to the Gates) for the Depths, and go into the alternatives in most of the Dominions, to the point where some Sineaters might see them as more like parallel dimensions accessed via the Depths than all part of the same world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm just weird, but I like the idea of the Upper Reaches having touches of life bleed through. Having them just be a cave system is lame, and doesn't really convey a sense of otherwordliness. The first section I had a player go to in the Underworld--after a long tunnel with no light--was &quot;Little Halicarnassos&quot;, a bustling shantitown of ghosts milling about in a subway station with two crisscrossing levels.<br /> Instead of talking about it, I'll just post this instead:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Me</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The corridor is a short one, at least as far as long curling tunnels to the realm of the dead are concerned, slopping downwards. The Witch leads the group through a doorway that looks like you'd find in an old access tunnel, though the letters and markings are in strange sigils. On the other side of the door there's an actual stairwell, made of stone and rusted iron, and with pipes that seem to pulse. At the bottom, the door opens on to more earthen tunnels. There's a noise of commotion and of all things life and after a while the flashlights go off as a glow comes from around a curve. And just around the bend the tunnel opens into a cavern...<br /> <br /> The cavern is rather large, with the ceiling fading off into darkness. The top half of it looks like a cave should, with stalagmites coming down from out of the darkness, dripping water every so often. Sometimes a strange pale batlike creature will flutter around from the dark. But below that is a different story. The tunnel they come from leads out into a rundown subway station, at the top level. Lights flicker, but they aren't electric, they're little bugs trapped behind the glass. People mill about, living in little sheds and hovels, all of them glowing a pale greenish white. In the distance there's the sound of something running along the rails, but there are people--ghosts--down on the lower level with their little plywood huts right on the tracks without a care. Strips of mostly faded cotton and gemstones decorate their houses, some with smears of dried blood or flaking paint. There is a lot of colour here, amongst the grey, even if most of it is old.<br /> <br /> All in all, there are perhaps hundreds of them living--in a manner of speaking, at least--down in this place, most down on the bottom level, but some talking up where Sabrina and Tacitus are. There's a rumbling in the distance, and the sound of pistons.<br /> <br /> &quot;Ah, 8:15, right on time,&quot; Sabrina murmurs as the ceiling shakes and drips more. Some of the strange white bat creatures fly away like birds startled out of a tree as a giant millipede runs across the top level track. It has an almost human mouth and it makes an unnerving high pitched whine as it rushes by, thousands of legs pumping in a wave motion across the raised track. The head disappears into the tunnels, but the legs keep going for almost a minute until getting to the end, which looks like the back end of a subway car, only with oversized human eyes instead of windows. After it's gone, it's like it was never there, and the bats start to fly back to their roosts.<br /> <br /> Heedless of the monster, Sabrina just leans against the rusted iron railing as it passes. &quot;Tacitus Lupo,&quot; she says with a bit of a grin, opening her arms to motion to the strangness around her, &quot;welcome to the Autocthonous Depths' Little Halicarnassus Station. The first last stop on your tour of the Underworld.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dominions, though? Those are vastly different. Some even have their own strangely shining suns, like the washed out reddish sepia of Dead Man's Hand, with it's Martian sands and warm, dry weather. Or the strange Egyptian city of Akar Hal, which had a night club, because I'll admit I panicked and just threw something in there. Or the Forge of Orcus, with it's massive ironworks. The Depths have their own strangeness, beyond just being rocky caverns, but it's the Dead Dominions where &quot;Something is uncomfortably uncanny&quot; goes to full blown &quot;We're not in Kansas anymore&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=275321#post275321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have a look at page 274 and 275. The book explains that once a ghosts purpose is resolved it is free to pass on of its own free will - a sin eater doesn't necessarily have to do anything. This looks contradictory but note that the ritual specifies the ghost has resolved all his anchors. I'm not sure if this was a mistake on the writers part</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing Geist? It was a mistake on the editor's part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":2998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","user":"Aspel","date":". 10-08-2014, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T18:36:41-07:00","id":275949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=275709#post275709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knowing Geist? It was a mistake on the editor's part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if it is, that ritual is incredibly boring if it's the bread and butter of the world rather than a niche response.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T07:23:27-07:00","id":276304,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d like to see more diverse antagonists in <b>Geist</b>: the earlier mention of porting ghostly Numina from <b>Mummy</b> into <b>Geist</b> is a good sta; but I\u2019d also want the chthonians (currently featured only in the Mage supplement <b>Summoners</b>) to be detailed in this game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T07:38:42-07:00","id":276322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Aspel:</b> Maybe I'm just weird, but I like the idea of the Upper Reaches having touches of life bleed through. </div> </div> </div>This is actually what I meant when I said &quot;twisted underground structures, though I admit the phrase probably didn't convey as much as thought it would. But yeah, I like the idea of the Underworld looking like cellars, underground systems, underpasses, sewers, and all of that - with the occasional noises, because that's awesome. I favour it becoming more cave-like as you go further from the Gates (and by extension further from the living world). But I also favour the Upper Reaches remaining entirely subterranean.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Dominions, though? Those are vastly different. </div> </div> </div>But, yeah, I have no problem with crazy-ass differences coming in here (though most of the Dominions in the Book of the Dead don't grab me).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T15:29:10-07:00","id":276700,"title":"","content":"@Aspel, I like to see life bleed into the Underworld through the Avernian Gateways too. I have this image in my mind I wanna put into a Geist game of the hospital scene from Jacob's Ladder, when the main character is wheeled strapped down on this trolley through a dark hospital full of rusting horrors and dark shadows very similar to what Silent Hill is doing now. For someone who had their near-death experience when being DOA at the hospital, the imagery of that scene is perfect as a representation of the Upper Reaches at such a location, especially the dialogue given to the main character by the 'hospital staff'... I really am trying to think how to place Jacob's Ladder into Geist's Underworld, especially due to the themes, of which I don't want to spoil but I recommend people check out the film... Its a good bit of inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T16:39:06-07:00","id":277678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=276322#post276322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have no problem with crazy-ass differences coming in here (though most of the Dominions in the Book of the Dead don't grab me).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've actually used Dead Man's Hand, and the goal was to go to Lowgate and free a prisoner or get him to talk (he had the secret to defeating the Strix, and I was escorting a Vampire through the Underworld). And some form of Mictlan and the Ocean of Fragments exists in my canon as well. Other than that... eh, varying levels of interesting. I like the Atheneaum and the Grave Dream has some good ideas. Oppia is also fun, and the Forge of Orcus is interestingish. I don't really think I'd use any of those in a game unless they fit for what I wanted, though. And even then I'd probably tweak their Kerberos a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=276700#post276700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have this image in my mind I wanna put into a Geist game of the hospital scene from Jacob's Ladder, when the main character is wheeled strapped down on this trolley through a dark hospital full of rusting horrors and dark shadows very similar to what Silent Hill is doing now.</div> </div> </div> </div> That scene and the aesthetics of <i>Silent Hill</i> (which was strongly inspired by <i>Ladder</i>) actually inspired an entire storyline of my Geist game. The players had previously defeated an Abmortal, their first big challenge, but one of them had been kidnapped and tortured and the other actually fought him and was beaten to hell (the third player fucked around in the Underworld while those two were in the hospital for a bit). They kept getting pulled down into the Underworld to this deathly reflection of the hospital as it was when it burned to the ground some fifty years ago. <br /> <br /> They were lucky enough that it never happened while anyone was in the room, but for them the paint would peel upwards and flake off like it was burning and they'd be in the Underworld, with faceless burned Nurses and a Geist in a plague mask and surgeon's outfit stalking the halls. In some places the walls were fleshy and convulsing. The operating theater had floors covered in blood. The sun room was a broiling hot place where outside the glass was burning fire. I thought I was very clever in that they actually found the proper entrance when one of the PCs died in the Underworld. (Sidenote: It never says whether Sin-eaters who die in the Underworld suffer as normal, or as if they were mortals who died in the Underworld; I went with the less harsh &quot;lose a dot of Sanity and you're ejected at the Avernian Gateway&quot; route).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-10T22:35:12-07:00","id":277890,"title":"","content":"It's a bit tangential and sort of a statement of the obvious, but as a general observation:<br /> <br /> I strongly suspect that having a handful or two of sample cities, as with any of the other 2e corebooks, will dramatically aid understanding and provide examples of weird plot seeds and local factions for STs to draw inspiration from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-11T17:06:45-07:00","id":278470,"title":"","content":"That would be without a doubt one of the best things that 2e Geist could do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-12T11:49:18-07:00","id":278962,"title":"","content":"It's a shame I never finished London Underground - but writing real world cities was never my strength.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-13T20:13:36-07:00","id":280467,"title":"","content":"I think Geist's biggest problem right now is a lack of focus. There isn't really a central theme holding the line together like the others. Are Geists horrifying burdens or are they mostly benign? The cover says its a &quot;Game of Second Chances&quot; but how does that tie-in to spelunking through the afterlife and being the ghost whisperer? There are ways to connect that stuff sure, but within the line itself, you don't have a lot of mechanics or fluff built around bringing those things together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T06:00:36-07:00","id":280920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=280467#post280467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Geist's biggest problem right now is a lack of focus. There isn't really a central theme holding the line together like the others. Are Geists horrifying burdens or are they mostly benign? The cover says its a &quot;Game of Second Chances&quot; but how does that tie-in to spelunking through the afterlife and being the ghost whisperer? There are ways to connect that stuff sure, but within the line itself, you don't have a lot of mechanics or fluff built around bringing those things together.</div> </div> </div> </div>This point has been stated before. Dont get me wrong. Your observation is entirely correct and everything. Its just that we've been over this before.<br /> Instead of pointing out the disonnance, lets talk about what we would like to see. Ultimately, <i>Should</i> they be benign or<i> Should </i>they be burdens?<br /> Personally, I rather prefer the burden-thing than the benign thing. I think it makes sure sense for an unliving death-god to be more inclined to be antagonistic than for it be entirely benign. They had a very cool system for this in World of Darkness: Inferno.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T07:06:30-07:00","id":280973,"title":"","content":"That was actually what I had in mind for the struggle mechanic I made. In Inferno I think the Possessed rolls Resolve + Composure against twice their total dots of Vestments. &quot;Roll against&quot; feels more struggly than the simple roll that Frenzy is now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-14T09:18:58-07:00","id":281129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=280920#post280920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This point has been stated before. Dont get me wrong. Your observation is entirely correct and everything. Its just that we've been over this before.<br /> Instead of pointing out the disonnance, lets talk about what we would like to see. Ultimately, <i>Should</i> they be benign or<i> Should </i>they be burdens?<br /> Personally, I rather prefer the burden-thing than the benign thing. I think it makes sure sense for an unliving death-god to be more inclined to be antagonistic than for it be entirely benign. They had a very cool system for this in World of Darkness: Inferno.<br /> <br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> I think Geists would work well as scary and unknowable. Its not much of a bargain if you get to come back and get superpowers and you can be a ghostbuster and you have a new buddy whos kinda creepy looking but hey they're good people. There needs to be some kind of conflict. As it is, <i>nobody</i> would refuse a bargain, even though the have the option to, because there are zero downsides. I feel like the bargain should feel like you're actually making a deal and have to give a little bit up. Having a weird, inscrutable superghost fused to your soul should be uncomfortable and kind of awful sometimes, because if it is, that means theres something you want bad enough to put up with it. There's something out there that you are (or were) willing to drag yourself back from the dead for. Make those second chances feel like second chances. Yeah, you and your ghost pal might have to learn to work with each other like a 90s buddy-cop flick, and yeah that's going to suck because you're just an average college student and this thing looks like a pig-zombie and wants you to kill your neighbor for eating porkchops, but you're gonna make it work whether the necro-swine likes it or not, because you got yourself a 1-UP and damn if you're going to waste it.<br /> <br /> The question every Sin-Eater should be asking themselves is &quot;Was it worth it?&quot;<br /> <br /> And at the end of the day the answer should be &quot;Yes.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T03:42:11-07:00","id":282143,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=281129#post281129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And at the end of the day the answer should be &quot;Yes.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I agree with you for everything except this last line. It's way more interesting if this answer changes between yes and no.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I like Geist's attitude towards this to be honest: at the end of the day you're running around with a powerful ghost running shotgun - as opposed to Inferno where the demon has the opportunity to run the show if it really wants to. I think, as cool as Inferno's mechanic might be, we should treat Geist as a completely separate beast. This is why I suggest using conditions rather than a tug of war condition to show a Geists influence on a humans mind.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">What I think Geist could use though to improve on this? How about a guide for creating and balancing a \u2018bargain\u2019 that actually affects players mechanically? It\u2019d have to have two effects: it\u2019d modify your synergy rolls - either changing a few of your synergy rolls or adding bonuses to them if the breaking point is a direct or indirect result of that bargain. I think it\u2019d also have a second effect - a punishment if a Sin-Eater went to long without finding some way of satisfying this bargain regularly.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">An example might be a Geist who\u2019s bargain is to ensure \u2018all dead are honored in death\u2019 - This gives the SE three unique aspects:</span><ul><li>Synergy breaking points are modified for this. Any breaking point that was reached as a result of fulfilling the bargain goes up 3 ranks in the breaking point chart. Thus, destroying a ghost that was desecrating the dead (by say, upturning a mausoleum or simply making a dead person look bad) goes from a rank 6 synergy breaking point to a rank 9.</li> <li>If the SE goes for more than a month without somehow finding a way to honor the dead, they gain the \u2018disjointed\u2019 condition - meaning -2 to all manifestation rolls. This condition worsens at six months and eventually leads to synergy breaking points. (Note: the time range should be adjusted depending on the difficulty of the task. A Geist that wants you to hunt down dangerous spirits might be happy if you catch one a year, as opposed to a month)</li> <li>Finally, the storyteller inflicts conditions of the character any time he hears of someone desecrating the dead - literally or figuratively. This leads to any story of someone desecrating the dead leading to a story complete with beat awards.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T10:38:27-07:00","id":282454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Oddness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=282143#post282143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I agree with you for everything except this last line. It's way more interesting if this answer changes between yes and no.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Good point.<br /> <br /> I think it might be an interesting twist if instead of straight up possessing the human's body when their synergy gets too low, the Geist just haunts the everloving crap out of them until they either do what the Geist wants or go mad (and then probably do what the Geist wants anyway). Like make it clear these are two separate beings from two separate planes of existence that got fused together. If the Geist can just possess the Human if they really want something, then why don't they just skip the whole bargaining bit and do that to begin with? I think you could break it down like this:<ul><li>The human is the master of the material world. They control their body, their environment, etc.</li> <li>The Geist is the master of the immaterial world. They control visions, emotions, ghosts, etc.</li> <li>When the two work together and have high synergy they can unite their abilities and do things like physically influence the immaterial or vice versa. (not sure if this part works but it sounds interesting in my head)</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T11:12:50-07:00","id":282540,"title":"","content":"It sort of works like that already - at least that's my justification for replacing morality with synergy rather than tracking two seperate stats - the Geist has fused with your subconcious, holding it together and filling out the weak points. This is why we no longer track morality - you're not going to go mad so long as you've got a powerful superghost holding your psyche together <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm OK with the idea of low Synergy meaning your Geist might even take over your body on occassion - when you're sleeping or possibly doing a multiple personalities disorder schtick. My thoughts is how to manage a high synergy relationship - and how to ideally maintain a good relationship with a Geist that should have its own reasons for being here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T14:28:47-07:00","id":282718,"title":"","content":"What I want to see:<br /> <br /> 1)Update Archetype: Really differentiate between them, make them more compelling.( I still don't get Mourners). Unique advantages and maybe Merits.<br /> 2)More on Chtonians<br /> 3)More on the DeathLords and the Five Horsemen<br /> 4)Update Synergy make it reflect better the agreement between Sin-Eater and Geist. Make it possible for the Geist to posses the Sin-Eater in case of low Synergy<br /> 5) More on Abmortals<br /> 6)More on weird creatures of the Underworld that defy classification<br /> 7)More on Krewes, including Conspiracies<br /> 8)Surprise me!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-15T15:06:35-07:00","id":282759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=282718#post282718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">( I still don't get Mourners).</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/75694-help-me-understand-mourners?p=75745#post75745\">You are not the first.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-16T11:38:47-07:00","id":283998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=275699#post275699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI have no idea what the point of the Thoth &quot;Now You Know&quot; is.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You know many things!&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-22T06:47:13-07:00","id":289504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Felipe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=282718#post282718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1)Update Archetype: Really differentiate between them, make them more compelling.( I still don't get Mourners). Unique advantages and maybe Merits.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main issue with the Archetypes is that the average Sin-eater is going to embody several of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-01T20:20:19-07:00","id":299579,"title":"","content":"Having reread the Geist book recently, having a bit of an expanded role in the greater World of Darkness would be a nice touch. They don't need to be numerous, nor even well understood unlike some of the other splats, but despite being fairly rare, it seems that more is known about Prometheans than Sin-Eaters as a whole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T10:27:53-08:00","id":301267,"title":"","content":"I see some support towards the Geister possessing the Sin Eater if they reach a low Synergy.<br /> <br /> #1 - Do you see this action as being active in the mechanics (like penalties towards rolls that go against what the Geister wants) or more of a passive ST (like the black alien symbiote suit from Spiderman who would swing Peter Parker around the city and beat the shit out of people using Peter's body while he was asleep).<br /> <br /> #2 - Is there ever a circumstance where you would <i>want </i>the Geister to take control, like the rules for &quot;Riding the Beast&quot; or &quot;Lashing Out&quot; from VtR?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/36-tomewilson","name":"tomewilson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar36_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T12:29:44-08:00","id":301414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tomewilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=301267#post301267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see some support towards the Geister possessing the Sin Eater if they reach a low Synergy.<br /> <br /> #1 - Do you see this action as being active in the mechanics (like penalties towards rolls that go against what the Geister wants) or more of a passive ST (like the black alien symbiote suit from Spiderman who would swing Peter Parker around the city and beat the shit out of people using Peter's body while he was asleep).<br /> <br /> #2 - Is there ever a circumstance where you would <i>want </i>the Geister to take control, like the rules for &quot;Riding the Beast&quot; or &quot;Lashing Out&quot; from VtR?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is just my interpretation, but it seems like the difference between VtR and Geist is that Vampire is giving into its base instincts while Geist is getting along with your subconcious. I think they are (and should be!) different implimentations - one is like getting carried away while the other is like having a split personality. So to answer your question, I think it should be a 'passive ST' thing - one that only happens in fairly extreme cases of extremely low synergy (like synergy 1)<br /> <br /> To put it another way, Geist shouldn't play out as I 'I have another mind in my head that I must appease' but instead play out more like 'I'm a little more likely to be conflicted about things thanks to the fact that my mind and a Geists mind have been grafted together'. It's not a matter of who's in control - its now a matter of how you have about 1.5 conciousnesses stapled together and stuck inside your head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T18:03:22-08:00","id":308682,"title":"","content":"I did a quickie conversion of Geist to GMC rules <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\">here.</a> I think, on the whole, Geist is good enough, and doesn't really need a HUGE change. The quickie conversion is meant to be just that, quickie to make Geist playable under 2E rules, not a full-on update. That said, it pretty much includes a lot of stuff I'd like to see explored more in-depth in a 2E Geist book.<br /> <br /> Primarily, that's the relationship between a Bound and her Geist. I love the concept, and Synergy is a REALLY interesting &quot;Morality&quot; stat, but I feel like the connection between the Bound and the Geist was glossed over quite a bit in the main Geist book. Why I came up with the idea of Ties, both to mechanically reflect Vampire Touchstones, but also so Bound players can think more in-depth about WHY this particular Geist chose to revive this particular person as Bound. I also really liked the idea of Geist's as &quot;part-spirit,&quot; in that they Geists are emblematic of certain concepts, and just do things related to those concepts. The core book has a passage talking about a Geist of car crashes, who causes car crashes not because it wants to, but just because that's what it is. So I came up with Compulsions (still looking for a better term) that represent a Geist's, shall we say, anti-social tendencies that the Bound has to try and keep in check. One of my favorite passages from the core book was talking about how Bound with more badass Geist's are considered more badass themselves. Someone keeping your regular old vengeance-y Geist in check is good, but someone who's holding in Spirit of Vengeance Itself? That guy's got to have some SERIOUS stones.<br /> <br /> I don't really want to see the Geist become &quot;the Beast by another name,&quot; in the Bound have the potential to be &quot;taken over&quot; by the Geist and forced to do things, by highlighting those times when the Bound and Geist's interests align perfectly, and those times when the misalign perfectly, would add a lot of interesting fodder to an already fantastic game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T17:08:18-08:00","id":314046,"title":"","content":"I've just been reading Hunter: Mortal Remains, and it states that there's a strong connection between geists and Ancient Egypt. I've never seen that before in any of the Geist sourcebooks; I wonder if this is a first hint at a future Geist chronicle.<br /> <br /> There's also an odd bit about a group of sin-eaters who go out of their way to free an &quot;evil&quot; ghost from a group of hunters and to cause trouble for trouble's sake. Again, I wonder if this is laying the groundwork for the antagonists in a future Geist chronicle.<br /> <br /> Of course, Mortal Remains is supposed to be revealing what Hunters &quot;know&quot; about various other supernatural beings. Conceivably, the stuff about geists being Egyptian is just misinformation believed by ignorant Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4310-jagardner","name":"jagardner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T11:51:55-08:00","id":314734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jagardner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=314046#post314046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've just been reading Hunter: Mortal Remains, and it states that there's a strong connection between geists and Ancient Egypt. I've never seen that before in any of the Geist sourcebooks; I wonder if this is a first hint at a future Geist chronicle.<br /> <br /> There's also an odd bit about a group of sin-eaters who go out of their way to free an &quot;evil&quot; ghost from a group of hunters and to cause trouble for trouble's sake. Again, I wonder if this is laying the groundwork for the antagonists in a future Geist chronicle.<br /> <br /> Of course, Mortal Remains is supposed to be revealing what Hunters &quot;know&quot; about various other supernatural beings. Conceivably, the stuff about geists being Egyptian is just misinformation believed by ignorant Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup, and Hunters will have a skewed understanding of all the other splats for two reasons: the nature of humans to be distrustful of anything they don't understand, and because they don't really care about angsty supercharged hunters who've learned to harness ghosts: they're only going to be concerned with the group they need to actually fight. There's plenty of reasons a Krewe could have for trying to get that ghost freed that might not be causing trouble for trouble's sake: perhaps they were disturbed by the fact that the hunters were using a ghost, or wanted to force that ghost to move on and the hunters had blocked that from happening, or perhaps they were legitimately just hooligans with some religious drive to unleash havoc on the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1085-oddness","name":"Oddness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-21T20:03:39-08:00","id":318647,"title":"","content":"Maybe sin-eaters could do things like protect the living world from the underworld which is always trying to merge into the living world. Think something like the Shadowman (both video games and comic books)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-25T01:08:13-08:00","id":321553,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see alittle more elaboration on the Keystone Mementos. They were a really cool idea, of a physical object soul-bound to the Sin-Eater which is the tangible manifestation of the link between the Geist and Sin-Eater, although the book hardly went into more detail than that.<br /> I'd like to see some rules of construction and customization, and perhaps some merits or other traits to further develope the Keystone and perhaps the link itself by proxy. Namely, I take issue with the fact that this Keystone can be any object - trinket or <i>weapon</i> - yet there is no mechanical benefit to choosing anything other than a weapon or other item with a utility purpose. I'd like such things to be explored somehow, and a handful of merits would be an easy way to go about doing that, in my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-17T15:54:08-07:00","id":446628,"title":"","content":"This may have been covered earlier in the thread, though I see some mention of there being really no downside to the Bargain a Sin-Eater enters into as is in the rules. Perhaps not at first glance, but when you look into it... There are specific things that make a Bound a walking target for ghosts... They can interact more clearly with ghosts than normal mortals and as such, ghosts are going to hound them to have them help the ghost with their unfinished business or bother them in some way. If the ghosts knew that Bound blood can rejuvenate them into an echo, then the Bound is going to find themselves being attacked by ghosts to get to that plasm-enriched blood.<br /> <br /> Also... I think it'd be hard for a Bound to find connections in the mortal world once they've received their Geist... They can see when a person is going to die and their general health conditions... Meeting someone you really like and seeing you have 'this much in years' time with them can be somewhat... morbid. So being hounded by Ghosts and knowing when everyone you love and care about in the world of the living is going to die... That kind of sucks, along with the Geist inside you being a dick and bringing you back from the dead and keeping you awake when you've taken a huge beating or are heavily injured, full of pain... But nope, you don't K.O until the reaper comes calling.<br /> <br /> I don't think Bound are all Blessed with Awesome with no downpoints at all. Of course having more mechanical ways to represent these downs with the ups would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T10:17:17-07:00","id":459124,"title":"","content":"I would like to see geister imposing presistant conditions on their respective sin-eater. The only way to resolve them would be to give in to the geists' demands which would cause a degeneration roll, or the sin-eater could cause a ghost to move on. both would temporarily alleviate the confition. But it would give sin-eaters a mechanical reason to help ghosts. I mean aside from plasm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1064,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","user":"miss_minty","date":". 03-27-2015, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-27T10:22:58-07:00","id":459130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=459124#post459124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see geister imposing presistant conditions on their respective sin-eater. The only way to resolve them would be go e in to the geists' demands which would cause a degeneration roll, or the sin-eater could cause a ghost to move on. both would temporarily alleviate the confition. But it would give sin-eaters a mechanical resdin to help ghosts. I mean aside from plasm.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a very nice idea!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T20:33:26-07:00","id":460636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=446628#post446628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Bound are all Blessed with Awesome with no downpoints at all. Of course having more mechanical ways to represent these downs with the ups would be great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blessed with Awesome is the selling point of Geist, though.<br /> <br /> Each game, after the main trio, departs from the standard WoD core themes in at least one way, which makes it's thematics distinct<br /> <br /> Prometheans are allowed to have a happy ending, even if they have to work their stolen asses off to get it: Hell, it's even got rules right inthe core book.<br /> <br /> Hunters flip flop the setting: You're not the creatures who go bump in the night, bringing darkness to the world even if you're good intentioned, you're a relativly normal human bumping back, serving as candle in the darkness even if you're intentions are less than pure.<br /> <br /> changeling is another flip flop: what in other games would be a sticky end is just part of your backstory: You've already lived through the worst there is, so the only options are heading up, or not moving on at all.<br /> <br /> Mummy reverses the power scale: You're not a new anything: You're an ancient and powerful being. You don't fear you're elders, you fear losing your powers and being forcibly reclaimed by the sleep that robs you of your memories.<br /> <br /> In most games, nobody has any clue how crap works. In Demon, you've got a pretty good idea, because you used to be part of the machine that maintained the world, and mos tof your rivals and allies are the same.<br /> <br /> In Upcoming Beast, instead of the isolation of the other gamelines, you've got a huge family themes, to the point where cross splat interation and friendlyness is both encouraged and being built into the system<br /> <br /> What makes Geist Different from the Blue Book and the Big Three? Most o fthe other splats, it sucks much bad to be one. The Bad always, in the long run, outways the good unless you work your ass off to avoid the bad. With Sin-Eaters, the good ultimately outweighs the bad: Given the choice between being dead or being alive, you got to choose alive. To sweeten the deal, you've got some fucking sweat psychic powers and a head guest who has it in their best interest to keep you happy and healthy. Yeah, ghosts can tell you can see them and will try to make you help them, but you get great rewards for helping them move on and you can always ward your pad to keep them out. and Yeah, sometimes you're head guest can be annoying or have disturbing requests, but unless it's an unusually crazy one, you're a spineless bastard, or you've died a lot, you can negotiate it down to something better or just tell it to shut the fuck up.<br /> <br /> The World sucks, nothing has any meaning to it, nothing lasts, and you're all going to die someday, but that day is not today. The closest thing to dying you experienced only made you stronger.<br /> <br /> You're alive, and that's something to celebrate, so pull up a chair and crack open a beer.<br /> <br /> Lack of Sin-Eater suckage is a feature, not a bug. It's what makes it distinct from the other game lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-28T21:18:57-07:00","id":460656,"title":"","content":"Including rules for playing as a ghost/Wraith would be pretty nice as there's a shitton of crossover between the two. Assuming a full-on Wraith line isn't in the cards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T17:58:02-07:00","id":462917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=460656#post460656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Including rules for playing as a ghost/Wraith would be pretty nice as there's a shitton of crossover between the two. Assuming a full-on Wraith line isn't in the cards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Lucid Dead Numen from Mummy goes a long way to making that doable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T04:52:59-07:00","id":464561,"title":"","content":"Different models of playable ghosts - from bodyhopers who make each vessel a Key/Manifestation wielding Bound (only they're the central self), to wraiths on a clock (ala Mummy) to complete their unfinished business, etc.<br /> <br /> For the Bound the biggest thing is they need to make the Bargain and dealing with your Geist have actual mechanical impact. Because if it doesn't it doesn't carry the pressure and tension it should for players as the downside of the Bound state. The easiest way to do this will be with 2E Synergy actually being about your personal relationship with your Geist and its thematic needs.<br /> <br /> Actually I wouldn't be surprised if Synergy ended up like Harmony, where you have an ideal rating at 5, with 10 you've smothered the Geist but are cut off from its power, and at 0 you are nothing but its meat-suit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T06:34:35-07:00","id":464628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=464561#post464561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if it doesn't it doesn't carry the pressure and tension it should for players as the downside of the Bound state.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is missing the point-the lack of amajor downside to the Bound Condition is one of the selling points of the game-It does not suck to be a Sin-Eater, unlike the many other supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> One of Geist's themes is very much &quot;Yeah, the world sucks, but you're alive and thats something to celebrate&quot;-a major downside would dilute this theme.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T06:40:09-07:00","id":464630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=464628#post464628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is missing the point-the lack of amajor downside to the Bound Condition is one of the selling points of the game-It does not suck to be a Sin-Eater, unlike the many other supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> One of Geist's themes is very much &amp;quot;Yeah, the world sucks, but you're alive and thats something to celebrate&amp;quot;-a major downside would dilute this theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>If being bound to a spirit that wants to promulgate death in the world has no thematic weight to it, I have zero interest in playing it.<br /> <br /> Life being WORTH IT ANYWAY, enhances the theme, it doesn't detract from it, while still keeping it a horror game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T09:34:59-07:00","id":464751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=464628#post464628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is missing the point-the lack of amajor downside to the Bound Condition is one of the selling points of the game-It does not suck to be a Sin-Eater, unlike the many other supernatural beings.<br /> <br /> One of Geist's themes is very much &quot;Yeah, the world sucks, but you're alive and thats something to celebrate&quot;-a major downside would dilute this theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it still a World of Darkness game? If the answer is Yes, then there sould still be a strong sense of downside and &quot;everything kinda sucks&quot;.<br /> I do agree though, that one of the really interesting things about Geist is the theme that life is still totally worth it and its still really awesome, in spite of all the shit and slightly <i>because</i> of all the shit.<br /> But there is still shit.<br /> <br /> Its mentioned multiple times throughout the fluff that some Geists are really unpleasant and spiteful, and its emphatized that its not always fun being a Sin-Eater. The fluff totally lends itself to this downside and it totally <i>should've</i> been there. My players were immensely surprised that it wasn't, actually, and I cant say my initial reaction was much different.<br /> It isn't missing the point. It would be missing the point if we were to argue that we wanted the &quot;life is good&quot; thematic to be removed. That would be missing the point.<br /> <br /> What I think we need, is actually mechanics that emphasizes both. We need some way for a Sin-Eater to mechanically benefit from going out and enjoying themselves, and showing the Geist what it means to be alive again. We had alittle of it in first edition, what with some Sin-Eaters being able to regenrate plasm by being beaten to a bloody pulp (hurting is still feeling alive, I guess) but I'de like some mechanics that emphasize this a bit more. Go out and sky-dive, get plasm! Go out and get laid, get plasm! Go out and jump onto the stage at a rock concert and then stagedive into the crowd, get plasm! Really any activity that gives the Sin-Eater (and by extension, the Geist) a great sense of feeling <i>alive</i>, should net you some plasm. Thats what the Geist wants, after all. To feel alive again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T19:44:33-07:00","id":465508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=464751#post464751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it still a World of Darkness game? If the answer is Yes, then there would still be a strong sense of downside and &quot;everything kinda sucks&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every Game, other than the main 3, plays with the general WoD thematic assumptions in a way that makes it unique.<br /> <br /> The fact that being a Sin-Eater doesn't suck is how Gesit plays with those thematics-it's the light grey in a world of dark grey and black.<br /> <br /> And the fluff specifically mentions that it sucks to be a sin-eater <b>if</b> 1). You have no spine, 2) You're Geist is exceptionally crazy(like Dem Bones or the over protective one from the antagonist chapter), or 3) You have very low synergy or have died to many times to have Synergy<br /> <br /> None of those are default assumptions for player characters, and they should not be default assumptions for a player character. If you want you're Geist to be exceptionally annoying so that you can't just negociate with it or tell it to shut the fuck up, fine, that's an optional flaw. Making it a default assumption of the setting makes being a Sin-Eater suck, and one of the things that Makes Geist Distinct goes down the toilet.<br /> <br /> The lack of supernatural Angst in Geist, the fact that the majority of Sin-Eaters do not suffer any major drawbacks to making the bargain, this what makes Geist Distinct.<br /> <br /> Now, lets look at this Logically: The Majority of Geister choose to merge with a mortal in order to experience the sensation of life again. If they have an Agenda, at all, it's something like &quot;:Go out and get shit faced&quot; or otherwise enjoying physical pleasures. I imagine very few hosts would be unwilling to sate at least some of those urges.<br /> <br /> but, a minority of Geister have some kind of major Agenda. Lets say some NeoNazi gets his ass kicked and dies from his injuries, he sticks around as a ghost and eventually he becomes a Geist. Lets say that it as his sheer hatred for the jews that kept him around as a ghost, so his Geist has an Agenda of &quot;murder all of the jews&quot;. He's not going to hop into a black guy and ask him to murder jews. He's going to wait for another racist dickbag to get the shit beat out of him and nearly die, and make the bargain with him, someone who'd be willing to fulfil the geist's agenda. Alternatively, he'll jump into a spineless coward who can easily be bullied into following his agenda. In the first case, the host is suffering no drawbacks. in the second, it's not a PC, because assuming the PCs are spineless cowards is bad game design.<br /> <br /> That just leaves the exceptionally Crazy Geister who are somehow Lucid enough to make the Bargain, Geister like Dem Bones. I would assume that Geister that crazy don't have many hosts, and the ones that do make Sin-Eaters that are exceptions to the normal &quot;being bound doesn't suck&quot; condition.<br /> <br /> Adding suckage and supernatural Angst as a Default Part of the Sin-Eater package is in fact missing the point, because if the condition sucks, then the life is good theme gets diluted.<br /> <br /> so, if more of the world of Darkness &quot;The world is shitty&quot; themes absolutely have to be added, it shouldn't be in the form of Drawbacks to the inherent Sin-Eater condition, it should be n the form of things External to the Sin-Eaters-some of those High Rank Specters have a habit of getting loose into the living world in the places that Sin-Eaters like to congregate due to the high number of fonts of Ectoplasmic Power and Avernian Gates. Sometimes these nasty rank 3+ spectres are hard to put back down, and sometimes they cause a lot of damage before you can destroy them or send them back.<br /> <br /> the core book mentioned that sin-Eaters tended to get on well with Werewolves, once they convinced the Uratha that they're not possessed by harmful spirits. But Werewolf 2.0 has the tribe that Hunts Claimed also Hunt Sin-Eaters because &quot;Claimed by the Dead is Still Claimed&quot; a few mentions of &quot;Sometimes the wolves are friendly, but sometimes one will tear your head off for no fucking reason, man.&quot; in the fluff would tone tha up, too.<br /> <br /> Maybe something in the underworld really hates how unnatural the bound are, and has these... Deathly things, not quite ghost, but definitely not Spirit, that it can send to the living world to really fuck up a Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> Just don't make the Bound Condition inherently sucky, I mean, a happy host is in the geist's best interests, after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 04-01-2015, 10:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-01T20:20:25-07:00","id":465551,"title":"","content":"In the interest of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/187013-morality-for-demon?p=187215#post187215\">pointing people away from what is, all told, a rather dull bit of lingering fancruft that doesn't do well outside the background</a>, I'm just going to point out that 2e in particular has been taking a tack of emphasizing why it's fun to play as [your playable supernatural entity here] instead of hammering on the Supernatural Life Is Suffering button.<br /> <br /> If the World of Darkness is conclusively anything, it is <i>weirder.</i> Geist is one of the gamelines for which that quality especially shines, in case things like rivers of scorpions or bleeding fog or being the incarnated vessel of the Elvis of Knives or forging bizarre mutant crossbreed mythology that can implicitly become the core of a world-spanning cultural tradition weren't clues enough that the Bound get a good long walk on the weird side.<br /> <br /> &quot;Overwhelmingly, the power of the Underworld is the power to break down the lines between what is real and what is not.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T03:45:50-07:00","id":465900,"title":"","content":"I dont think you're entire wrong in your acessment, but I think you might be forgetting that contrast is what ultimately causes emphasis.<br /> We dont determine a games impact by where the line is, but by how much it wavers. As such, if we have no &quot;Life kinda sucks&quot; emelemts, the impact of the &quot;life is good&quot; thematic will be entirely lost, because thats just setting a conssistently high horizontal line. It'll have no impact.<br /> Conversely, if you take away the &quot;life is good&quot; thematic, the &quot;Life kinda sucks&quot; thematic will be weaker for it, because thats also just a horizontal line, set at a different altitude.<br /> You need contrast because of this.<br /> <br /> Also, a game where &quot;Everything is good and life is awesome&quot; might be a very unique World of Darkness game, but it wont be fun or interesting. What interesting stories are you going to tell in a game like that? My own life is allready kinda good and everything is allready kinda awesome, so why would I interested in a game that portrays that, but with a supernatural twist? I make the assumption here, that peoples whoose lives are shitty and sucks, have better things to do than play tabletop roleplaying games, of course...<br /> <br /> Interesting stories rise from adversity, and I honestly think its alittle derailing to call this internal adversity &quot;angst&quot;. Honestly, the very principle and core of Geist is that you have another person <i>living in your head!</i> I get extreamly fed up with my room mates, and I dont see them 1/10 of the time I would be forced to put up with a Geist. How is having another person living in your head, not something that lends itself to a bit of internal adversity?<br /> Sure, the good should still outway the bad, I agree on that. After all, having a dude live in your head is still better than dying, but it certainly wont be fun all the time, even if the dude is lovely.<br /> Of course you could always make the arguement that such can be handled by storyteller fiat on a case by case basis, but the thing is, if there isn't any concret systems to it, it gets forgotten.<br /> <br /> As I said, saying; &quot;I want Geist to be a darker game&quot; would be missing the point. Saying; &quot;I want systems for the thematic elements that was allready part of the game, but was left out of the mechanics of 1ed, for some obscure reason&quot; certainly is not.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T06:29:51-07:00","id":466007,"title":"","content":"It was left out, because it was assumed to be a minority occurrence-the PCs were not playing as spineless cowards, were not playing as people with Geists that were so disturbing or anoying that you couldn't function with them, and were not playing as Wretched. The three of those are the places were it's said that having a Geist is a problem, but none of those are PCs.<br /> <br /> Like I said, if you want more WoD life Sucks, include it as things <i>external </i>to the Sin-Eater: Instead of making the Sin-Eater Condition inherently Sucky, make them have to deal with problems that sometimes suck.<br /> <br /> sin-Eaters are, at the time, the only Splat that has no inherent Super Natural Angst: Yeah, you've got a head guest that can be annoying or disturbing sometimes, but for the Most Part you can ignore it or negotiate it down to something else, and besides, you're alive and you have Super Powers, and that's better than being dead.<br /> <br /> Introduce major inherent Drawbacks into the default Sin-Eater condition, if you introduce something that would honestly make more than a minority of Sin-Eaters regret making the Bargain, then you introduce Supernatural Angst to the Splat, and Supernatural Angst , that is, &quot;Woe is me, my awesome powers make my life suck&quot; is utterly incompatible with &quot;Yeah, sometimes bad things happen, but in general, life is good&quot;<br /> <br /> So, if you need more of that WoD life suckage, making it completely External to the Sin-Eater-The Sin-Eaters doesn't have anything inherently Sucky about their nature, but sometimes they have to interact with Sucky things or make difficult decisions.<br /> <br /> If you want more incentive for a Sin-Eater to interact with Ghosts, use carrots, not sticks.<br /> <br /> But don't introduce Supernatural Angst to the splat, especially not by making Minority Cases default PCs, because &quot;WoD, now with less Supernatural Angst&quot; is the selling point of Geist: There's no Supernatural Angst, and even with Weird and Creepy stuff going on, in general life is good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T07:28:22-07:00","id":466035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=466007#post466007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sin-Eaters doesn't have anything inherently Sucky about their nature</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you the fucking sunshine man and the god-king of space, to aparently be able to get along with anyone and everyone?<br /> Seriously dude, the base premise of Geist is that you have a dude living in your head. I have a brother, and I love my brother to bits. He is probably the one person in the world, that I get along with the most. We have spend hours and hours discussing random and just straight up bullshitting about, for fun.<br /> But we still get on each others nerves sometimes, and if he was grafted to the left side of my head, I'm pretty sure we would get on each others nerves all the fucking time. Honestly, I think it would suck significantly less to have everyone kinda hate you (Promethean) than it would to never be truely alone. Maybe thats just the way I view things, as a nihilistic, misanthropic introvert, but having somebody grafted to your mind and soul would suck heaps, in my opinion. You can sorta emulate Disquiet by not bathing for a few days, and at the few occations where that has happened to me, its not nearly as annoying as the times I've had the displeasure of being around people 24/7 for a few days.<br /> <br /> The very basic premise - the one thing in Geist that you simply cannot escape, write out, or change without changing the fundamentals of the game - lends itself to atleast a small degree of what you refer to as &quot;angst&quot;...Still not a really apropriate term for it, but whatever.<br /> You cannot actually and seriously, be saying that having an alien ghost grafted to your mind, would carry no &quot;angst&quot;, can you?<br /> Do you really seriously mean to say, that having a Geist whisper in your ear, as you drive the &quot;Run down that old lady. Its her time to do. She wont be missed!&quot;, wont be kinda unsetteling? How about going to a club, and having a gorgeous woman come up to you and chat with you, only to realize half-way through your first kiss, that this lady is going to die of breast cancer in 6 months, so striking up a relationship with her would be meaningless? How about having the walk from home to school be a cold and clammy experience, because a tripple homicide happened here last year, and the Death Stain still hasn't gone away? How about waking up 3 AM at night, because a Ghost is screaming at you, because you didn't stop the man who murdered the ghost, which happened last week in front of your apartment complex while you were sitting there playing World of Warcraft entirely oblivious to it all? <br /> <br /> Those are experiences that the 1ed incorporated entire and multiple of them even had a sizeable amount of mechanics behind them. Are you suggesting those wouldn't cause any &quot;angst&quot;? Really? I agree, that Geist shouldn't be <i>about the &quot;angst&quot;</i>, but theres a significant difference between being about the &quot;angst&quot; and having it be there to a lesser degree.<br /> <br /> As you can probably see, I dont really agree that the &quot;Geist is kinda unpleasant&quot; applies to only Wretched, the weak-willed and monstrous Geists. Even the most benevolent Geist will be off-putting at times. Even if its not trying to be. Besides, being a &quot;spineless coward&quot; means having a low Resolve+Composure score. I've seen a few PC's who had a low Resolve+Composure score, so those were spineless cowards. Lets not make any assumptions at all, and just assume the baseline. Assuming that a character is a spineless coward is equally as bad as assuming the character isn't a spineless coward.<br /> <br /> Really, all I'm asking is something like a mechanic that allows the Storyteller to apply Conditions on behalf of the Geist, if its (dis)pleased. Like &quot;The Geist fancies that lady. You get the 'Swooning' Condition&quot;. Or &quot;The Geist is feeling good about this, you get the 'Inspired' Condition&quot; or &quot;The Geist is displeased with you. You get the 'Regrets' Condition&quot;. I would even be fine with just having it as an optional rule. As long as its recognized in some small fashion, I wouldn't mind.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T08:08:55-07:00","id":466101,"title":"","content":"Sin Eaters do not live in happy unicorn land where everything is just perfect for them. Geist is an extremely Nietzscheian game, where the point is staring at the ultimate fatality of the universe and smiling. The trick is to add those grim dark elements but in a way where people can still laugh at them and have fun. Yes, you see a literal timer clicking down over your child's head and it's much shorter than yours. Other people would mourn the sudden loss of their child. You have the chance to make every second on that clock matter. Do you?<br /> <br /> Unless the Geist's motivations are something to <i>completed</i> I think the best place for them is Virtue and Vice. Instead of whatever the character was before, now relaxing and affirming oneself enough to get willpower involves cowtowing to the Geist. Through playtesting, determine whether or not Sin Eaters should regain willpower through sleeping. Include a Virtuous / Vice-Ridden equivalent merit. People with Geists whose Virtue and Vice are things like, &quot;Give your victims enough time to beg before killing them / sucker punch orphans in the face&quot; are obviously going to have a harder time than someone with tamer and more common ones, representing the particularly crazy Geist without making it mandatory.<br /> <br /> Another good place to introduce drama is the Geist equivalent of Touchstones. One subversion I simultaneously like in concept but feel was underutilized was the fact that Sin Eaters really don't need to fear death. It's simply off the table. However, if we are going down that path then we really need to highlight something else as what's at stake. Making Touchstones attached to integrity similar to Vampire puts them at stake, with the concept of <i>permanently</i> losing them by dying enough times on the table. The trick here is being very careful about what the &quot;sins&quot; are.<br /> <br /> On that note, you know what would be cool? Taking on a Ghost's Anchors and Unfinished Business like Demons do with pieces of someone's life to patch in parts of their Cover. Maybe grant &quot;Finished Business Beats&quot; for both taking Unfinished Business on and for resolving it. Maybe the Sin Eater can only keep one batch of &quot;Unfinished Business&quot; per dot in Psyche. When you gain someone's Unfinished Business you gain some plasm and merits or something to represent the passions of the Ghost helping you and the world strangely accepting that you are the person with that specific unfinished business. When you resolve it, you lose the benefit for having it but completely refill on Plasm. Could replace Ectophagia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","user":"SoulGambit","date":". 04-02-2015, 11:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T08:25:57-07:00","id":466138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=466101#post466101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note, you know what would be cool? Taking on a Ghost's Anchors and Unfinished Business like Demons do with pieces of someone's life to patch in parts of their Cover. Maybe grant &quot;Finished Business Beats&quot; for both taking Unfinished Business on and for resolving it. Maybe the Sin Eater can only keep one batch of &quot;Unfinished Business&quot; per dot in Psyche. When you gain someone's Unfinished Business you gain some plasm and merits or something to represent the passions of the Ghost helping you and the world strangely accepting that you are the person with that specific unfinished business. When you resolve it, you lose the benefit for having it but completely refill on Plasm. Could replace Ectophagia.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like this idea, actually. I dont think it should nessesarily replace Ectophagia. We can have both, I feel.<br /> Actually, when I can get myself balled around to doing it, I'll try to do some homebrewie stuff on this. I think its a pretty cool concept. Also ties into the name. &quot;Sin-Eater&quot;. Currently, you cant really eat any sins. This way, you actually can <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-02T17:28:40-07:00","id":466713,"title":"","content":"Not being able to actually eat or resolve sins is my #1 gripe against Geist. Lack of fleshed out Geister mechanics and the patchwork and unfocused presentation of the material is my ties for #2 and #3. That said, Sin Eater remains one of the best presentations of mood in 1e and deals with some potentially really evocative stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-03T12:44:58-07:00","id":467788,"title":"","content":"It should definitely keep the mood of being alive is great, but the game definitely needs obstacles and direction for characters to work with, perhaps more fleshed out antagonists or even new antagonists to deal with in both the living and underworld, as great as it is to be alive again, you need fight to keep things that way I feel, something to evoke the &quot;I fought to get a second chance at life and I'll be damned sure to keep on fighting to see it through so I can live it up!&quot; feeling. The proposed Geist Dark Era for Golden Age of Piracy probably would have been a good direction for this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> As great as it is to have as many options to do whatever you want in a game like Geist, it can leave things feeling a bit aimless or without direction. Not necessarily by throwing in angst to drag things down, but the symbiotic relationship with Sin-Eaters and Geists could definitely stand to be built on, the touchstone system introduced in Vampires 2e is seems like a good direction to go with things like the Keystone memento and the other types of memento, or especially the anchors one needs when Psyche gets too high.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T07:38:28-07:00","id":476936,"title":"","content":"Something to keep in mind is that none of the other supernaturals get a choice in the matter (save for Demons, arguably). Mages have the veil ripped from their eyes, Werewolves and Prometheans (and Beasts) are born this way, Vampires, Changelings, and Mummies have it forced on them. Even many Hunters answer the call out of necessity rather than personal desire.<br /> <br /> <i>Every</i> Sin-Eater <i>chose</i> to be a Sin-Eater. Every one. So right from the start the tone of the story is going to be different from the others, because every problem you run into because of your supernatural-ness becomes a price you are willing to pay. You don't need to have everything be awesome and great and your Geist is your best bud, because that would undermine what is otherwise a pretty strong theme. That regardless of the problems you'll run into down the line, life is worth it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-11T10:26:38-07:00","id":477074,"title":"","content":"Since there is a Tokyo setting for 2e, I think Aokigahara would be an interesting location to bring up for the Sin-Eaters of Japan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T23:38:20-07:00","id":494447,"title":"","content":"Mostly I'd like a few things:<br /> <br /> 1) Reworked Manifestations/Keys. Either what they're doing now but very fine tuned or a complete reworking, but whatever the case it's gotta be done.<br /> <br /> 2) Do something interesting with Synergy. I feel a lot of a splat's flavor comes from it's Integrity version, especially in 2e; Geist 2e's Synergy is one of my least favorite.<br /> <br /> 3) This one might be a little controversial: I'd like the hard limit on a Sin-Eater's resurrections being determined by Synergy removed. If there is a limit to their ability to come back - and at this point I'm not convinced that there needs to be* - I think it should be tied to something cool and flavorful. Likewise, I'm open to ways to kill a Sin-Eater permanently but they should also be cool and flavorful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T01:08:42-07:00","id":494512,"title":"","content":"I think removing the reduction of max Synergy could be fine. It costs experience to bump it back up anyway and few players may want to risk using their experience on bumping their Synergy back up if they have a Killer GM that's going to have their character go through another death real soon...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T03:20:44-07:00","id":494564,"title":"","content":"That would be the easiest method, but like I said I would rather Synergy get reworked anyways so I don't know if tying it to that trait at all is the best move.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T11:39:57-07:00","id":508221,"title":"","content":"Sorry, been awhile since I've been to this subforum and sort of forgot about this conversation, so sorry for how late this is.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=466035#post466035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you the fucking sunshine man and the god-king of space, to apparently be able to get along with anyone and everyone?<br /> Seriously dude, the base premise of Geist is that you have a dude living in your head. I have a brother, and I love my brother to bits. He is probably the one person in the world, that I get along with the most. We have spend hours and hours discussing random and just straight up bullshitting about, for fun.<br /> But we still get on each others nerves sometimes, and if he was grafted to the left side of my head, I'm pretty sure we would get on each others nerves all the fucking time. Honestly, I think it would suck significantly less to have everyone kinda hate you (Promethean) than it would to never be truly alone. Maybe that's just the way I view things, as a nihilistic, misanthropic introvert, but having somebody grafted to your mind and soul would suck heaps, in my opinion. You can sorta emulate Disquiet by not bathing for a few days, and at the few occasions where that has happened to me, its not nearly as annoying as the times I've had the displeasure of being around people 24/7 for a few days.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yes. You're sharing your body 24/7 with somebody that you wwillingly and knowingly let in. You will note that in order to get what they want, it's in their best interest to keep you happy and healthy because unless you're at synergy zero, they can't make you do anything. and you can just tell them to shut up if they start bugging you.<br /> <br /> And you'll also note that between a choice of being dead or having a head guest whose best interest includes your health and happiness, I doubt anybody would choose &quot;being dead&quot;. That's the point. if being s sin-eater sucked that bad, nobody would take the deal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The very basic premise - the one thing in Geist that you simply cannot escape, write out, or change without changing the fundamentals of the game - lends itself to at least a small degree of what you refer to as &quot;angst&quot;...Still not a really appropriate term for it, but whatever. </div> </div> </div> <i>Supernatural</i> angst. All of that &quot;wah, my super powers are terrible and it sucks so much to be me&quot; bullshit. Being a vampire is awful. Being a guy with psychic powers, with a head guest that has to keep you happy and healthy to get what it wants and you can just tell to shut up if it annoys you, and most importantly not being dead sounds pretty fucking awesome with maybe one downside that you might have to tell your head guest to shut up a bit more often than the other guys.<br /> <br /> If you don't like Ghosts coming to you at all times of night and nobody can teach you how to ward your house against them, yeah, that's something you can angst about, but the sin-eater condition by itself is nothing to angst about unless you're a whiney bitch or you're one of the minority cases who has a geist who has an agenda and/or is too crazy or stupid to understand that you're the boss.<br /> <br /> Even one with an agenda, baring insanity/stupidity, is going to pick a host that's likely to work towards the agenda<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You cannot actually and seriously, be saying that having an alien ghost grafted to your mind, would carry no &quot;angst&quot;, can you? </div> </div> </div> If it's a choice between willing allowing that alien ghost into my body, being the boss in the relationship, not losing any control of my body, and getting some swaet ass powers out of the deal, and um, being <b>fucking dead</b>, I'd happily take the deal.<br /> <br /> That's something I think people are forgetting. A Sin-Eater isn't like a vampire who became what he was against his will, or a werewolf who was born as he is. A Sin-Eater, after a fatal circumstance, was approached by a geist and made a deal. Let the geist piggy back in your soul so that it can experience the sensation of being alive again, and occasionally do things for it, and in exchange you don't die and have some awesome super powers with no inherent downsides.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you really seriously mean to say, that having a Geist whisper in your ear, as you drive the &quot;Run down that old lady. Its her time to do. She wont be missed!&quot;, wont be kinda unsettling? </div> </div> </div> That's not an inherent quality of the condition of being a sin-eater. That's a case of someone having a particularly murderous geist. And, assuming that in this scenario I'm a player character and thus by default assumed to not be a spineless bastard, I can just tell the geist to shut up. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How about going to a club, and having a gorgeous woman come up to you and chat with you, only to realize half-way through your first kiss, that this lady is going to die of breast cancer in 6 months, so striking up a relationship with her would be meaningless? </div> </div> </div> Death sight works on sight. you'd know long before the kiss and you'd have to be a newby to have not seen other people that are about to die soon. You'll get used to the death sight and just not get involved with those people baring an other choice. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How about having the walk from home to school be a cold and clammy experience, because a triple homicide happened here last year, and the Death Stain still hasn't gone away? </div> </div> </div>How about the satisfaction of helping the ghosts of those murder victims find rest? The cold and clammy shit you'll get used to <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How about waking up 3 AM at night, because a Ghost is screaming at you, because you didn't stop the man who murdered the ghost, which happened last week in front of your apartment complex while you were sitting there playing World of Warcraft entirely oblivious to it all? </div> </div> </div> How would the ghost even know you were able to stop it's murder, had you been aware of it? Or were there when it happened?? All it would know is you can see it.<br /> <br /> Besides, all of that is a trivial price to pay for not being fucking dead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Those are experiences that the 1ed incorporated entire and multiple of them even had a sizeable amount of mechanics behind them. Are you suggesting those wouldn't cause any &quot;angst&quot;? Really? </div> </div> </div> Compared to being dead, those would be signifigantly less angsty. Besides, I was specifically talking about supernatural angst. the &quot;I hate myself becuase I'm not a normal human&quot; bullshit. If someone agnsts about those things, it becuase that's how they would persoanllly react to those scenarios. Not how all sin-eaters in genral react to those scenarios. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree, that Geist shouldn't be <i>about the &quot;angst&quot;</i>, but theres a significant difference between being about the &quot;angst&quot; and having it be there to a lesser degree. </div> </div> </div> The point I repeatedly tried to make is that the sin-eater, inherantyly, has no source of legitimate supernatural angst. Everything that could casue other sources of angst is external-it's not becuase he's a sin-eater, it's becuase h'es a human being interacting with situaltions that could potentially cause certian human beings to angst.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As you can probably see, I dont really agree that the &quot;Geist is kinda unpleasant&quot; applies to only Wretched, the weak-willed and monstrous Geists. Even the most benevolent Geist will be off-putting at times. Even if its not trying to be. Besides, being a &quot;spineless coward&quot; means having a low Resolve+Composure score. I've seen a few PC's who had a low Resolve+Composure score, so those were spineless cowards. Lets not make any assumptions at all, and just assume the baseline. Assuming that a character is a spineless coward is equally as bad as assuming the character isn't a spineless coward. </div> </div> </div> Kinda unpleasant is not the same as supernatural angst. The Wretched, sin-eaters to weak willed to control their geists, and exceptionally insane or monsterous geists, none of which are defualt assumptions for PCs, those are the only ones with any justification to experiance supernatural angst<br /> <br /> you want Supernatual Angst, talk ato the ST about plaiying someone with an exceptioanly monsterous or insane geist. you want any other kind of angst, you make a PC whose normal reaction tot he situations that you described would be to angst and ask the ST to play up situations like those. By by defult that all takes a bakck seet to the &quot;Life sucks sometimes, but we're all stilll alive so lets party&quot; theme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Really, all I'm asking is something like a mechanic that allows the Storyteller to apply Conditions on behalf of the Geist, if its (dis)pleased. Like &quot;The Geist fancies that lady. You get the 'Swooning' Condition&quot;. Or &quot;The Geist is feeling good about this, you get the 'Inspired' Condition&quot; or &quot;The Geist is displeased with you. You get the 'Regrets' Condition&quot;. I would even be fine with just having it as an optional rule. As long as its recognized in some small fashion, I wouldn't mind. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the gheist should't be able to inflict any conditions that majorly influence you negativly. That keys back into the supernatural angst thing-if being a sin-eater sucked much bad, then nobody would take the deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 05-08-2015, 02:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T15:24:30-07:00","id":508485,"title":"","content":"Synergy needs reworking, yes.<br /> <br /> I think there could be something more effective done to make resurrection have downsides than the current system has. That's something I would like to see considered and expanded.<br /> <br /> Geist has a celebratory tone, even surrounded by death, however. Macabre and dark but as a line bright. That's something I would like to keep. The darkness comes from the world around the Sin-Eater, who shines a light in. As an opposite to, say, Vampire that corrupts what it touches.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T17:31:18-07:00","id":508571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baron Samedi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=508485#post508485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Synergy needs reworking, yes.<br /> <br /> I think there could be something more effective done to make resurrection have downsides than the current system has. That's something I would like to see considered and expanded.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's something I can get behind, if more angst neds to be added to the setting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T04:30:40-07:00","id":508857,"title":"","content":"I think you're forgetting that people aren't always privy to the specifics of the deal in advance. Its not like the budding Sin-Eater is handed a document to sign with all the details lain out in plain english in black ink on white paper and compared to the alternative (being dead) literally anything and everything sounds appealing. Thats not entirely wrong either. Compared to being dead, being a Sin-Eater is a pretty sweet deal but that doesn't mean it doesn't have its low points occationally. Yes, you can get used to all the creepy shit, but thats true for any game line. You can get used to drinking peoples blood, you can get used to people forming hate-mobs to kill you. Just because you can get used to a few things doesn't mean they're pleasant. Its true that compared to being dead, it is pleasant, but it doesn't have to be pleasant all the time.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the fluff of the 1ed Sin-Eater book heavily implied that the Geist was a really creepy and often alien as fuck companion, even if it didn't try to be. Its still a ghost, and even a sane and pleasant ghost is still a really freaky and wierd thing. The infliction of negative conditions was also something I grew out of something wirtten in the 1ed book where its mentioned that a Geist gives its Sin-Eater a huge guilt trip after the Sin-Eater fucked something up. I am not grasping this out of thin air. I am merely asking for the mechanics of 2ed to support the narrative fluff of 1ed. Did we read the same book??","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T06:51:54-07:00","id":508889,"title":"","content":"Yes, but we apparently took away different meanings-having to get used to creepy stuff is considerably less sucky than having to eat people to survive or having literally the entire world wanting to kill you, me thinks, and making it suck bad enough that the majority of Sin-eaters would have legitimate reason to angst about their condition would seriously detract from the gameline's celebratory tone.<br /> <br /> As for the deal&quot; Hey, you died. I can bring you back to life, but you have to let me piggyback in your soul so I can experience what it's like to be alive again.&quot;<br /> &quot;I don't know&quot;<br /> &quot;you get super powers out of the deal&quot;<br /> &quot;sold!&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a deal. Even fairy bargains tend to tell you the details, even if it's in a rhyme or in wording that makes it unclear. The vary nature of the Bargain as a bargain means at least some details have to be shared, and it's in the geists best interest to make the mortal see that the deal is better than dying. For that reason, incidentally, it is logical to conclude that exceptionally monstrous, insane, or otherwise inhuman geists don't get hosts very often, simply do to not being able to communicate why taking the bargain is better than dying.<br /> <br /> Creepy sometimes is not enough to say that being a sin-eater is bad. Sin-eaters arguably have it the best of any splat right now, what with having no reason, by default, in general, to angst about being a sin-eater. Anything they could angst-angry ghosts, and the like, is external to the sin-eater. They'd have the same problems with the ghostly version of the unseen sense merit.<br /> <br /> And again, an alien intelligence whose best interests include you being happy and healthy, that you willingly agreed to let piggy back into your soul, that can't control your body unless you die at least seven times, that you are the dominant partner in the relationship with... Might get creepy sometimes, but considering that you let the spooky alien intellect into your soul willingly and doing so brought you back to life, you'd kind of have to be the kind of person who'd complain about anything to angst about that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T16:22:01-07:00","id":509291,"title":"","content":"You're right, its a bargain. It's <i>The</i> Bargain. But as it is, it feels more like The Gift. What are you giving up for your second chance? What could compel you to refuse it? With the exception of a few types of hunters (and arguably Demons), Sin-eaters are the only splat to <i>choose</i> to become a supernatural. Everyone else is generally a victim of circumstance. Literally every Sin-eater is a Sin-eater because they chose to be one. That's huge. But it loses a lot of its emotional power if its just this blind, snap decision without any real consequence. With the way The Bargain works now, all I know about a Sin-eater is &quot;They were dying.&quot; If that deal becomes a more weighty thing then it automatically informs the base nature of every Sin-eater. So rather than &quot;They were dying.&quot; you get something closer to, &quot;They want to be alive <i>that</i> badly.&quot; Look at how we view, say, a drowning person grabbing a lifejacket versus someone going through chemotherapy. <br /> <br /> Every Sin-eater should absolutely know what they're getting into, and what they're getting into shouldn't be always be pleasant, because that just means that what they <i>want</i> is that much more meaningful. It's the difference between &quot;not dying&quot; and &quot;living.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T17:02:34-07:00","id":509310,"title":"","content":"And that goes against the celebratory theme of Geist<br /> <br /> I think you're looking at the Bargain from the wrong perspective. Why do most Geist's approach dead or dying mortals to make The Bargain?<br /> <br /> After all, in most cases, The Bargain was horribly one sided... In the Host's favor.<br /> <br /> The Host gts to not be dead. They get some super powers that have a few tiny downsides but nothing to angst about, and they get a head guest whose best interests include keeping them happy and healthy.<br /> <br /> The Geist... loses all ability to interact with the world other than, unless their host is Wretched, whispering in their host's ear and asking them to do things for them. but they get to experience all of those sensations the living get but the Ephemeral Dead do not.<br /> <br /> That imbalance in favor of the mortal is intentional, methinks.<br /> <br /> This is an other one of those inversion points: It's not the Mortal who is just that desperate to live(which is the same for anyone who is desperate to live, which um, almost everybody who's dying before their time is, it's because however much the host wants to keep living, the Geist wants to live <i>again</i> That much <b>more</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T11:18:56-07:00","id":512152,"title":"","content":"I agree with Soulgambit that any splat referred to as Sin Eaters should have something to do with eating sins (or at least something that would inspire the notion in ages past).<br /> <br /> I also agree with Illuminated Minutia that The Bargain as presented in the flavor text has little resemblance to the mechanics of the current edition. The flavor text strongly indicated that the geist would urge the host to commit acts that furthered its spiritual sphere of influence. I would really like to see this given mechanics similar to a contract and tied into Synergy.<br /> <br /> Rater, the reason The Bargain works out better for the mortal host is that the mortal host is the player's character, while the geist is usually a storyteller character. Just as there are many different geister there are many potential bargains, not all of which need to turn the potential Sin Eater into a murderer or some such. Still, keeping with the overall themes of the World of Darkness, it is perfectly reasonable for Sin Eaters to have a celebratory outlook on life overall while still being urged to commit (and committing) some potentially atrocious acts on occasion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T11:40:21-07:00","id":512171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThomasM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=512152#post512152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree with Soulgambit that any splat referred to as Sin Eaters should have something to do with eating sins (or at least something that would inspire the notion in ages past).</div> </div> </div> </div>They do. The term is applied based on the culturally common idea that ghosts are the symptoms of restless souls if not the souls themselves and that the things preventing a ghost from moving on (i.e. the things that create the Anchor Conditions that prevent a ghost from entering the Underworld) are burdens to be taken up by the Bound.<br /> <br /> The Underworld's showcasing of Vice tends to mean that any persistent returnees are almost necessarily going to tend toward the &quot;sinful,&quot; as well, and my word if ectophagia doesn't bring a bluntly literal version of the name to bear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:07:56-07:00","id":512186,"title":"","content":"I realize its my issue, but I just don't like that application of the term. It just seems that there should be a physical Ceremony, so common as to be almost universal, that Sin Eaters perform for the living, dying and nearly dead. Maybe I missed it and need to re-read that section.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:22:17-07:00","id":512204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThomasM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=512186#post512186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I realize its my issue, but I just don't like that application of the term. It just seems that there should be a physical Ceremony, so common as to be almost universal, that Sin Eaters perform for the living, dying and nearly dead. Maybe I missed it and need to re-read that section.</div> </div> </div> </div>You appear to be proposing a widespread mechanical aspect that <i>stops ghosts from happening</i>, which seems ill-considered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:47:53-07:00","id":512222,"title":"","content":"Glad to see I'm not the only one who wants a bit more activity from the Geist.<br /> I once heard somebody propose a mechanic that essentially allowed a Sin-Eater to absorb the Ghosts Anchors (Its 'Sins') letting the Ghost pass on, but giving the Sin-Eater something akin to a Ban that tied into which specific ghost whose 'Sins' they 'Ate' which lasted untill they had &quot;Wronged the Sins of the Ghost&quot;. I really liked this idea, and might make it a thing in my own Sin-Eater game, seeing as how I agree that the name &quot;Sin-Eater&quot; seems a bit nonsensical as it stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T13:04:34-07:00","id":512234,"title":"","content":"I'm in the same camp that doesn't want more activity from the Geists. On the one hand, I don't want the Geist to be the NWoD counterpart to a Wraith's Shadow. On the other hand, I also don't think we need to incorporate a mechanic that necessarily strips agency from the player in a game about Second Chances and with the overall positive tone. Even if it's a simple carrot/stick mechanic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T18:12:23-07:00","id":512436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ThomasM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=512152#post512152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IJust as there are many different geister there are many potential bargains, not all of which need to turn the potential Sin Eater into a murderer or some such.</div> </div> </div> </div>And again, it's said that the main reason Geister find hosts is because they want to experience the sensations of life again.<br /> <br /> For every Geist that wants you to do something atrocious, there's a lot more that want you to go out and get drunk, or get high, or get laid, just so they can experience those sensations again second hand. Even the ones that do want something atrocious can be talked down. The Example given was the burning woman, who wants her host to douse her enemies in gasoline and light them up? The host puts her foot down on that, and instead pacifies her by going out to see wildfires during the burning seasons and burning down haunted houses to deal with the ghosts.<br /> <br /> I'm just saying, making the condition of being a Sin-Eater, of making like a vampire where you are better off Dead than Undead, completely kills the Celebratory theme of Geist.<br /> <br /> &quot;Bad things happen and sometimes life sucks, but you're still alive and that's something to celebrate&quot; stops dead when most experienced members of the splat wish they were dead.<br /> <br /> &quot;You know for a fact that your friend/son/lover is going to die before you do, so let's make every second count&quot; falls short when you're state of life is too awful for you to enjoy mundane things anymore.<br /> <br /> If the default Sin-Eater condition is so bad that the average Sin-Eater is justified in angsting about being a Sin-Eater, then the Celebratory theme, which is one of the things that makes Geist Distinct from the rest of the WoD, goes away.<br /> <br /> you know what the other thing is? The fact that, in an encounter with the Supernatural, the mortal party comes out on top. The Mortal gets the better end of The Bargain. As I said before, there's no way that's a mistake.<br /> <br /> Besides, all of those cases where the mechanics don't line up with the fluff, most of the time the fluff is talking about sin-eaters with particularly monstrous or insane Geists(like Dem Bones) Geists with an Agenda, or host's that are too weak willed to say no to their geists. Find me an example that is not one of the three, and we'll talk, okay, but until then, I'm just going to keep pointing out that the first and third cases are not likely player characters, the second case the Geist is probably going to look for a host who would support the agenda, and in the first case all logic dictates that the Geist would have trouble getting a host to accept the bargain in the first place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":3405,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","user":"Rater202","date":". 05-12-2015, 09:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T07:02:01-07:00","id":512891,"title":"","content":"What I think Geist could do with is having a bit more focus on what the game Geist is about. Sure there are mystery angles, but Mage is pretty much the quintessential &quot;looking for weird shit&quot; game, and Werewolf has done wonders with the whole &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt&quot; angle. Geist needs a more accessible hook not as to why you want o be a Sin-Eater (game wise, that is) but why you should want to play a game about Sin-Eaters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T08:12:55-07:00","id":514124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>That Other Guy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=512891#post512891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I think Geist could do with is having a bit more focus on what the game Geist is about. Sure there are mystery angles, but Mage is pretty much the quintessential &quot;looking for weird shit&quot; game, and Werewolf has done wonders with the whole &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt&quot; angle. Geist needs a more accessible hook not as to why you want o be a Sin-Eater (game wise, that is) but why you should want to play a game about Sin-Eaters</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with this.<br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Since Geist first came out, I've been puzzled by this game. I loved the mechanics, the mood... But I had no idea what to do with a Sin-eater. They felt liike someone had tried (successfully) to make Moros more specialized and interesting.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I also felt that they lacked focus. Vampires had their political power games, the Forsaken policed the spirits in their territories, the Mages tried to finnd a way back to the Supernal Realms, the Prometheans tried to become human, etc...<br /> What did the Sin-Eater do? Why did they need all those awesome powers? There were no higher goal, no sacred mission, no terrible menace. The game was a ghost infested sandbox.<br /> Not a bad thing, but it would feel better to be able to spin Sin-Eater only tales. They need a purpose, an agency, an enemy, something to challenge them specifically, to pull them from their comfort zones and throw them into interesting conflicts.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T10:34:00-07:00","id":514298,"title":"","content":"A bit more encouragement to help deal with ghosts and abmortals, in the form of a bigger carrot, and maybe an outside context threat that wants to fuck up the party?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T09:56:40-07:00","id":515259,"title":"","content":"Has any of OP's developers taken interest in a 2nd Edition yet?<br /> <br /> Rich T recently said in a blog post (after I mentioned that Geist needs some love) &quot;Nobody puts Geist baby in the corner&quot; Which suggests that yes, they plan on doing one, but can't talk about it until the next pitch season gets approved.<br /> <br /> I would just like to hear from any of the Freelancer's that regularly post on these forums, if they have heard any serious talks about a 2nd Edition happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2545-ninjar","name":"Ninjar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2545_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T11:08:49-07:00","id":515307,"title":"","content":"Going by the pattern they've had for releasing the 2E corebooks, I'd say its a safe bet that they'll announce Hunter and Geist 2E's at this year's Gen-Con.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T16:39:55-07:00","id":516540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illuminated Minutia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=515307#post515307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going by the pattern they've had for releasing the 2E corebooks, I'd say its a safe bet that they'll announce Hunter and Geist 2E's at this year's Gen-Con.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I will have EMTs on standby for when they do. Because I will DIE.<br /> <br /> ...It would be hilarious if it turned out that Geists were real at that exact moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-16T18:24:55-07:00","id":516628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=516540#post516540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...It would be hilarious if it turned out that Geists were real at that exact moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course they're not real. That's crazy. You're crazy malonkey.<br /> <br /> ^shifty eyes*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-25T00:01:08-07:00","id":527393,"title":"","content":"So. Anybody else think the system for a High Psyche Sin-Eater's anchors should be overhauled?<br /> <br /> As in, be there in the first place.<br /> <br /> I mean, it basically served no purpose but to be an arbitrary weakness. I guess you could say that it was the mandatory drawback on High Psyche... except the Sin-Eater also had to spend increasingly large amounts of time in the underworld.<br /> <br /> Anchor's should be like, I don't know, something that either is an optional thing that reduces time needed to be spent in the underworld(trade one weakness for an other) or like... I don't know, make it easier for high Psyche Sin-Eaters to come back.<br /> <br /> So you know, actually act like ghost anchors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm an aspergic individual. This means that I can't imagine how others will react to situations. This has led to me accidentally offending someone, and has also led to me being less clear in statements than I thought I was. I'd like to apologize, and ask that others don't get mad, but just ask me to reword or clarify. Thank you","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3405-rater202","name":"Rater202","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"521"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T12:02:47-07:00","id":599683,"title":"","content":"I've been kicking this around in my head for a while, and this is what I came up with. How I'd do Geist 2E, were it up to me:<br /> <b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Themes:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Living in the Face of Death - Geist is about being constantly reminded that death is an ever-present shadow over life, and choosing to embrace life in response. It's about helping the living and the dead accept the inevitability of mortality. It's about ghost stories. It's about not being a ghost story while you're still alive. It's about developing bonds of love and friendship and helping people through the darkness. It's about throwing glorious fucking parties for the living and dead alike. It's about grief. It's about celebration. It's about fear. It's about fun.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Ties that Bind - The Bound are aptly-named: they're wrapped tight in supernatural chains that link them to their Geists, to their Krewe-mates, and to their Anchors. Each Sin-Eater sits at the center of a web of deathly energies that spread from her into the worlds of the living and dead, and its from these bonds that they draw much of their occult power. Such bonds, however, require at least as much of the Bound as they grant, and maintaining them is often dangerous for everyone and everything involved.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The Dark Passenger - Each Bound has forged a dark bargain. For a second chance at life, she's taken on a ghostly presence, a presence she can never escape, that pushes her to indulge its desires and pursue its drives. The Bound must learn to exist with their Geist, distracting it with endless earthly pleasures or giving in to its dark needs. The Geist, meanwhile, pursues its own agenda, whispering always to its Sin-Eater, encouraging her power in order to further its goals.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Bridging the Ultimate Gap - The ideal Sin-Eater isn't so much a guardian policing the border between the living and the dead, but rather a link between those two states. She helps the living remember the dead and make peace with their own mortality. She reminds ghosts of the pleasures of life and the import of letting go and moving forward. She is a grief counselor whose effectiveness is rooted in the fact that she knows grief only too well.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Depthless Mysteries - Ultimately, Death is unknowable. Even the Geist's knowledge of what they truly are is muddy and inconsistent. Are they ghosts that have taken on spiritual import? Spirits that have descended into the Underworld and fed on ghosts? The echoing remnants of dead gods? Somehow all of these? The depths of the Underworld shift with time, populated with impossible creatures and the graveyards of broken ideas. The caverns descend forever downward. And then there's what's beyond - what awaits those dead who aren't grasped by the cold halls of the doomed. Krewes often form for companionship and support, but as the Geists within a krewe interweave, they inevitably push the krewes to delve into the mysteries of their own dread being.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What Sin-Eaters <i>do</i>:</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Sin-Eater stories are ghost stories with a twist - the haunted are on equal footing with the haunters. Sin-Eaters often have a good sense of what they're dealing with in any particular haunting, and they're in a strong position to defend themselves from spectral assault. Geists don't terribly like destroying ghosts, however, and strongly favor the Bound ridding the world of problematic ghosts by resolving their Anchors. This is how the Bound &quot;eat sins:&quot; they take it upon themselves to correct whatever imbalance keeps ghosts in the world of the living. Sometimes this is as simple as making sure the ghost is remembered by someone important. Sometimes it can involve murderous vengeance. The rush of plasm they gain when resolving a ghost lends weight to the metaphor of sin consumption.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Sin-Eaters <i>know</i> that the world is filled with death. Ghosts linger on every corner, in most buildings. They're omnipresent echoes, only a handful of which have the wherewithal to inflict themselves upon the living. Even the most thorough Sin-Eaters, those wholly dedicated to moving the dead along, have to pick and choose their battles. As a result, Geist stories are intrinsically <i>personal</i>. They're stories about what matters to the ghosts. They're stories about the effects that death has on those left behind. They're tales of frightened faith, shaken hope, abject grief, desperate denial, and - just sometimes - acceptance. Sin-Eaters get to know people. They make friends and lovers. They cultivate Krewes. They collect Anchors.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Occasionally, Sin-Eaters delve into the Underworld. For the most part, this involves going into the Depths to recover a destroyed item, deliver a message, escape an enemy, pursue a banished ghost, or help the living move on. Sometimes it's to indulge their vices or abuse the dead. Older Bound find themselves increasingly drawn into the depths or risk their deathly potency infecting their Anchors. The Bound generally try to avoid crossing the rivers or passing the gates they find there, but sometimes sacrifices must be made. Sin-Eaters who enter the Lower Mysteries witness entirely new vistas of mortality that often force them to face their own inner shadows, leaving them - and their Geists - forever changed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Geist stories sometimes become epic. Bloody-handed necromancers raise ancient ghosts with powers that shake mountains. Entombed godkings rise in search of plundered relics, stirring even normally docile ghosts to acts of violence and opening the gates of death to release half-dead monstrosities into the world. The boundary between life and death frays, and entrances to the Underworld begin appearing throughout a small town in the mountains. Dead gods ascend from the depths to claim a city as their personal dominion. Epic Geist tales add a gonzo flavor to the game, challenging even powerful characters and driving them to forge disparate cults into larger factions or even unearth the secrets of long-forgotten conspiracies.</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">2E Upgrades:</span></span></b></u><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><img src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/RnNZfQn2o2xpggJQqefCOervMbPIci5mujDPJnvl43kv6Rtxjyh5gHN_JKVzeU-aaGz3pePFgxfoAAtZJZNx8mveVTc-11j98EfuAJVcumUenA=s0-d-e1-ft#https://ssl.gstatic.com/ui/v1/icons/mail/images/cleardot.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> <br /> Do away with Archetypes. <br /> <b>Instead:</b><br /> Willpower is regained through Purpose - the player's reason for being in the face of death. This is the reason they choose To Be rather than Not To Be. <br /> <br /> Making major progress towards the character's Purpose in the face of significant danger returns all spent Willpower. <br /> <br /> Making minor progress towards Purpose in the face of minor obstacles returns a single spent Willpower.<br /> <br /> Characters also possess Aspirations which grant beats, as per core World of Darkness characters. Each character furthermore possesses a Deathly Aspiration, a short-term goal of the Geist, which grants a Synergy beat. (See below.)<br /> <br /> Bound characters regain Plasm primarily through two other unique traits: Drive and Desire. (Plasm can still be harvested from ectophagia, Haunts, Flesh Fairs, and the resolution of hauntings.)<br /> <br /> Drive represents the Geist's raison d'etre. It's almost always something too huge to actually accomplish. It may be something like &quot;Punish all rapists&quot; or &quot;Learn all secrets.&quot; This is the thing that keeps the Geist bound to the world, the thing that keeps it from passing on. Were it ever to be truly resolved, the Geist would move on to its final destination. Fulfilling the Geist's Drive in a minor way restores a single Plasm. Making major progress towards the Drive in the face of tremendous difficulty restores all spent Plasm and grants a Synergy beat.<br /> <br /> Synergy beats are tracked independently from other beats and Experiences. When a player earns a number of Synergy beats equal to her current Synergy, her Synergy increases by 1.<br /> <br /> Desire is the Sin-Eater's primary tool in distracting her Geist from its Drive. It's an earthly pleasure that the Geist particularly responds to. It may be drinking, dancing, fucking, reading, gorging on food, or playing videogames. It is, by its nature, something that the Geist can't experience when not bound and does not further the character's Drive, Purpose, or Aspirations. In short, it's an unproductive distraction. But that's part of <i>living life</i>. Indulging the Geist's desire nets the Player a single spent Plasm. Doing so in a manner that significantly undermines the character's goals or endangers her restores all spent Plasm and a spent Willpower point. Most importantly, a player can avoid experiencing a Synergy Breaking Point resulting from ignoring an opportunity to fulfill (or - rarely and at Storyteller discretion - actively opposing) her Geist's Drive by engaging in her Desire within the same or following scene. Using Desire this way costs a Synergy beat, however.<br /> <img src=\"https://ci6.googleusercontent.com/proxy/RnNZfQn2o2xpggJQqefCOervMbPIci5mujDPJnvl43kv6Rtxjyh5gHN_JKVzeU-aaGz3pePFgxfoAAtZJZNx8mveVTc-11j98EfuAJVcumUenA=s0-d-e1-ft#https://ssl.gstatic.com/ui/v1/icons/mail/images/cleardot.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>Synergy Re-Imagined:</b><br /> Synergy is rated 1 to 10, and player characters begin at 5. Synergy is gained by engaging in the Geist's Drive, pursuing its Deathly Aspiration, and otherwise behaving in a manner appropriate to the Geist. Synergy is lost by ignoring the Drive or performing actions inimical to the Geist. (These latter actions are not tiered - any of these actions can trigger a Breaking Point, regardless of Synergy rating. Some actions are particularly destructive to the bond between Sin-Eater and Geist, however, and levy a penalty to the roll to avoid discord.) <br /> <br /> Discord Breaking Points include: Closing an Avernian Gate (with a penalty of -2 if the Sin-Eater destroys the gate). Destroying Mementos (with a -2 penalty if it is a Deathmask or Keystone). Destroying a ghost (with a penalty of -2 if the Sin-Eater performs ectophagia). Inadvertent killing (-1 die). Reviving the dead (-1 die). Destroying a Geist (-2 dice). Mass or serial murder (-2 dice). Attempted suicide or attempting to destroy one's own Geist (chance die).<br /> <br /> Synergy grants various bonuses at high levels (and penalties at low levels as the angry wails of the neglected Geist distracts its host), but the most valuable of these is Keys. For every second dot of Synergy (1, 3, 5, 7, and 9) the Sin-Eater gains access to a Key. This is the only way to earn Keys. Keys are lost when Synergy drops below the threshold necessary to maintain it. The Synergy 1 Key is always appropriate to the character's Threshold, the Synergy 3 Key is always appropriate to the Geist's, and the Synergy 5 Key is open to player choice. Either the Synergy 5, 7, or 9 Key must be the character's second Threshold Key.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Anchors Re-Imagined:</b><br /> All Sin-Eaters possess Anchors, the parts of the living world that keep them returning to it. These have a similar role to Touchstones in Requiem, but rather than being something the player uses to prevent bestial descent, cultivating Anchors reinforces the Bound's connection to the world of the living, allowing her to channel greater deathly power. Each Anchor is associated with either a Lock (see below) or her Psyche trait, and the character's relationships with these characters, organizations, or locations deepen as she grows in power. These relationships are not without risk, of course - the loss of a valued Anchor can cripple a Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> Just as Anchors tie the Bound to the living world, the Bound touch their Anchors with the energies of death. Anchor locations become haunts or even Cenotes. Anchor characters become mediums or attract ghosts. Many of those offered the Bargain were once Anchors for a Sin-Eater or ghost themselves. The appeal of Anchors as beings with a connection to the Underworld (or as leverage against a Bound) often brings them to the attention of Sin-Eaters, ghosts, unbound Geists, abmortals, living human magicians, and things stranger yet. The dangers faced by Anchors often drive Sin-Eater stories.<br /> <br /> When a Sin-Eater's Psyche rises above 5, she must begin spending a set amount of time in the Underworld to keep her power concentrated in her own physical form. If she doesn't do so, her Psyche seeps from her, becoming reduced. More troubling, that energy flows along the invisible lines tying her to her Anchors, infusing them with the morbid energies of death and decay. This can ruin an Anchor's life as they suffer nightmares, experience visions, inadvertently open Avernian Gates, and become shining beacons of power to ghosts, the Bound, abmortals and necromancers.<br /> <br /> Each Anchor functions as a Merit, and each level of the Merit grants bonuses to Manifestations involving the Lock the Anchor represents (such as a bonus die at first and increased dice tricks later on). For the Anchor that represents the character's Psyche, the Merit provides bonuses to harvesting Plasm. Sin-Eaters possess Mementos that represent these bonds (generally an object given by the or taken from the Anchor), and without them, they lose the benefits of the Merit until they recover or replace the Memento. If an Anchor (or the Sin-Eater's relationship with her) is destroyed, the Bound not only loses the advantages granted by the Merit, but suffers a significant penalty when using the trait the Anchor was tied to.<br /> <br /> Characters begin play with three 1-dot Anchors (one for her Psyche and one each for two of their Locks). They may increase the rating of any of these Anchors with Merit dots during character creation, or even purchase a fourth Anchor if they have a third Lock.<br /> <br /> At high Psyche, Sin-Eaters become a danger to their Anchors if they don't spend time in the Underworld. Anchors bound to high-Psyche Sin-Eaters who don't bleed off their deathly energies in the stygian depths gain increasing penalties to actions as they become plagued by unearthly sounds and visions. Worse yet, ghosts gain a bonus to rolls to notice such individuals, to affect them with Numina, and to manifest in their presence.<br /> <br /> Going it alone: the lone wolf character is still a viable playstyle for Geist, though it somewhat flies in the face of the themes of the revised game. Loner Sin-Eaters tend to focus on Psyche and Synergy rather than Anchors, and thus have more Keys and fewer Locks than more social Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Krewes Revised:</b><br /> Do away with tiers.<br /> <br /> Many small Krewes are informal groups of Sin-Eaters who meet up to talk shop and generally support one another. They're trauma survivors, uniquely situated to understand what one another has gone through, and that gives them a common ground that often leads to bonds of deep loyalty. Most Krewes take this a step further, performing a ceremony that binds them together with metaphysical chains not entirely unlike those between a Sin-Eater and her Anchors. This binding results in a profoundly deep communion between the Bound involved, a communion accompanied by flashes of blinding insight. Krewes exit the binding with a deeper working understanding of the mysteries of death, the relationships between their Geists, and the role their Krewe plays in the living world. This allows the Krewe to purchase Merits as a group, much as they might share a Safe Place, and even Krewe members who join later or have not contributed to the pool gain the benefit of these Merits. <br /> <br /> Those members of the Krewe present at the binding, however, are known as the Founders, and they gain a handful of supernatural benefits from the experience. These Founders gain additional powers as their Krewe expands and evolves. More importantly, their Geists change as their cult grows and their mystery deepens. They reveal more about themselves and their origins, revelations that wholly alter how they are perceived (and even what they are called) by the Sin-Eaters.<br /> <br /> Characters who join large, established Krewes may purchase a one-dot Merit to represent their membership. (This Merit is a two-way street - it both allows the owner to benefit from the Krewe's pool of Merits and it adds the owner's Anchors to the overall number of Anchors associated with the Krewe.) Additional Merits can be purchased by non-founding members, and the types of Merits available are based on the Psyche of the Founders. As the Founders grow in mystical power, their channel and mythos evolves, granting greater advantages to their followers. Mechanically, this is handled as a prerequisite for Merits based on the Founders' average Psyche.<br /> <br /> The Founders, on the other hand, gain access to additional Merits as their base of allies and followers grows. Founders Merits have prerequisites based on the number of total Anchors possessed by all of the members of the Krewe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Manifestations Revised:</b><br /> Manifestations are powers that combine a Key (a manifestation of a deathly archetype embodied by the Geist) with a Lock (an aspect of the living world embodied by a Sin-Eater's understanding of one of her Anchors). This combination of life and death manifests a ghostly power.<br /> <br /> The goal of revising Manifestations is to make the system more coherent. Locks should provide a specific set of powers while the Keys alter them in reasonable ways. Abilities that fall too far outside of the logical combination between Locks and Keys should be recast as Ceremonies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Ceremonies and Mementos</b> are largely unchanged. The latter could perhaps be fiddled with a bit to build Mementos out of traits rather than having set traits at set levels. Any other changes will be focused on making these cool, collectible aspects of Sin-Eater existence. Players should want to load up on them, and the game should support that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> </span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4030-alexs","name":"AlexS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T14:59:23-07:00","id":599850,"title":"","content":"One of the things that bothered me most with the Sin-eaters was their lack of link to a real world legend. They could have been the WoD versions of soul reapers (like Shinigamis, the Ankou, etc..) or resurrection deities (like Osiris, Tammuz, Adonis, Attis...) at the center of fertility rites and mystery cults. Instead we have a strange combination of the cWoD Wraith and Mummy who don't really do anything the Moros weren't already doing before. It feels too much like they only exist because we needed a ghost splat to mirror the cWoD.<br /> In short, I hope the second edition will move beyond that and give the Sin-Eaters the distinct identity they need and deserve.<br /> <br /> A lot is being said about how Geist is about second chances and celebration of life. This aspect needs to make it into the game's mecanics and gameplay. Sin-Eater powers especially, should be as much about life and joy than about death and horror.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T15:10:19-07:00","id":599856,"title":"","content":"I think I'd like to see a ground-up rethink of this game, including possibly rebranding it to a better fitting name.<br /> <br /> &lt;name rant&gt;Unlike poltergeist, geist isn't an appropriated word in English, it's just German for ghost. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Revenant: the Risen would have been a much more evocative name. Wight and even Zombie would have also been topical. &lt;/name rant&gt;<br /> <br /> On the whole, +1 to the ideas listed above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T04:26:59-07:00","id":602786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=599856#post599856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'd like to see a ground-up rethink of this game, including possibly rebranding it to a better fitting name.<br /> <br /> &lt;name rant&gt;Unlike poltergeist, geist isn't an appropriated word in English, it's just German for ghost. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Revenant: the Risen would have been a much more evocative name. Wight and even Zombie would have also been topical. &lt;/name rant&gt;<br /> <br /> On the whole, +1 to the ideas listed above.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't speak German, so I'm only going on what I've heard during the development, and from others - but as far as I was aware &quot;Geist&quot; isn't a simple translation into English. I believe it can mean Ghost, Mind, Spirit - so with ambiguity of what the Geists actually are, as well as the word itself in English, then I would think that it's quite a fitting term.<br /> <br /> I'm happy to stand corrected if someone who speaks German well can tell me this is wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><b>Danny James - FL Editor, Writer, &amp; Proofreader - @AlienStoneDog<br /> - Onyx Path, Pinnacle, C7, TAG</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/510-meetsintaverns","name":"MeetsInTaverns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar510_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-25T22:30:12-07:00","id":603508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=599850#post599850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things that bothered me most with the Sin-eaters was their lack of link to a real world legend. They could have been the WoD versions of soul reapers (like Shinigamis, the Ankou, etc..) or resurrection deities (like Osiris, Tammuz, Adonis, Attis...) at the center of fertility rites and mystery cults. Instead we have a strange combination of the cWoD Wraith and Mummy who don't really do anything the Moros weren't already doing before. It feels too much like they only exist because we needed a ghost splat to mirror the cWoD.<br /> In short, I hope the second edition will move beyond that and give the Sin-Eaters the distinct identity they need and deserve.<br /> <br /> A lot is being said about how Geist is about second chances and celebration of life. This aspect needs to make it into the game's mecanics and gameplay. Sin-Eater powers especially, should be as much about life and joy than about death and horror.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Sin-Eaters who think life is only party hard are not seeing the big picture. Life is toil and choices, pain and war, art and science. Life is Change. Your Geist did not make the Bargain so you could be wasted 24/7.<br /> <br /> I would like stories about the major Krewes throughout historical periods where Death was prominent in one way or another. It doesn't have to be just pirates, Crusades and Black Plague in the Middle Ages and the two World Wars. Death is also Transition, doubly so for Sin-Eaters. I could totally get into stories about Krewes during the Renaissance and Avant-garde movements, which served as boundaries separating the old and stale from the new and experimental. Krewes that founded themselves around the birth of the Internet would also be awesome, since the Internet marked the start of a completely different era for the entire world (yeah, sorry for being Captain Obvious there, but my point stands).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-26-2015, 01:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T08:12:28-07:00","id":604712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MeetsInTaverns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=602786#post602786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't speak German, so I'm only going on what I've heard during the development, and from others - but as far as I was aware &quot;Geist&quot; isn't a simple translation into English. I believe it can mean Ghost, Mind, Spirit - so with ambiguity of what the Geists actually are, as well as the word itself in English, then I would think that it's quite a fitting term.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, that's correct. Being a German word, you can find it in the Oxford English Dictionary (English being a Germanic language) where it retains it's &quot;spirit&quot; meaning. In ordinary colloquial English you only see it used as part of particular loan words, e.g., poltergeist, zeitgeist, etc. The original German usage is closer to what the ancient Romans meant by the term &quot;genius&quot; (as in genius locus). The problem for the game is that &quot;Geist&quot; is too vague of a name, which ultimately translated into issues of thematic focus. It's hard to play a game that doesn't really know what it wants to be. It must also be hard to write such a game as the quality of Geist 1.0 was so poor a 1.5 edition of the book was ultimately necessary to patch up its many problems.<br /> <br /> IMO, if the goal was to channel spirit (and thus canonize how Claimed could / should be played) then it should have had a broader scope than just ghosts. That it doesn't have a broader scope argues that it's goal was to bring into being a &quot;Ghost&quot; game (and they could have just used that name and saved alot of trouble) that would serve as a nWoD spiritual successor to Wraith (by scavenging most of its popular themes -- Ego v Id, Underworld, Fetters, etc.). I would have preferred an actual nWoD Wraith but since Geist took so many themes from the oWoD one, it would necessarily only resemble the Oblivion in the broadest sense of topicality, i.e., players play non-Vampire Undead.<br /> <br /> Now there is a question of how best to fold Wraith's into the existing PC splats without breaking the existing spirit rules. IMO, the best approach would be if Wraith's were Claimed dead who (exception to normal Claimed rules) did not deteriorate over time (because they leech life from their surroundings).<br /> <br /> A nWoD Wraith game would need some new themes to focus on too. As Geist has pretty much already staked out the whole 'resolve one's past life' theme, I'd suggest that a new Wraith not focus on that topic. Picking up on some of the military themes from oWoD Wraith might be appropriate in its stead (the dead are legion). Wraiths are captains and dukes (again the Ancient Roman meaning -- general) of the dead. To avoid power creep and metaphysical problems, the long &quot;war&quot; they've been party too is over. Maybe they won, maybe they lost, whatever the case, the truth is lost to history. Maybe the wraiths were the heads of an invading force, maybe they were there to defend the world from an invading force, who knows... The point is they are stuck in the material world (the Romani are a good precedent for this kind of thing -- anthropological evidence suggests that their ancestors were a &quot;lost&quot; army from the Indian sub-continent) and they have to find ways to cope. This steals rather well from ghost stories like Beetlejuice and Being Human, as finding a way to co-exist with the living is a central part of the game. Of course, like Demon, there are those who think that the whatever war is still going on...<br /> <br /> Of course that's what I'd do / hope for in a nWoD Wraith game, the topic was Geist 2.0. Mainly, I think a rebranding to something like Revenant: the [whatever] would do some wonders for thematic unity. &quot;Geist&quot; is such a rarely used word it's hard to tell what the game is going to be about (without jumping to the ghost conclusion). I should be able to read the title and instantly know what kind of game it is (like Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Changeling, Hunter, Mummy, Demon, and Beast). Promethean is a bit of an exception but Frankenstein: the Stitching sounds ludicrous. Others have already laid out suggestions for what things in Geist should be changed / updated and I refer you back to the top of the thread for those suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 07-27-2015, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T01:30:37-07:00","id":609091,"title":"","content":"Well, guys, Geist: the Self-Contained Chronicle isn't coming this year. Better luck next time around.<br /> <br /> Unless... Does any one have a brochure? Does it have anything in it except illustrations on a deep blue background confirming it exists and those ready made characters and that one main line book? Is anybody at Gencon there to snoop something not shown yet? Perhaps one of you can resurrect a book that died before it saw release?<br /> <br /> Oh. Cool, I guess. It's still a fun game and cool concept. Time to think about the twisted dead of the gold rush, I suppose.<br /> <br /> (In all seriousness, this was always a game I'd have liked to see more of. I believe I came into the fandom around the time this released. So, what high hopes do you all have for this? Personally, Archetypes were never much of a y-splat. They were more some form of willpower gain a person could engage in if they felt like it, which seems to fit things like masque/dirge or blood/bone more adequately - except Demon, which still uses vice/virtue for some reason. If these were reworked to be more substantial, I'd welcome their inclusion. If not, maybe replace them with something more impactful or excise them entirely. Geist seems to work alright with Thresholds as their sole definition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3708-amateur-hour","user":"Amateur Hour","date":".  diminish the raw, unmitigated snark. 07-31-2015, 04:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3708-amateur-hour","name":"Amateur Hour","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-31T11:44:24-07:00","id":609792,"title":"","content":"Geist remains a game line in need of a serious overhaul. I personally would like to see it rebranded and / or a nWoD Wraith released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T13:20:26-07:00","id":616764,"title":"","content":"I really like the idea of Drive / Desire replacing Virtue and Vice. I think Touchstones can keep their traditional place and name, representing the reason(s) that you came back and your ties to this world. If you had become a ghost instead of a Sin-Eater, your touchstones would have become your Anchors.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Anchors. I think the core innate ability of Sin Eaters should be to &quot;eat&quot; the Sins (basically Anchors) or Ghosts or the dying. They can store one Anchor per Psyche. While a Sin Eater has an Anchor they can tap that ghost's related memories (possibly other things, possibly other traits via a merit or something). This should be an active experience. No combing the Ghost's memories randomly, you have to ask specific questions (that get answered with memories) and you get bonuses for things like holding an item related to the anchor. Notably, Ghosts who have only some of their Anchors become extremely violent towards the Sin Eater, encouraging Sin Eaters to work in tandim to get all of a Ghost's anchors very quickly. Resolving Anchors should be an Aspiration. Successfully resolving an Anchor should have some decent rewards.<br /> <br /> Synergy is a tricky thing. It should be a case of &quot;higher is universally better&quot; and it should represent not a balance between life and death but how well you work with death (as personified by your Geist). Do you walk across the rivers in the underworld hand and hand with death as an old friend, or do you struggle against death in the world? I think this should stay away from murder being good or death being allowed to run rampant, but high synergy should have a very somber and solemn &quot;tone&quot; to it, so to speak.<br /> <br /> The major powers (manifestations)... not going to lie I don't have much in the way of good ideas for. I'm also not sure how to really fit the doors and key metaphore into the scheme of Sin Eaters. Mechanics aside, I'm not sure what they really add to the game. I feel like &quot;Death is the door, you have the keys&quot; is very evocative until you sit down and thing &quot;okay but what do you <i>do</i> with that?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T07:49:10-07:00","id":619994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=599856#post599856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I'd like to see a ground-up rethink of this game, including possibly rebranding it to a better fitting name.<br /> <br /> &lt;name rant&gt;Unlike poltergeist, geist isn't an appropriated word in English, it's just German for ghost. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Revenant: the Risen would have been a much more evocative name. Wight and even Zombie would have also been topical. &lt;/name rant&gt;<br /> <br /> On the whole, +1 to the ideas listed above.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> i'm with you. The name Geist is not very evocative. For me it's like a ghost. When i listen Geist, i think at an incorporeal entity. Or we play a sort of revenant. Revenant the Risen is very good. <br /> Zombie is too evocative of a body in a poor state i think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2307-arcanum-magicae","name":"Arcanum Magicae","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T01:33:15-07:00","id":629705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=508889#post508889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And again, an alien intelligence whose best interests include you being happy and healthy,</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it really isn't. It's best interests is getting you to Synergy 0 so it can drive and you are bound and gagged in the trunk.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T01:41:26-07:00","id":629706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AlexS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=599683#post599683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Discord Breaking Points include: Closing an Avernian Gate (with a penalty of -2 if the Sin-Eater destroys the gate). Destroying Mementos (with a -2 penalty if it is a Deathmask or Keystone). Destroying a ghost (with a penalty of -2 if the Sin-Eater performs ectophagia). Inadvertent killing (-1 die). Reviving the dead (-1 die). Destroying a Geist (-2 dice). Mass or serial murder (-2 dice). Attempted suicide or attempting to destroy one's own Geist (chance die).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Out of curiosity, why did you go this way instead of something like, &quot;Before play make a list of behaviors that you're Geist would find objectionable using this list as a model.&quot;?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1882-ghost","name":"Ghost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1882_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T17:28:41-07:00","id":631758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=629705#post629705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it really isn't. It's best interests is getting you to Synergy 0 so it can drive and you are bound and gagged in the trunk.</div> </div> </div> </div>Best interests possibly, but the books seem to make it out that the Geist gets annoyed at the Sin-Eater for hitting a breaking point and it seems Synergy 0 is basically the Geist saying 'Okay, I've had enough of your shit now...'. The book makes it seem that the Geist pretty much usually just wants to live vicariously in the back of the Sin-Eater's mind. The strange part comes in when building up Psyche means the Sin-Eater feels the pull to the Underworld, becomes more ghost-like and needs to spend time in the Underworld, where I think the Geist would rather keep playing Shadow with it's chosen Bound in the living world than play ghost-prison warden... Of course some Geists may like that kind of power play, so I don't know...<br /> <br /> It's best interests seem to be keeping a Sin-Eater away from ghost stuff altogether, though a Sin-Eater needs their Plasm to defend themselves against more insistent ghosts looking for help, so it makes a vicious cycle of helping ghosts pass on to be able to defend against a potential Bigger Fish Yellowbones if one comes knocking...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T18:38:48-07:00","id":631812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=629706#post629706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Out of curiosity, why did you go this way instead of something like, &quot;Before play make a list of behaviors that you're Geist would find objectionable using this list as a model.&quot;?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's not super clear in my write-up, but ignoring/acting against the Geist's Drive is a Breaking Point, as well. (Cf. the paragraph above the one you quoted.) The idea is that there are some actions that disturb the bond, regardless of what either the Sin-Eater or the Geist <i>desire</i>. These are generally things that spit in the face of the natural cycle of life and death. A big part of that is to underscore the themes of the game (as I set them out above).<br /> <br /> I think that a system for easing some restrictions (becoming somewhat calloused as in Mage, or adopting something like a code from Hunter) would not be wildly out of the question. A way for the Geist and Sin-Eater to decide as a unit to ignore some deathly taboo in favor of their goals, but they'd suffer some distress (which would require more thought than I currently have to give it) as a trade-off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4030-alexs","name":"AlexS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-19T10:11:33-07:00","id":632478,"title":"","content":"I'm actually drawn to the idea of a &quot;Geist&quot; game being made up of <i>multiple</i> protagonist splats: sineaters, wraiths, revenants, born-with-a-caul hard-core mediums; species essentially being a &quot;W axis.&quot; Thresholds, Psyche, and most of the powers would make sense as the same for all of them - one or two inherent powers, systems for injury, and integritypes would be things that vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T00:48:12-07:00","id":641263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=632478#post632478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually drawn to the idea of a &amp;quot;Geist&amp;quot; game being made up of <i>multiple</i> protagonist splats: sineaters, wraiths, revenants, born-with-a-caul hard-core mediums; species essentially being a &amp;quot;W axis.&amp;quot; Thresholds, Psyche, and most of the powers would make sense as the same for all of them - one or two inherent powers, systems for injury, and integritypes would be things that vary.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds good. Sounds similar to the Promethean splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5544-ancientswordrage","name":"AncientSwordRage","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-27T21:17:57-07:00","id":642527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=632478#post632478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually drawn to the idea of a &quot;Geist&quot; game being made up of <i>multiple</i> protagonist splats: sineaters, wraiths, revenants, born-with-a-caul hard-core mediums; species essentially being a &quot;W axis.&quot; Thresholds, Psyche, and most of the powers would make sense as the same for all of them - one or two inherent powers, systems for injury, and integritypes would be things that vary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know. The themes of Geist are already fairly dilute, and if we tried to spread it out any more, it'd be see-through.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T19:07:44-07:00","id":643691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=642527#post642527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. The themes of Geist are already fairly dilute, and if we tried to spread it out any more, it'd be see-through.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just like ghosts? \u263a","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-30T03:17:04-07:00","id":645207,"title":"","content":"I'm just hoping <b><i><u>Geist the Sin-Eaters 2nd edition featuring the Krewe Chronicles </u></i></b>gets made.<br /> <br /> I trust the Devs to take their time and do it right; I still enjoyed the rushed original and I believe it can be something that can make even the best of them proud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-05T05:27:24-07:00","id":652322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=642527#post642527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know. The themes of Geist are already fairly dilute, and if we tried to spread it out any more, it'd be see-through.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;How do* you live when you inescapably see the death beneath the world?&quot; is a pretty good theme for any of the species I mention.<br /> <br /> * Not &quot;how do&quot; as a synonym for &quot;how can&quot; - but as a choice, an expression of a self to strong for either life or death to contain.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-13T20:50:22-07:00","id":663806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=599850#post599850\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things that bothered me most with the Sin-eaters was their lack of link to a real world legend. They could have been the WoD versions of soul reapers (like Shinigamis, the Ankou, etc..) or resurrection deities (like Osiris, Tammuz, Adonis, Attis...) at the center of fertility rites and mystery cults. Instead we have a strange combination of the cWoD Wraith and Mummy who don't really do anything the Moros weren't already doing before. It feels too much like they only exist because we needed a ghost splat to mirror the cWoD.<br /> In short, I hope the second edition will move beyond that and give the Sin-Eaters the distinct identity they need and deserve.<br /> <br /> A lot is being said about how Geist is about second chances and celebration of life. This aspect needs to make it into the game's mecanics and gameplay. Sin-Eater powers especially, should be as much about life and joy than about death and horror.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought that that is what sin eaters are......the base for those legends. Although they have no real power in that direction (aside from making ghosts come alive and being able to devour them that is). They just did not feel &quot;gritty&quot; / &quot;death&quot; enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T04:52:24-07:00","id":664103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=663806#post663806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> They just did not feel &quot;gritty&quot; / &quot;death&quot; enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understood it, that's the paint job. Looking at the details of their existence: hounded by restless shade, knowing full well what awaits most on the other side, and that there really is no decent way to escape your fate (without trading it for something worse). And through it all, you have a psychotic room-mate that's with you <i>all the time </i>(or your don't, actually, and that's just your schizophrenia personified).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-14T12:02:00-07:00","id":664588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/227352-what-would-you-want-to-see-in-a-sin-eater-chronicle-book?p=663806#post663806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always thought that that is what sin eaters are......the base for those legends. Although they have no real power in that direction (aside from making ghosts come alive and being able to devour them that is). They just did not feel &quot;gritty&quot; / &quot;death&quot; enough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nope! IRL, sin-eaters function more like shamans that specialize in funerals. <br /> <br /> That said, I would not be opposed to Sin-Eaters being recast as Ghost-Claimed Exorcists or something similar. Still would like a name-change unless the scope of the game broadens from ghosts to spirits...<br /> <br /> Would also still prefer a nWoD version of Wraith instead of (or at least in addition to) a second edition of this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T05:40:14-07:00","id":665570,"title":"","content":"The equivalent of the Lucid Dead Numina would be nice to have in the Geist Corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-15T16:29:34-07:00","id":666141,"title":"","content":"Emphasis on &quot;the equivalent of&quot;. The Lucid Dead Numina was an exercise in concision \u2014 of getting as much utility out of as little space as possible. And the GMC rules for ephemeral entities connects Lucidity to rank, about which I have mixed feelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-17T20:29:06-07:00","id":669164,"title":"","content":"All of my knowledge of Geist comes second hand so take these random ideas with a grain of salt.<br /> <br /> you could emphasize the partnership between the two halves of the Sin-eaters by making it have a negative impact for the sin-eater to dominate the Geist <i>and </i>when the Geist dominates the sin-eater. so it is a partnership. some of the character creation is about the Geist and what it disagreements with the sin-eater are for the synergy compromise questions.<br /> <br /> also as an alternative to the storyteller playing all the Geists each player controls two characters one sin-eater and one geist. Whether that geist is their own or an other players is up to the group","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7525-quinn-h","name":"Quinn H.","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T03:01:35-08:00","id":771347,"title":"","content":"Guys, I've given possible chronicles a lot of thought. Here are some ideas.<br /> <br /> <b>The Fragmented Chronicles</b> (as in the ocean of fragments)<br /> <b>The Gatekeeper chronicles</b> (as in the gates found within the underworld)<br /> <b>The Grey [Ghost] chronicles</b> (exploring the perspective of ghost to sin eater and using them as antagonist when raising them above 2nd rank)(also their could be some added effects to the bargain and how synergy effects the &quot;ghost&quot; in the making within a sin eater)<br /> <b>The Highway Chronicles</b> (effectively this would just be a midnight roads setting for Geist: The Sin Eaters; but a lot of it)<br /> <b>Sounding the Seventh Trumpet chronicle</b> (This would be a vain attempt to stop the end of days. The interesting thing here would be showcasing Sin Eaters in an end of days setting because I love the idea of the RP between players when the bargain becomes absolute, do the players still care?)(There should also be a section in the book for tier 4 Sin Eaters, which is to say, not bound. I'd recommend some mechanic that allows for the synergy of the hybrid soul to harmonize with the underworld, I've been thinking of a mechanic named &quot;Cacaphony&quot;. The hybrid tier 4 named &quot;Barons&quot; or &quot;Baronesses&quot; is not quite a death lord in function, but can control a lesser threshold for example: instead of death by deprivation - death by dreams or instead of death by chance - death by curse.)<br /> <b>To Rule Below</b> (The idea here is a book entirely based upon how the dead dominions function in the greater scheme of things)(Sin Eater is basically a weak version of Werewolf due to a lack of investment, this is were we start investing. This book would explain the ramefications of manipulating the dead dominions and their inhabitants in the lower mysteries in the fallen world.)<br /> <br /> There are plenty of ways to go about it and sadly even if this game line does make it to 2nd ed its growth has been so stunted that there's no way to know if it would ever be on par with the other lines. Personally Sin Eater has my favorite themes and is my favorite to run out of Cwod and Nwod. If there's any developers who want to tackle this game line send me a message, I'm willing to dedicate my personal time to see the most under appreciated line gets a second chance I just don't have the skill set to do it alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6516-mefathiel8","name":"mefathiel8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}